\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP & MUSK TOUT ACCOMPLISHMENTS OF FIRST MONTH IN OFFICE IRS FACES THOUSANDS OF JOB CUTS DURING TAX SEASON\b0\par\par\uc2 754 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINTER WHIPLASH\par \par \uc2 DEEP FREEZE, TEMPERATURES, FROZEN, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TEMPERATURES, WIND CHILL, FREEZING, WARM UP\par \par \uc2 ATTACK, ISRAEL, BUSES, EXPLOSIONS, HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 LAYOFFS, TRUMP, MUSK, \uc2 IRS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, USPS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bad situation. Okay, Martha, thanks very much. We're gonna get the latest now on President Trump and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's purge of the federal work force. They celebrated the sweeping change to the government last night, as thousands of \uc2 IRS\uc2  workers are fired in the middle of tax season. Chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce has the story. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP & MUSK TOUT ACCOMPLISHMENTS OF FIRST MONTH IN OFFICE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Well one month into his term and the President and his team are lauding their overhaul of the federal government and defending their approach. They say the thousands of federal employees fired so far deserved to go. But workers we've talked to say they've been given no real explanation.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, President Trump celebrating his first month in office, touting his swift and sweeping policy changes.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 A few hundred more week likes this and we're gonna be in great shape.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The President also praising \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and his team at Doge for slashing federal agencies. Musk, at a conservative conference in Washington, chainsaw in hand, boasting of his cuts as thousands of federal workers are now out of a job.\par \par \uc2 ELON MUSK (CO-LEAD DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT EFFICIENCY)\par \par \uc2 This is the chainsaw for bureaucracy\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Musk and the President now floating the idea of giving some of the money allegedly saved by the Doge team, directly to the American people, without providing any details on how it would work.\par \par \uc2 ELON MUSK (CO-LEAD DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT EFFICIENCY)\par \par \uc2 It's money that's taken away from things that are destructive to the country and from organizations that hate you, to you. That's awesome.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But direct payments would need congressional approval. Speaker Mike Johnson already throwing cold water on the idea.\par \par \uc2 REP MIKE JOHNSON (REP) (LOUISIANA/SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE)\par \par \uc2 We have a giant deficit that we're contending with. I think we need to pay down the credit card, right, that's what I think we need to do.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 IRS\uc2  FACES THOUSANDS OF JOB CUTS DURING TAX SEASON\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The latest target, the \uc2 IRS\uc2 . The agency now beginning to lay off more than 6,000 employees across the country, roughly 6% of its work force, right in the middle of the busy tax season. Sources tell us no one being laid off plays a direct role in processing Americans tax returns, but that there are still widespread concerns within the \uc2 IRS\uc2  that the layoffs could ultimately cause delays.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a letter this week Senate Democrats warning of a catastrophic impact on the filing season and the ability of Americans to quickly get tax refunds and assistance filing their taxes this year.\par \par \uc2 SENATE MEMBER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 This is an attempt to undermine the efficiency of the \uc2 IRS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 IRS\uc2  worker likes Kia in Philadelphia informed by email.\par \par \uc2 FORMER \uc2 IRS\uc2  EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I was like the first person on my team that got the email, and I just broke down into tears.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The administration insist, without providing evidence, that they are firing people for cause, but many of these fired workers, who have only been on the job for less than two years, say they've never even had a performance evaluation. Like Nicholas Berardi.\par \par \uc2 NICHOLAS BERARDI (FORMER \uc2 IRS\uc2  EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 It even says here in the email that they're citing the reason why I'm fired is because of my performance. But until today I hadn't gotten a performance review.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPOT: TRUMP EXPECTED TO TAKE CONTROL OF US POSTAL SERVICE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this morning "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " is reporting that the President is preparing to take control of the \uc2 US Postal Service\uc2  and dissolve its leadership. In the meantime, a federal judge has ruled that the Trump administration must restore funding to aid programs worldwide, finding the administration failed to comply with the previous order lifting the 90 day foreign aid freeze. Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250319el2l00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MUSK: TAKING "CHAINSAW" TO BUREAUCRACY IRS BEGINS LAYING OFF 6,000+ EMPLOYEES\b0\par\par\uc2 821 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, ICE, TAUBE, MILLER\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, WIND CHILLS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, BOMBING, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUS EXPLOSIONS ROCK CENTRAL ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , MUSK, LAYOFFS, HASSETT, FREERKS, INFLATION, \uc2 IRS\uc2 , POLL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MUSK: TAKING "CHAINSAW" TO BUREAUCRACY\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, as President Trump's sweeping job cuts now target the \uc2 IRS\uc2  next, and thousands of government workers already in several agencies across the country, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , late today, center stage, wielding a chainsaw, boasting about slashing the federal bureaucracy. The President's team today defending his first 30 days in office. And tonight here, the new poll. What Americans think of this first 30 days. Here's Mary Bruce tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 IRS\uc2  BEGINS LAYING OFF 6,000+ EMPLOYEES\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, before a conservative conference in Washington, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , chainsaw in hand, boasting of slashing the federal workforce.\par \par \uc2 ELON MUSK (DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT EFFICIENCY)\par \par \uc2 This is the chainsaw for bureaucracy. Chainsaw.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With tax season in full swing, the \uc2 IRS\uc2  tonight beginning to lay-off more than 6,000 employees across the country, roughly 6% of its workforce. Employees, like Kia (PH), informed by email.\par \par \uc2 FORMER FEDERAL EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I was, like, the first person on my team that got the email and I just broke down into tears.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sources tell us no one being laid off play as direct role in processing Americans' tax returns, but that there are still widespread concerns within the \uc2 IRS\uc2  that the layoffs could ultimately cause delays. The firings part of the administration's sweeping effort led by Musk to dramatically downsize the federal workforce.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL CIVILIAN EMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) More than 2 million people spread out across all 50 states, with the largest number in DC, Virginia, Maryland, Florida, Texas, and California. The administration insists they're firing people for cause, but many of these fired workers who have only been on the job for less than two years say they've never even had a performance evaluation. From Nicholas Berarti (PH), who works for the \uc2 IRS\uc2  in Philadelphia...\par \par \uc2 FORMER FEDERAL EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 It even says here in the email that they're citing the reason why I'm fired is because of my performance. But until today, I hadn't gotten a performance review.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) To Emma Freerks, who works for the \uc2 US Geological Survey\uc2  in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 EMMA FREERKS (FORMER FEDERAL EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 The thing is, I never had a meeting implying or even official, like, sit down, letter saying, here's your performance review, you're not doing a good job.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Still, today at a press briefing marking one month of the Trump administration, the President's top economic adviser insisting the thousands of workers who have been fired deserve to go.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WH ECONOMIC ADVISER STANDS BEHIND MASS FIRINGS\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 So, you're saying everybody who's being let go was doing a bad job?\par \par \uc2 KEVIN HASSETT\uc2  (WHITE HOUSE ECONOMIC ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 I'm saying that we're studying every agency in deciding who to let go and why and we're doing so very rationally with a lot of support from analysis.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Because we're being told by a lot of people who have been let go at other agencies that they were told they were being dismissed because of poor performance when, in some cases, they haven't even had a performance review yet because they've only been on the job a couple of months.\par \par \uc2 KEVIN HASSETT\uc2  (WHITE HOUSE ECONOMIC ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I've never seen a person who was laid off for poor performance say that they were performing poorly.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But as the President's team stood in the briefing room defending his first 30 days, tonight, a new "Washington Post"/Ipsos poll has Trump's approving rating at 45%, with 53% of Americans disapproving. 57% say the President has exceeded his authority since taking office. Only 34% approve of how Musk is handling his role, with 49% disapproving. The President gets his strongest numbers on his top issue, immigration. But even there, the public is split. 50% approving of his performance, and 48% disapproving.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And on the issue of the economy, the President keenly aware that inflation is rising, and now floating the idea of giving money saved through the work of Musk's team directly to the American people. In the meantime, the Senate today confirming Trump's pick for \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, his staunch supporter Kash Patel. This was a tight vote, two Republicans voting against him. But tonight, Patel will now lead the nation's top law enforcement agency. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce at the White House tonight. Mary, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020250224el2k0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SOME FEDERAL WORKERS BEING REHIRED AMID MASS LAYOFFS GROWING FALLOUT FROM TRUMP & MUSK'S MASS LAYOFFS\b0\par\par\uc2 779 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARCTIC BLAST\par \par \uc2 STORMS, SNOW, ICE, ARTIC, FLOODS, TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 STORMS, SNOW, ROADS, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 CRASH, LANDING, FLAMES, ROLLOVER, PASSENGERS, CREW\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, HOSPITALIZED, PNEUMONIA, MARTIN\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, TRUMP, ZELENSKYY, ALLIES\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , LAYOFFS, EMPLOYEES, FALLOUT, KENNEDY, SANDERS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sure doesn't. Okay, Ian, thanks very much. We're gonna turn now to President Trump and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's latest moves to reduce the federal work force. Some of the workers who had been the victim of the mass layoffs, are now being rehired. Senior political correspondent Rachel Scott tracking the story from Mar-A-Lago. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME FEDERAL WORKERS BEING REHIRED AMID MASS LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, good morning to you. We know these federal agencies are moving quickly with the orders from the administration for mass cuts and firings. So much so that the administration this morning is acknowledging that some workers were let go by mistake.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning as the Trump administration works at a break neck pace to shrink the federal work force, ABC News learning mistakes are being made. Food safety and inspection officers for the Department of Agriculture, vital to the nation's bird flu response, fired over the weekend, just as the outbreak intensifies in the US, driving up egg prices.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But a spokesperson says those workers are now being swiftly hired back. And that's not the only agency to reverse course. Hundreds of workers at the \uc2 National Nuclear Security Administration\uc2  fired, then nearly all rehired days later. Sources say some officials were unaware the agency is responsible for managing the nation's nuclear stock pile. The President says he has no concerns about how that was handled.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 In some cases they'll fire people and then they'll put some people back. Not all of them, because a lot of people were let go.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Thousands of workers fired at the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  where the new Secretary, \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2 , plans to investigate the childhood vaccine schedule, even after he promised to support it in his confirmation hearing.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT F. KENNEDY JR\uc2 . (SECRETARY OF HEALTH & HUMAN SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 I promise to listen to all the stakeholders, all the parties, to the conversation including the ones, especially the ones ,with whom I've disagreed in the past. I promise to keep an open mind.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the head of the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's food division under Kennedy is stepping down. Jim Jones saying the firings at the agency demonstrate "The Trump administration's disdain for the very people necessary to implement the Department's agenda of improving the health of Americans."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING FALLOUT FROM TRUMP & MUSK'S MASS LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sources say among those fired, staff working on nutrition and food safety, reviewing potentially unsafe food ingredients. Top officials at the Social Security Administration and Treasury Department resigning too, after \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's staff demanded access to sensitive information about millions of Americans.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A federal judge yesterday refused to immediately block Doge from accessing government data systems. The judge saying there are legitimate questions about what appears to be the "Unchecked authority of an unelected individual," but said the states who sued failed to show how doge poses "Irreparable harm." Democrats and critics insisting there's no oversight.\par \par \uc2 SEN BERNIE SANDERS (IND) (VERMONT)\par \par \uc2 Do you think that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is staying up nights just worrying about excessive spending in the CDC? I don't think so.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For federal workers like Justine Beaulieu, who worked for the Department of Agriculture, the last several days have been a complete roller coaster.\par \par \uc2 JUSTINE BEAULIEU (FMR RISK MANAGER USDA ANIMAL PLANT HEALTH INSPECTOR)\par \par \uc2 I was three days away from my due date on Friday when I got that termination letter. And I had my baby yesterday, right on time. But my maternity, paid maternity leave is off the table and my health insurance is set to lapse at the end of this month.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So adding to all this confusion, we have spoken to some federal workers who opted in for the federal buyout program to resign and be paid through September, but then were fired anyway. They told us they are now receiving conflicting information from both the administration and their direct managers about whether they still have a job, Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250314el2j0002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW ROUND OF MASS GOVERNMENT LAYOFFS IMPACTING MULTIPLE DEPARTMENTS AND AGENCIES\b0\par\par\uc2 1,032 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, MUDSLIDES\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , HOSTAGES, RELEASED, DEKEL-CHEN\par \par \uc2 FEDERAL, WORKER, LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 HELICOPTER, PLANE, DC, CRASH\par \par \uc2 ROCKY, ASSAULT, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 PHILADELPHIA, EAGLES, SUPER BOWL, CELEBRATION\par \par \uc2 LUNAR NEW YEAR, CELEBRATION, SAN FRANCISCO\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP OF "THE GOONIES"\par \par \uc2 FEDERAL, FIRINGS\par \par \uc2 TEEN, RESCUED, MINE\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTS' DAY, SALES\par \par \uc2 SHEDD AQUARIUM, CHICAGO, BELUGA, NAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 STORM\par \par \uc2 HOSTAGES, ISRAEL, DEKEL-CHEN\par \par \uc2 LAYOFFS, GOVERNMENT, MILBURN, ARATA\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are gonna turn now to the latest firings of tens of thousands of federal workers. Some are calling it chaos among the government's workforce. And ABC's senior White House correspondent Selina Wang is here. We brought you in from the White House lawn to be here in the studio to take this, take this on for us. Hey, Selina.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ROUND OF MASS LAYOFFS IMPACTING MULTIPLE DEPARTMENTS & AGENCIES\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is better to be here in the much warmer studio. But you mentioned the word chaos. This is also sending shockwaves throughout the system. The Trump administration is firing thousands of federal workers across the country, and workers who have suddenly been laid off tell me it's not just their livelihoods that are at stake here, but also the people they serve.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the Pentagon bracing for potential cuts with tens of thousands of federal workers from the Department of Health, Homeland Security, and Energy, already in shock after they were suddenly fired from their jobs.\par \par \uc2 CHELSEA MILBURN (FORMER EMPLOYEE DEPT OF EDUCATION)\par \par \uc2 I was definitely upset.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Chelsea Milburn, a disabled veteran, terminated from the Department of Education, says she fears for her financial future, left to juggle her disability and her family's wellbeing.\par \par \uc2 CHELSEA MILBURN (FORMER EMPLOYEE DEPT OF EDUCATION)\par \par \uc2 It kind of felt like having that piece of myself that was given to me, yanked back out from under me.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Milburn says she hopes Americans realize that an attack on civil servants is an attack on veterans.\par \par \uc2 CHELSEA MILBURN (FORMER EMPLOYEE DEPT OF EDUCATION)\par \par \uc2 To the American people, I think they don't recognize that almost 30% of the federal workforce are veterans.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The administration first targeting roughly 200,000 federal workers who were hired within the last one to two years. At least 2,000 workers fired from the Department of Energy, more than a thousand from Veterans Affairs, and another thousand from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control\uc2 , including half of the agency's doctors and scientists who are sent across the country and world to respond to outbreaks. And Carly Arata shocked after she was fired at the Department of Agriculture.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TARGETING 200,000 FEDERAL EMPLOYEES\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What would be your message to Trump and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 CARLY ARATA (FORMER EMPLOYEE DEPT OF AGRICULTURE)\par \par \uc2 This isn't about you anymore. This is about lives that you are ruining.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Trump claims these mass layoffs will make the government more efficient.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We want to downsize government, but make it better.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Cory Crizan Mata (PH) who was laid off from the Department of Energy, working on the legal team for a nuclear cleanup site, tells me he disagrees.\par \par \uc2 CORY (LAID OFF FROM DEPT OF ENERGY)\par \par \uc2 There's no consideration for whether or not this position is critical.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And these cuts are just beginning and federal workers also tell me they've been given no notice, just told to get out and leave. In fact, some are telling me that they're really worried about their colleagues, there was no time to offload their work, and they say that they're already understaffed and overworked, even before all of these layoffs began.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And each of those people has - every single person has a family.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly, exactly.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Selina, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE PROSECUTORS RESIGN OVER NYC MAYOR ADAMS CASE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, another - veteran federal prosecutor has resigned, joining six others in refusing to file a motion to dismiss corruption charges against New York City Mayor \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2 . That motion was eventually filed late Friday, but the dropping of the charges still needs to be approved by a judge. Former acting US Attorney Danielle Sassoon, the first to resign, accused top Justice Department officials of knowledge of a quid pro quo with Adams, dropping the charges in exchange for cooperation on immigration enforcement. Adams has denied any wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK BOXES REVEAL NEW DETAILS IN DEADLY DC CRASH\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Janai, this morning, investigators are shedding new light about what may have gone wrong when a Black Hawk helicopter collided with an \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  plane last month. The \uc2 NTSB\uc2  saying the helicopter pilots may not have known exactly how high the chopper was flying because of bad information from their computers. That crucial black box data comes just over two weeks after the devastating crash, which killed all 67 people aboard the two aircraft. This, of course, was the deadliest crash in the US in decades.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All right. Still coming up here on, in our "GMA" Morning Menu, with credit card debt at an all-time high, we have proven strategies for paying off the charges.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY: CREDIT CARD DEBT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also ahead here, you know who's here, Tory Johnson with "Deals & Steals" to keep you comfortable this weekend.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS: COMFORT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And will Ganss is also here. Hey, Will.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BINGE THIS: OSCARS EDITION\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 From the best deals and the best products, I'm breaking down the best Oscar nominated movies to binge, based on what type of movie fan you are. You don't have much time left until the Academy Awards. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250318el2f00064\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW ROUND OF MASS LAYOFFS IMPACTING MULTIPLE DEPARTMENTS & AGENCIES\b0\par\par\uc2 767 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, MUDSLIDES\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , HOSTAGES, RELEASED, DEKEL-CHEN\par \par \uc2 FEDERAL, WORKER, LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the latest firings of tens of thousands of federal workers, including more than 400 at the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 . Some are calling it chaos amongst the government's workforce. ABC's senior White House correspondent Selina Wang is here following it all. Good morning, Selina.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ROUND OF MASS LAYOFFS IMPACTING MULTIPLE DEPARTMENTS & AGENCIES\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, and great to be on set with you guys for the first time. But first of all, this news, it is sending shockwaves throughout the system, and the Trump administration is firing tens of thousands of federal workers across the country, and workers who have suddenly been laid off tell me it's not just their livelihoods that are at stake here, but also the people they serve.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the Pentagon bracing for potential cuts with tens of thousands of federal workers from the Department of Health, Homeland Security and Energy already in shock after they were suddenly fired from their jobs.\par \par \uc2 CHELSEA MILBURN (FORMER EMPLOYEE DEPT OF EDUCATION)\par \par \uc2 I was definitely upset.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Chelsea Milburn, a disabled veteran terminated from the Department of Education says she fears for her financial future, left to juggle her disability and her family's wellbeing.\par \par \uc2 CHELSEA MILBURN (FORMER EMPLOYEE DEPT OF EDUCATION)\par \par \uc2 It kind of felt like having that piece of myself that was given to me yanked back out from under me.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Milburn says she hopes Americans realize that an attack on civil servants is an attack on veterans.\par \par \uc2 CHELSEA MILBURN (FORMER EMPLOYEE DEPT OF EDUCATION)\par \par \uc2 To the American people, I think they don't recognize that almost 30 percent of the federal workforce are veterans.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TARGETING 200,000 FEDERAL EMPLOYEES\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The administration first targeting roughly 200,000 federal workers who were hired within the last one to two years. At least 2,000 workers fired from the Department of Energy, more than a thousand from Veteran's Affairs, and another thousand from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control\uc2 , including half of the agency's doctors and scientists who were sent across the country and world to respond to outbreaks. And Carly Arata shocked after she was fired at the Department of Agriculture.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What would be your message to trump and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 CARLY ARATA (FORMER EMPLOYEE DEPT OF AGRICULTURE)\par \par \uc2 This isn't about you anymore. This is about lives that you are ruining.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Trump claims these mass layoffs will make the government more efficient.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We want to downsize government but make it better.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Corey Krzan Matta, who was laid off for the Department of Energy working on the legal team for a nuclear cleanup site, tells me he disagrees.\par \par \uc2 COREY KRZAN MATTA (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF DEPARTMENT OF ENERGY)\par \par \uc2 There's no consideration for whether or not this position is critical.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And guys, these cuts are just beginning and federal workers tell me they've been given no notice, just told to get out and leave. And some of these workers, guys, they're telling me that they're also worried about their colleagues. They say that they were already understaffed and overworked before all of this started.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and, and Selina, one of the things that's also happening is that the Vice President gave a policy speech in Germany, and that's really making waves right now, isn't it?\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Gio. Parts of it were pretty surprising. First of all, the Vice President was highly critical of our European allies, and he also told them that their greatest security threat is not Russia or China, but actually from within. He accused them of censoring and pushing aside right wing nationalist groups. And any European leader who was there sitting there in the audience hoping to hear about the Trump administration's plans to end the war in Ukraine, well, they left disappointed because Vance didn't even mention Russia's invasion of Ukraine. But Vance did later meet with Ukrainian leader Zelenskyy, guys.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, Selina, it was great to have you in studio. We appreciate you being here.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250318el2f0005o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP ADMINISTRATION BEGINS MASS LAYOFFS OF FEDERAL WORKERS NEW QUESTIONS OVER MUSK'S MEETING WITH INDIA'S LEADER\b0\par\par\uc2 584 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 STORM, WEST COAST, RAIN, MUDSLIDES, FIREFIGHTERS\par \par \uc2 STORM, ALERTS, SNOW, RAIN, ADVISORIES\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, HOSPITALIZED, TESTS, RESPIRATORY\par \par \uc2 VANCE, ZELENSKYY, RUSSIA, UKRAINE, CHERNOBYL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, FEDERAL, WORKERS, LAYOFFS, MUSK, INDIA\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Huge stakes in these talks. Okay, Tom, thank you. We go now to Washington and the Trump administration beginning mass layoffs of federal workers impacting multiple agencies. Tens of thousands of employees are expected to lose their jobs. Our senior political correspondent Rachel Scott is tracking the latest from the White House. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ADMINISTRATION BEGINS MASS LAYOFFS OF FEDERAL WORKERS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rebecca, good morning to you. And federal workers who did not resign as part of that buyout offer, were warned that they could be laid off or fired. And this morning we are learning that mass layoffs have started across multiple federal agencies.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning the Trump administration taking its sweeping effort to shrink the size of the federal work force one step further, ordering agencies to lay off nearly all probationary employees, meaning those hired within the last one or two years, a move that could impact as many as 220,000 federal workers.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At the Department of Veteran Affairs alone, more than 1,000 new workers were dismissed. Overnight the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau also firing term employees with expectations that the rest may be fired today, leaving a skeleton staff of around 5%. The \uc2 CFPB\uc2  and VA are just two of several agencies that have started to cut federal workers so far.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The administration also targeting the Department of Education and the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 . The largest federal employee union slamming the layoffs, calling it a "Blatant violation of the principles of fairness and merit that are supposed to govern federal employment," and saying "The firings are about power." At some agencies, workers learned by email they had been laid off. But at the Office of Personnel Management, others found out on a call.\par \par \uc2 CHARLES EZELL (ACTING DIRECTOR OFFICE OF PERSONNEL MANAGEMENT)\par \par \uc2 You will receive your termination notice via email shortly. As a result, your employment with the Office of Personnel Management will end today.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW QUESTIONS OVER MUSK'S MEETING WITH INDIA'S LEADER\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who has billions of dollars in federal contracts and spearheading the efforts to slash government spending, also calling for the elimination of whole agencies. Musk sitting down with Indian Prime Minister Modi Thursday before he met with President Trump.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The President unsure the capacity of Musk's meeting and whether Musk was acting as a private citizen wanting to do business in India or a member of the administration.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I would imagine he met possibly because, you know, he's running a company.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump pushed on how a foreign leader may know the difference.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Well he's meeting with me in a little while so I'm gonna ask him that question.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So the Indian Prime Minister was also asked if they discussed any business. He would only say that he has known \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  for a very long time, guys.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250314el2e00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THOUSANDS OF FEDERAL WORKERS FIRED AT LEAST A DOZEN DEPARTMENTS AND AGENCIES AFFECTED\b0\par\par\uc2 700 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, MUDSLIDES, FLASH FLOODING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ADAMS, HOMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7TH PROSECUTOR QUITS OVER ADAMS CASE\par \par \uc2 MUSK, TRUMP, ARATA, LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS OF FEDERAL WORKERS FIRED\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn, in the meantime, to the massive layoffs playing out today of government workers, thousands of them at multiple federal agencies, including the Department of Education, the CDC, and Veterans Affairs. And tonight, ABC News learning that hundreds were laid off at the \uc2 National Nuclear Security Administration\uc2 , the agency that maintains the agency that maintains America's nuclear stockpile before they were called back. Here's Mary Bruce.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST A DOZEN DEPARTMENTS AND AGENCIES AFFECTED\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, across the country, tens of thousands of federal workers from the Department of Education to Health and Human Services, from Veterans Affairs to the Department of Energy, suddenly told they are out of a job.\par \par \uc2 CARLY ARATA (FORMER FEDERAL EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 Last night, I got an email around 9:00 PM saying that that my position was terminated.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Greensboro, Georgia, Carly Arata worked at the Department of Agriculture.\par \par \uc2 CARLY ARATA (FORMER FEDERAL EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I saw the subject of it, and I kind of screamed. I didn't think it was real at first, so I reread it like three times and then kind of started crying. Because, yeah, I was relying on this job. My husband and I just purchased this house in December. And now, we're not really sure what we're going to do.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a meeting at the Office of Personnel Management, some employees were told to, quote, "Gather your personal belongings and exit the premises." ABC News obtaining this audio.\par \par \uc2 CHARLES EZELL (ACTING DIRECTOR OFFICE OF PERSONNEL MANAGEMENT)\par \par \uc2 You will receive your termination notice via email shortly, and it will include the reason for termination. As a result, your employment with the Office of Personnel Management will end today.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The layoffs across at least a dozen departments and agencies, all part of an effort to cut government costs spearheaded by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who told an international conference that whole agencies would have to go.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEARHEADED BY MUSK'S COST-CUTTING INITIATIVE\par \par \uc2 ELON MUSK (DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT EFFICIENCY)\par \par \uc2 We do need to delete entire agencies, as opposed to leave part of them behind.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The administration first targeting the roughly 200,000 federal employees who have been on the job less than a year. At the Department of Energy, at least 2,000 workers let go, more than 1,000 people fired from Veterans Affairs, and another 1,000 from the CDC. Among them, half of the agency's so-called disease detectives. Doctors and scientists who fan out across the country and the world to respond to outbreaks. But this process has been far from smooth. Sources tell ABC News, yesterday, roughly 300 employees at the \uc2 National Nuclear Security Administration\uc2 , the agency that maintains America's nuclear stockpile, were fired. But today, multiple sources tell us those firings were put on hold.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Managers frantically calling the fired employees back, telling them, as of now, they're not fired after all. Their security badges turned back on and their access to federal systems restored, at least temporarily. The firings sending shockwaves through the federal workforce, but President Trump today saying this dramatic workforce reduction is all part of the plan.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We want to downsize government, but make it better. Run it better but downsize.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, this is only the beginning. All day long, we've been learning of more and more cuts at these agencies. Tonight, word that Homeland Security is cutting over 400 employees, including 200 from FEMA. And workers we've talked to say, it just feels so haphazard. No two weeks' notice, no guidance on benefits, just told to pick up and leave. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce at the White House tonight. Mary, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020250221el2e0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOZENS INJURED AFTER CAR DRIVES INTO MUNICH CROWD DRIVER RAMS MINI COOPER INTO TRADE UNION RALLY\b0\par\par\uc2 673 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WINTER, STORM, TRACKING, RAIN, SNOW, ICE, MUDSLIDE, CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST-TO-COAST WINTER STORMS WREAKING HAVOC ACROSS US\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, PUTIN, ZELENSKYY, WAR, HEGSETH, FOGEL, VINNIK, BOLTON\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , MUSK, AGENCIES, BUYOUT, TESLA, STORCH, NYC, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MUNICH, GERMANY, RALLY, CAR, ATTACK, VANCE, ZELENSKYY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, George. We're going to go now to breaking news this morning, an attack in Germany. Dozens of people injured as a driver drove into a group of people in Munich. James Longman join us with the latest. Good morning, James.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOZENS INJURED AFTER CAR DRIVES INTO MUNICH CROWD\par \par \uc2 JAMES LONGMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, good morning, Michael. A car has rammed into a group of people in the southern city of Munich. Twenty-eight people have now been injured. Among them there are critical injuries. A man has now been taken into custody. He's been described as a 24-year-old individual of Afghan origin. It is being described as an attack. A beige MINI Cooper he drove at the scene is now being searched. This was a trade union rally that he drove into, people marching in support of childcare services. And among the belongings that are strown on the street, a stroller. So, this does look to have been an incredibly serious attack.\par \par \uc2 JAMES LONGMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Security in Germany already very high because there have been a number of these sorts of ramming attacks in recent months. And tomorrow is the Munich Security Conference. Vice President \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  is due to speak, as well as the President of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2 . This attack happening just a mile or so away of that conference venue. Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, James, thank you. We turn now to the investigation into a Navy fighter jet crash. The pilots ejected before the plane went down in the water off San Diego. Chief Global Affairs Correspondent Martha Raddatz is in Washington with the latest. Good morning, Martha.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INVESTIGATION INTO NAVY FIGHTER JET CRASH OFF SAN DIEGO\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. Incredible images of this crash, an accident that truly could have been a major disaster.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning extraordinary video of the Navy jet crashing into the San Diego Bay. Watch again as it plunges nose down into the water. And here, a distant image from a nearby surveillance camera.\par \par \uc2 AUDIO CLIP FROM EMERGENCY DISPATCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF DIALOGUE\par \par \uc2 DISPATCHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 They advise that it did land in the water. There's Navy boats now searching the water.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) An immediate search launched for the two pilots after parachuting from the aircraft, rescued within one minute by a tourist fishing boat.\par \par \uc2 DANIEL MOEN (SAN DIEGO HARBOR POLICE DEPARTMENT)\par \par \uc2 They went to the hospital to get treatment. And at that point we just assisted with perimeter for this large debris field that's out here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILITARY PLANE CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRAVEL MAP\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The 67 million dollar Navy jet was attempting a landing on North Island Naval Air station off Coronado Beach. As it came to the end of the runway, it started a go around. The pilots headed back up. And that's when they ejected, landing in the bay avoiding potential catastrophic casualties. That is Shelter Island just a few hundred yards from the point of impact.\par \par \uc2 COLONEL STEPHEN GANYARD USMC (RET) (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As the pilots ejected, it forces the nose of the aircraft down. If they had waited just a fraction of a second longer, that nose down impact could have been into a crowded San Diego neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The good news is that both pilots are in good shape, so they will be able to tell investigators why they felt they had to bail out of that aircraft. George?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250313el2d00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JUDGE EXTENDS FEDERAL WORKER BUYOUT EMPLOYEES PROTEST AT GOVT. CONSUMER WATCHDOG \uc2 CFPB\b0\par\par\uc2 935 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TARIFFS, STEEL, ALUMINUM, GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP TARIFFS ON STEEL & ALUMINUM\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , MUSK, VANCE, BUYOUT, \uc2 CFPB\uc2 , GOGGANS, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE EXTENDS FEDERAL WORKER BUYOUT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's another developing headline involving President Trump at this hour. A judge extending his block on the President's effort to get millions of federal workers to resign, take a buyout or risk getting fired.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the Vice President and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  are now openly questioning the authority of some of these judges. And now, the \uc2 Consumer Financial Protection Bureau\uc2  has been halted. Workers told to stay home. Protests outside today.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The bureau set up to protect Americans from banks becoming too big to fail, and to protect against risky mortgages and other financial products after the banking collapse and Great Recession. So, is the bureau's work protecting consumers over? Here's our senior political correspondent Rachel Scott tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EMPLOYEES PROTEST AT GOVT. CONSUMER WATCHDOG \uc2 CFPB\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, in Washington, frustrated workers at the \uc2 Consumer Financial Protection Bureau\uc2  demanding to be let in to do their jobs...\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Let us work.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...after \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  essentially shut down the agency. Posting on X, "CFPB RIP." The bureau, the government's consumer watchdog, created after the 2008 financial crisis and housing crash to protect American families from unfair and deceptive practices on everything from mortgages to credit cards to bank fees and student loans. But this morning, employees got an email from White House budget director \uc2 Russell Vought\uc2 , saying they should not come into the office and instructing them, "Please do not perform work tasks."\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 You show up to work on Monday morning excited to get started on the week. I had an agenda of things I was ready to do to fight for American consumers. And to be told that I'm not supposed to do that is supposed to do that is heartbreaking.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Like 2 million other federal workers, the people here face a stark choice. Take the government's buyout offer to get paid through September, or risk getting laid off. April Goggans, who works for the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , wrestled with that decision.\par \par \uc2 APRIL GOGGANS (FEDERAL EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I think the last three weeks have been a little bit like some psychological warfare. I mean, just getting tossed back and forth between, do I need to worry about moving? Am I going to lose my house? Do I need to worry about my job? And what can I and cannot I do?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The deadline to accept that deal was extended to today. Now, a federal judge had put it on hold yet again. But April tells me her decision is made.\par \par \uc2 APRIL GOGGANS (FEDERAL EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 No, I'm not resigning. I'm going to hold the line. I'm not resigning.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why?\par \par \uc2 APRIL GOGGANS (FEDERAL EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 You know, first of all, you're not going to, you're not going to bully me out of a job.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The judge's decision to put the buyout offer on hold, just one in a series of legal setbacks for the new administration. And on X, Musk lashing out at the judges, calling a New York judge who blocked his efforts to access Treasury data a corrupt judge protecting corruption. Adding, "He needs to be impeached now."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VANCE: JUDGES CAN'T CONTROL "EXECUTIVE'S LEGITIMATE POWER"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President J.D. Vance taking it even further, posting, "If a judge tried to tell a general how to conduct a military operation, that would be illegal. Judges aren't allowed to control the executive's legitimate power." The big question, will the administration openly defy the rulings of these courts? Tonight, one federal judge determined that's already happening, finding the administration violated his order to fully lift its pause of federal funding, calling the pause likely unconstitutional and adding that it continues to cause irreparable harm to a vast portion of this country.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and his team he already gained access into at least 15 federal agencies.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Musk, a billionaire, is the world's richest man. He owns the social media platform X, \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , and \uc2 SpaceX.\uc2  And tonight, there are reports that he's making a play to buy \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , a leading artificial intelligence company.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The President did launch an initiative with companies initiative with companies, including \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , so this does raise questions about a possible conflict of interest for Musk, who is working with this administration and raises concerns about his growing influence, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott there at the White House as well. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY JET COLLISION AT AIRPORT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're also following a breaking story involving a deadly plane collision at an airport in Scottsdale, Arizona. At least one dead, others have been transported to trauma centers tonight.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This all involved a Learjet coming in for landing, veering off the runway in Scottsdale, then colliding with another Gulfstream jet. Authorities say at least one person has died, multiple people now taken to that hospital. The airport issuing a ground stop there.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020250213el2a00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMPS BUYOUT OFFER FOR FEDERAL EMPLOYEES PUT ON HOLD NEW DETAILS ON MUSK'S PLAN TO CUT USAID WORKFORCE\b0\par\par\uc2 889 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINTER BLAST\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, ICE, HIGHWAYS, ROADS\par \par \uc2 TRAIN, FIRE, PASSENGERS, SERVICE, EVACUATE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BUYOUT, EMPLOYEES, PAUSE, \uc2 USAID\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So grateful for those workers. All right, Stephanie, thank you. We turn now to President Trump and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  drive to reshape and slim down the federal government. Hours before a Midnight deadline a judge temporarily blocked the buyout that's been offered to some federal employees. Senior political correspondent Rachel Scott is tracking this from the White House. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S BUYOUT OFFER FOR FEDERAL EMPLOYEES PUT ON HOLD\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rebecca, good morning to you. And at least 60,000 people opted in to this buyout program from the federal government. But this morning a judge putting that on pause right before the deadline, it's prompting widespread confusion for those who want to resign and those who want to stay on the job.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, widespread confusion for federal workers. It's been just over a week since two million federal employees received this email with a stark choice, resign now and be paid through September or run the risk of being laid off.\par \par \uc2 CHONDA LODER (DEPARTMENT OF VETERAN AFFAIRS EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 It's just all kind of a mess.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Chonda Loder, a mother of two in Kentucky, works for the Department of Veterans Affairs. She took the offer but hasn't gotten any clarity since.\par \par \uc2 CHONDA LODER (DEPARTMENT OF VETERAN AFFAIRS EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 Everyone is just, they're all shaken up and they're all scared. And it was very much a scare tactic, and it definitely worked.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The offer now on hold until Monday, as a legal challenge plays out. Unions calling it arbitrary and unlawful. But the administration insisting the program is not being blocked or cancelled.\par \par \uc2 KAROLINE LEAVITT (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 We encourage federal workers in this city to accepted the very generous offer.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sheria Smith, a civil rights attorney at the Department of Education and a union official, says the offer is flat out insulting.\par \par \uc2 SHERIA SMITH (AFGE UNION OFFICIAL & DEPT OF EDUCATION LAWYER)\par \par \uc2 We're being asked to give up our careers, you know, give up our commitment to the public in a week's time with very conflicting and often at times erroneous information given to us.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The email's title, fork in the road. The same one billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  used when he slashed the work force at \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . Now Musk, who last night posted this photo in the oval office, and his team on a blitz through federal agencies, looking to cut costs.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ON MUSK'S PLAN TO CUT USAID WORKFORCE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sources tell \uc2 USAID\uc2 , the relief agency that brings food, water and health care to victims of natural disasters, will soon have its global work force reduced from roughly 14,000 people to fewer than 300 employees. An internal email shared with ABC News, shows just 12 employees to be assigned to the entire continent of Africa, and only 21 to the whole Middle East. It's an agency whose work the First Lady praised in 2018.\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY MELANIA TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We care, and we want to show the world that we care. And I partnered and I'm working with \uc2 USAID\uc2 , and that's what I want to show, that we care.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And this morning "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " identified more than 30 studies that have now been frozen, from trials for malaria treatment for children in Mozambique, to nutritional support for children in Ethiopia.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A 25-year-old staffer connected to \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's department of government efficiency has resigned after "The Wall Street Journal" reached out to the White House about social media posts they described as racist. ABC News has not independently verified those posts, which have now been deleted.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we are learning that staffer did have access to sensitive information over at the Treasury Department. So now all of this once again prompting questions about who exactly is working for \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and what they have access to, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And whether what they're doing is legal. And in the latest in a series of personnel moves that appear to be illegal on their face, the President moved to dismiss the chairman of the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FEDERAL ELECTION COMMISSION\uc2  CHAIR SAYS TRUMP TRIED TO FIRE HER\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, George. And the FEC was created by Congress to be this independent watch dog over our election system. Overnight the chair of the FEC, \uc2 Ellen Weintraub\uc2 , says that she was fired by President Trump in a letter. She is a Democrat. But this is a bipartisan commission. And under law, the President is supposed to first nominate her replacement. In a statement on social media, she says there is a legal way to remove her and this is not it, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250311el270002w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MUSK DRIVES GOVERNMENT SHAKE-UP DEMOCRATS CALL ON MUSK TO TESTIFY BEFORE CONGRESS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,044 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, ICE STORM\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , GAZA STRIP, PALESTINE, HERZALLAH, LEAVITT, RUBIO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP DOUBLES DOWN ON GAZA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , MUSK, CIA, CONNOLLY, STANSBURY, SPORTS, TRANSGENDER, SPORTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MUSK DRIVES GOVERNMENT SHAKE-UP\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the chaotic moment on Capitol Hill when Democrats called for \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  to testify to explain to the American people what he's doing after being given access to the personal information of millions of federal workers. Tonight, the CIA, the newest agency affected, and millions of federal workers now have 24 hours to respond. Will they take the buyout? And late today at the White House, President Trump signing an executive order banning transgender women from competing in women's sports. How many players does this affect? And what the \uc2 NCAA\uc2  is saying about this just moments ago. Here's our senior political correspondent Rachel Scott tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS CALL ON MUSK TO TESTIFY BEFORE CONGRESS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, on Capitol Hill, Democrats calling on \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  to testify before Congress, demanding to know what he's really up to, now with access to millions of federal workers' personal information.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE GERRY CONNOLLY (DEM) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 I move that the committee subpoena \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  to come report as a witness at the earliest possible moment.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The hearing quickly descending into chaos.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE MELANIE STANSBURY (DEM) (NEW MEXICO)\par \par \uc2 I think it's outrageous that this committee will not even entertain a motion...\par \par \uc2 CONGRESSMAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 That's not a point of order.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE MELANIE STANSBURY (DEM) (NEW MEXICO)\par \par \uc2 He's breaking the law and dismantling our federal agencies and firing federal employees.\par \par \uc2 CONGRESSMAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Out of order. Out of order.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE MELANIE STANSBURY (DEM) (NEW MEXICO)\par \par \uc2 And you will not even entertain a motion to bring him in front of the Oversight Committee?\par \par \uc2 CONGRESSMAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I agree, this is out of order.\par \par \uc2 CONGRESSMAN (MALE) (CONTINUED)\par \par \uc2 The committee is in favor of tabling...\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE MELANIE STANSBURY (DEM) (NEW MEXICO)\par \par \uc2 Yes, let's have order in this country.\par \par \uc2 CONGRESSMAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Stansbury, you're out of order. You know you're out of order. You know the rules of this committee. There's been a motion and...\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE MELANIE STANSBURY (DEM) (NEW MEXICO)\par \par \uc2 Mr. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is out of order in dismantling...\par \par \uc2 CONGRESSMAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CIA, INTELLIGENCE OFFICERS NOW OFFERED BUYOUT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The next target for Musk, the CIA. The agents responsible for keeping Amica's secrets and keeping America safe. Originally exempt from the buyout offers extended to the federal workforce, some 2 million federal workers have just 24 hours left to respond to their buyout offers. At least 40,000 already accepting. Intelligence workers now facing that same deadline to decide whether to resign now or risk getting laid off in the future. A US official tells ABC News, the CIA emailed over a non-classified system a list of new employees to the White House to comply with its view of the federal workforce.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The list including the first names and last initial of employees hired in the past two years. Those employees still on probation or in training are easier to fire. And there is fear tonight. Now the identities of those intelligence officers could be at risk.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTING DEPUTY AG PLEDGES NO REVENGE ON \uc2 FBI\uc2  AGENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LETTER FROM EMIL BOVE, ACTING DEPUTY ATTORNEY GENERAL\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And tonight, at the Justice Department, the acting deputy attorney general sending a letter, calling for calm amid fears of mass firings after requesting the \uc2 FBI\uc2  turnover a list of thousands of \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents and investigators who worked on January 6th cases involving the people who attacked the Capitol and police. Writing, "Let me be clear, no \uc2 FBI\uc2  employee who simply followed orders and carried out their duties in an ethical manner with respect to January 6th investigations is at risk of termination or other penalties." Warning, "Only agents who acted with corrupt or partisan intent" in those investigations should be concerned. And at the White House today, President Trump before the cameras and a cheering crowd in the East Room, signing an executive order banning transgender women and girls from competing in women's sports.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 With this executive order, the war on women's sports is over.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump made this a key issue on the campaign trail, running campaign ads in battleground states. Trans athletes are already barred from participating in sports at K-12 schools or colleges in more than two dozen states. The head of the \uc2 NCAA\uc2  said, of the approximately 510,000 the approximately 510,000 college athletes in this country, fewer than ten are known to be transgender. And tonight, advocacy groups fear this move will only lead to more discrimination and harassment. Surrounded by female coaches and athletes, the President telling schools they will risk losing federal funding if they do not comply.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 With my action this afternoon, we are putting every school receiving taxpayer dollars on notice that if you let men take over women's sports teams or invade your locker rooms, you will be investigated for violations of Title IX and risk your federal funding.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And just moments ago, the \uc2 NCAA\uc2  released a statement, calling President Trump's executive order a clear national standard, saying they will be taking the necessary steps to better align their policies with this new executive order, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott just outside the White House as well tonight. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIRTHRIGHT CITIZENSHIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE BLOCKS TRUMP ORDER\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, one of the President's executive orders is on hold. A federal judge indefinitely blocking his attempt to end birthright citizenship.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The judge ruling the President's executive order barring citizenship to children born to undocumented or temporary immigrants, quote, conflicts with the plain language of the 14th Amendment. The President's order on hold now nationwide as it potentially works through the courts.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020250208el2500004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UNPRECEDENTED MOVE TO OFFER BUYOUTS TO FEDERAL EMPLOYEES\b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 February 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MEDICAL, JET, CRASH, PHILADELPHIA\par \par \uc2 PLANE, HELICOPTER, CRASH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , HOSTAGES, RELEASED, SIEGEL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TARIFFS, MEXICO, CANADA, CHINA\par \par \uc2 DRONE, FIRE FIGHTING PLANE, CRASH\par \par \uc2 OXFORD, SHOOTING, MOTHER, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , CONCUSSIONS\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS, SPACEWALK, RECORD\par \par \uc2 NANCE, PLANE, CRASHES\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , RESPONSE, PLANE, CRASHES\par \par \uc2 TARIFFS, CANADA, MEXICO, CHINA\par \par \uc2 FEDERAL, WORKER, BUYOUTS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meantime, Selina, another topic that we're following here. What more are you learning about Trump's unprecedented move encouraging millions of federal workers to quit their jobs by offering buyouts? How can all of this play out?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNPRECEDENTED MOVE TO OFFER BUYOUTS TO FEDERAL EMPLOYEES\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, guys. This is unprecedented, but President Trump sees it as him fulfilling his campaign vow to slash the size of the federal government. So earlier this week, his administration offered roughly 2 million federal workers the option to resign and to continue getting paid for several months. But if even a fraction of the work force takes the Trump administration up on this offer, it could send shockwaves through the economy, and it could lead to disruptions of critical federal services.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And in the wake of that tragic plane collision, there are concerns here about how this could impact the \uc2 FAA\uc2 . And as you guys know from covering this story, the \uc2 FAA\uc2  has been dealing with a critical shortage of air traffic controllers for decades. So in response to this, the Air Traffic Controller's Union is saying that they are concerned that this could impact public safety if enough of their experienced workers were to resign.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250307el210000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP BLAMES DEI POLICIES FOR COLLISION PRESSED FOR PROOF THAT DIVERSITY HIRING PLAYED A ROLE\b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 January 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CRASH, DONNELLY, SHULMAN, HOMENDY, KERRIGAN, INMAN, SHCRAN\par \par \uc2 PLANE, BLACK HAWK, COLLISION, HEGSETH, INMAN\par \par \uc2 CRASH, COLLISION, BLACK HAWK\par \par \uc2 PLANE, BLACK HAWK, COLLISION, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meantime, tonight, President Trump coming before the cameras in the White House briefing room today calling for a moment of silence. And then, moments later, the President implying that DEI policies, diversity, equity, and inclusion, might have contributed to the crash. Mary Bruce was in the briefing room.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP BLAMES DEI POLICIES FOR COLLISION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESSED FOR PROOF THAT DIVERSITY HIRING PLAYED A ROLE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, with the recovery effort underway and the investigation only just beginning, President Trump, without any evidence, blaming the diversity picks of his predecessors for the deadly crash.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 A group within the \uc2 FAA\uc2 , another story, determined that the workforce was too white, that they had concerted efforts to get the administration to change that and to change it immediately.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The President accusing the previous administrations of hiring air traffic controllers based on diversity goals, not qualifications.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Are you saying this crash was somehow caused and the result of diversity hiring? And what evidence have you seen to support these claims?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 It just could have been. We have a high standard. We've had a much higher standard than anybody else. And there are things where you have to go by brain power.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Trump also acknowledged he wasn't sure if the air traffic controllers made any mistakes. Former President Biden's Transportation Secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  responding, "Despicable," saying, "As families grieve, Trump should be leading, not lying. We put families first, drove down close calls, grew air traffic control, and had zero commercial airline crash fatalities out of millions of flights on our watch."\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, tonight, President Trump is doubling down on these claims that diverse, equity, and inclusion programs are to blame for this tragedy saying it's, quote, "because I have common sense." But, again, he's presented no evidence and this investigation is only just beginning. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce in the briefing room today. Mary, thank you. When we come back here, the other major news of the night. News coming in on the hostages, in fact, eight have been released in Gaza. And right here in the US, millions are on alert right now for severe storms from Texas right up into the northeast. We'll take you through it.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020250203el1u0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP OFFERS BUYOUTS TO MILLIONS OF FEDERAL WORKERS JUDGE TEMPORARILY BLOCKS TRUMP'S FEDERAL FUNDING FREEZE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,013 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 January 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUYOUT TO GET OUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S FUNDING FREEZE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BUYOUT, EMPLOYEES, FUNDING, FREEZE, LEAVITT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She's also tracking a look at the interest rates, there are gonna big some decisions today. We're gonna begin with the latest moves by the Trump administration offering a mass buyout to federal employees with a warning that the jobs could be cut if the buyouts aren't taken.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's also facing backlash over its freeze on spending for billions of dollars in federal programs, and challenges in court. A federal judge has temporarily blocked the freeze pending further review. Chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce starts us off. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP OFFERS BUYOUTS TO MILLIONS OF FEDERAL WORKERS\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Well President Trump is moving at a break neck pace to reshape the federal government and root out what he calls the deep state. This morning taking unprecedented steps to push out people and programs that aren't in lock step with his agenda.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, more than two million federal employees are facing a choice, resign and be paid until the end of September or risk being fired. In an email with the subject line, "Fork in the Road," those interested in the buyout told to reply with one word, "Resign." And given until February 6th, just eight days.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There are a few exceptions, including military personnel, postal staff and immigration and national security officials. The plan, designed not just to trim the federal budget but to ensure a work force that is reliable, loyal and trustworthy according to the email, which also says workers who do lose their job will be treated with dignity and afforded the protections in place for such positions. The largest union representing federal employees says it's not a voluntary buyout but a purge.\par \par \uc2 UNION LEADER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 No one can believe this is a good faith offer and should know that, you know, it's fast track to federal workers being ripped.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE TEMPORARILY BLOCKS TRUMP'S FEDERAL FUNDING FREEZE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And this morning, Trump's plan to halt potentially billions of dollars in federal assistance, has been placed on hold. A federal judge temporarily pausing a White House order to freeze federal grants and loans, possibly impacting millions of Americans just minutes before it took effect.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The White House immediately sparking confusion and panic after it announced plans to pause and review funding for federal assistance programs, potentially impacting everything from disaster relief to free school lunches and Headstart programs for hundreds of thousands of children. Helene Groves is an educator at Camp Field Early Learning Center in Baltimore County.\par \par \uc2 EDUCATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It seems that our most vulnerable populations are the ones who are suffering the most at the, with these executive orders.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The White House is defending the move, saying the review is needed to save money and root out programs that run counter to Trump's priorities, like climate change initiatives or diversity, equity and inclusion programs. But the broad directive sparked confusion even at bigger programs like Medicaid, which provides health insurance for 72 million low income Americans.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) States reporting they couldn't access the Medicaid online portal, instead receiving a warning about possible payment delays due to executive orders regarding potentially unallowable grant payments. The White House saying payments are still being processed and sent, and insisting programs that provide direct benefits to Americans will not be impacted, including Medicaid and also Medicare, Social Security and federal food assistance. But questions remain about funding handed out to states and organizations that's pass along to people in need.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There certainly are lots of organizations that receive funding and then may pass along a benefits, Meals on Wheels for one. They provide meals for over 2.2 million seniors. What is the President's message to Americans out there, many whom supported him and voted for him, who are concerned that this is going to impact them?\par \par \uc2 KAROLINE LEAVITT (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 Again, direct assistance will not be impacted. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But it isn't direct assistance, Karoline, is going to another organization and then trickling down.\par \par \uc2 KAROLINE LEAVITT (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 Direct assistance that is in the hands of the American people will not be impacted.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, Meals on Wheels telling us in a statement, "The lack of clarity an uncertainty unfortunately means seniors will panic, not know where their next meals will come from." George, still a lot of questions about how all of this is going to play out.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There sure are. On another front, during the campaign, President Trump suggested that \uc2 Mark Milley\uc2 , the former Chairman of the Joints Chief of Staff, should face execution. Now his administration is taking action against him.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENTAGON REMOVES GEN MILLEY'S SECURITY DETAIL & CLEARANCE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is continuing to try and seek retribution as promised against his former Chairman of the Joint Chiefs, \uc2 Mark Milley\uc2 . The Trump administration now removing his security detail, suspending his security clearance, and directing the Pentagon to look into General Milley's conduct to determine if his military rank should be reduced.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That could impact his benefits and his personal financials. And they continue to try and wipe his memory from the Pentagon. They are now looking into taking down his official portrait from his time as the Army Chief of Staff. ABC News has reached out to Milley. We have not heard back. George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce, thanks. Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250228el1t0002u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WHOLE FOODS\uc2  WORKERS FORM FIRST UNION AMAZON'S FIRST WORKERS UNION IN PHILADELPHIA\b0\par\par\uc2 738 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 January 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TUBERCULOSIS, OUTBREAK, WIDMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KANSAS REPORTS LARGEST DOCUMENTED U.S. TUBERCULOSIS OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , FUNDING FREEZE, MILITARY, TRANSGENDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP WHITE HOUSE FREEZES FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE PROGRAMS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , IMMIGRATION, NOEM, RAIDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S IMMIGRATION CRACKDOWN INTENSIFIES\par \par \uc2 DEEPSEEK, ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE, SOSNICK, ALTMAN, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, KU, MOGHADDAS, DUNLEAVY, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW POSSIBLE CLUES IN CALIFORNIA WILDFIRES INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 FLU, CASES, HOSPITALIZATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CDC RELEASES ALARMING NEW FLU NUMBERS\par \par \uc2 LOVE, COLLEGE BASKETBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRAMATIC BUZZER-BEATER HELPS ARIZONA UPSET IOWA STATE\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM TV SHOW, "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 LYNSKEY, SUBWAY, RESCUE, HAWKINS, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUBWAY SHOVE SURVIVOR SHARES INCREDIBLE STORY\par \par \uc2 KEYS, AUSTRALIAN OPEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUSTRALIAN OPEN CHAMP MADISON KEYS LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 DOG MAYOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, DEPORTATION, ICE, NEW YORK, NORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S IMMIGRATION CRACKDOWN INTENSIFIES\par \par \uc2 TUBERCULOSIS, OUTBREAK, KANSAS, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KANSAS REPORTS TUBERCULOSIS OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, \uc2 WHOLE FOODS\uc2 , UNION, PHILADELPHIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 WHOLE FOODS\uc2  WORKERS FORM FIRST UNION\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  and the first unionized store in \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's grocery chain. Andrew Dymburt is here for what this means for employees and unionizing across the country. Good morning, Andrew.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning. It'll be the grocery chain's first ever union after workers at a Whole Food in Philadelphia successfully voted to form one, staffers opting to join the \uc2 United Food and Commercial Workers Union\uc2 , in large because they say they want better pay, improved schedules and fair workloads. It's the first successful unionizing effort at a \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  since \uc2 Amazon\uc2  bought it for over $13 billion back 2017. And the company faced a growing number of unionization efforts and talks ever since.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 -owned giant has tried\u160\'00\'A0to fend off attempts at labor organizing by not just \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  stores, but by delivery drivers and warehouse workers, with some employees even going on strike. Last year, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers at a warehouse in Canada did successfully unionize, only to learn their facility, along with all \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouses in Quebec, would be shut down permanently. And after a years-long battle, workers at an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  fulfillment center in North Carolina are finally set for a union vote next month. Similar union progress was made by workers in New York's Staten Island location, but they say \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has refused to come to the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As for the Philadelphia Whole Foods voting to unionize, the company says it's disappointed by the outcome, saying, in part, it offers competitive wages and other benefits, such as 401 (k) plans, guys?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, a lot of activity there. Andrew, thank you. Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," Tennessee women's basketball coach, Kim Caldwell, back on the court seven days after having a baby.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We also have the Jonas Brothers making a special announcement. You're going to hear it first in "Pop News."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, we're kicking off three days, not one, not two but three days of "Deals & Steals" with that woman right there, Tory, and this morning we have a winter with hot bargains starting at $10. And Lara, you have two very special guests with you.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I do, and I'm going to ask a question, and we're doing "Jeopardy!" style. What do Sterling K Brown and Lisa Ann Walter have in common? Well, many things that, some I can't share, but they are both on hit shows, they're both live on "GMA," and they both love "Deals & Steals." How good is that? Stay with us, everybody. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Ooh, that's a new take on it. Did you arrange that yourself?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Well, you know, a little something, something, a little India Arie and I, you know...\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hey, DJ.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Does everybody know that? Robin is responsible for our theme song.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, India Arie, it was a segment that we did here on "GMA" many years ago.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Many years ago. It's taken off.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Well, thank you, Lara Spencer, appreciate that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250228el1s0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SOURCES: 2 MILLION+ FEDERAL WORKERS OFFERED BUYOUTS LUMP-SUM PAYMENT WOULD INCLUDE 8 MONTHS' PAY\b0\par\par\uc2 925 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 January 2025\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , SPENDING FREEZE, EMPLOYEE BUYOUTS, LEAVITT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening, and it's great to have you with us here on a Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We begin tonight with the breaking headline. Sources telling ABC News President Trump is now expected to offer buyouts to nearly all federal workers. More than 2 million Americans. So, how would this work? And what's driving this?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: 2 MILLION+ FEDERAL WORKERS OFFERED BUYOUTS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And it comes as the White House aimed to put a freeze on billions of dollars of federal aid effective at 5:00 today. But then, with minutes to spare, federal judge temporarily blocking the move. That freeze could impact millions of Americans, from seniors to schoolchildren. Questions whether this could affect Head Start, school lunches, Meals on Wheels for seniors.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have it all covered tonight, beginning with the plan to offer buyouts to millions of those buyouts to millions of those federal workers. Here's our chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LUMP-SUM PAYMENT WOULD INCLUDE 8 MONTHS' PAY\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continuing his overhaul of the federal government. ABC News learning the administration is offering all well over 2 million federal employees a buyout to resign, as long as they do it by February 6th, just nine days from now. In an email blasted to federal employees tonight, those interested in taking the buyout told to reply with one word, "Resign." The White House tonight saying, "American taxpayers pay for the salaries of federal government employees, and therefore deserve employees working on their behalf who actually show up to work in our wonderful federal buildings, also paid for by taxpayers." The White House saying they would be paid out until September.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) All of this coming as Trump tries to root out federal spending that doesn't align with his priorities. Tonight, just minutes before the White House put in place a sweeping freeze on potentially billions of dollars in federal grants and loans, possibly impacting millions of Americans, seniors and children across the country, a federal judge temporarily blocking it. Saying, "It seems like the federal government currently doesn't actually know the full scope of the programs that are going to be subject to the pause." The White House today sparking major questions after it announced plans to pause and review funding for federal assistance programs, for everything from free school breakfasts and lunches, Head Start for hundreds of thousands of children, and Meals and Wheels for millions of seniors.\par \par \uc2 KAROLINE LEAVITT (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 Good afternoon, everybody.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The new White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt, in her first briefing, defending the move, saying it's needed to make sure these programs don't run counter to President Trump's agenda.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE PAUSES WHITE HOUSE FUNDING FREEZE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLOCKS TRUMP'S ORDER TO FREEZE BILLIONS IN GRANTS, LOANS\par \par \uc2 KAROLINE LEAVITT (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 What does this pause mean? It means no more funding for illegal DEI programs. It means no more funding for the green new scam that has cost American taxpayers tens of billions of dollars. It means no more funding for transgenderism and wokeness across our federal bureaucracy and agencies.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The broad directive immediately prompting confusion, even at much bigger programs like Medicaid, which provides health insurance for 72 million low-income Americans.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATES REPORT MEDICAID WEBSITE OUTAGES AMID CONFUSION\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) States reporting the online portals down. Medicaid warning of possible payment delays due to executive orders regarding potentially unallowable grant payments. The White House says they expect the portal will be back online shortly, and payments are still being processed and sent.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FUNDING FREEZE COULD IMPACT MILLIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WH: SOCIAL SECURITY, MEDICAID, FOOD NOT IMPACTED\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the administration is adamant, programs that provide direct benefits to Americans, like Medicaid, Social Security, Medicare, and federal food assistance programs will not be impacted.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What is the President's message to Americans out there, many of whom supported him and voted for him, who are concerned that this is going to impact them directly?\par \par \uc2 KAROLINE LEAVITT (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 Again, direct assistance will not be impacted.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Indirect assistance, Karoline. If it's going to another organization and then trickling down?\par \par \uc2 KAROLINE LEAVITT (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 Direct assistance that is in the hands of the American people will not be impacted.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Meals on Wheels telling ABC News, "The lack of clarity and uncertainty unfortunately means seniors will panic, not knowing where their next meal will come from."\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, lawmakers in both parties are accusing the President of overstepping his power, blocking funding that was already allocated by Congress. And on this breaking news of these buyouts, the union that represents federal workers is now blasting the move, saying, quote, "Purging the federal government of dedicated career federal employees will have vast, unintended consequences that will cause chaos for the Americans who depend on a functioning federal government." David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Mary Bruce leading us off tonight. Mary, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020250130el1s00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SETTING CAREER GOALS FOR THE NEW YEAR ON HOW TO GET THE JOB OF YOUR DREAMS\b0\par\par\uc2 988 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HONORING PRESIDENT JIMMY CARTER\par \par \uc2 CARTER, LEGACY, PRESIDENCY, HUMANITARIAN, ROSALYNN\par \par \uc2 PLANE, CRASH, JEJU, VICTIMS, SURVIVORS, WRECKAGE\par \par \uc2 ROUGH LANDINGS, \uc2 AIR CANADA\uc2 , KLM\par \par \uc2 CRASH, VICTIMS, BLACK BOXES, LANDING, SPEED\par \par \uc2 NEW YEAR'S EVE, TIMES SQUARE, SECURITY, \uc2 NYPD\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , EAGLES, NFC EAST, BARKLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CROSS COUNTRY STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CARTER, LEGACY, PRESIDENCY, HUMANITARIAN, ROSALYNN\par \par \uc2 UPDEGROVE, CARTER, LEGACY, PRESIDENCY, NOBEL LAUREATE\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, FREEDMAN, DA, ATTORNEY GENERAL, CONFLICT\par \par \uc2 SEACREST, "NEW YEAR'S ROCKIN' EVE"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRIBUTE, PRESIDENT, CARTER, DEATH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING TRIBUTES FOR THE FORMER PRESIDENT\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, PLANE, CRASH, SOUTH KOREA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 179 KILLED IN SOUTH KOREA PLANE CRASH\par \par \uc2 HIRASHIKI, CAMERAMAN, MEMORIAL, ABC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TONY HIRASHIKI\par \par \uc2 CARTER, MARRIAGE, FAITH, LOVE, BOND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JIMMY & ROSANYLNN CARTER'S LOVE STORY\par \par \uc2 "DICK CLARK'S NEW YEAR'S ROCKIN' EVE", SEACREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RYAN SEACREST TALKS NEW YEAR'S ROCKIN' EVE\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, GIFT CARDS, HOLIDAYS, DISCOUNT, DEALS\par \par \uc2 GADOT, VIKINGS, MONTY\par \par \uc2 GOALS, CAREER, ADVICE, OTTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SETTING CAREER GOALS FOR THE NEW YEAR\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now with setting career goals for the new year, and joining us is career expert and author Laura Gassner Otting with some great tips for how to get the job. It's nice to see you, Laura. Happy almost new year to you.\par \par \uc2 LAURA GASSNER OTTING (CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 It's great to be back.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And there's a lot of people who look at a new year as a new opportunity, and you say there could be really good work opportunities for people in the new year.\par \par \uc2 LAURA GASSNER OTTING (CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. January is an amazing time to look for jobs because the decision-makers are back in the office, the fiscal year is starting, projects are getting underway, and we're also going to get a slew of people who quit, maybe after they got their end-of-year bonus or maybe if they didn't get their end-of-year bonus. So, it's a time to make a plan to start networking and to follow up.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And if you were sending out emails last year, and you weren't, or at this time, and you weren't getting follow-ups, good to re-reach out to them.\par \par \uc2 LAURA GASSNER OTTING (CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. You know, the people who are hiring you, it's usually not their job. Most of the jobs in this country are small businesses, and so they don't have someone whose entire job is hiring. So, go back, follow up because they likely were a little busy. It has nothing to do with you. They were just busy.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, always, I try to never think that it's about you, and I always tell young people to not go that route because you don't want to get in that negative headspace.\par \par \uc2 LAURA GASSNER OTTING (CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely, don't take it personally.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, we have a great viewer question from Will White, he's from Huntington, New York. Let's take a look.\par \par \uc2 WILL WHITE (VIEWER)\par \par \uc2 How can I focus on my strengths and stand out when I'm applying for a new job?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESUME REFLECTIONS: WHAT COMES EASY TO YOU?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Standing out, especially in this world, everything is digital, how do you do it?\par \par \uc2 LAURA GASSNER OTTING (CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 So, your strengths are hidden in three places. The first, look at the compliments that you get. We're so used to going, like, "Oh, it's nothing" and brushing it off, but the truth is what seems mundane to you is actually magical to others, and your strengths lie in that magic. The second is look at your wins. So, pick three to five things that you did really well, either professionally, could even be personally, like in your place of worship or your fantasy football league, and figure out what habits, what skills, what traits you had to bring about to get those goals all the way to successes?\par \par \uc2 LAURA GASSNER OTTING (CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 And then lastly, think about what didn't go so well. What did you have to learn? Who did you have to meet? What skills did you have to bring about in order to persevere to the other side of that challenge?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And when you, on that number three, what should people, how should people frame that idea, and how much should you be bringing that to an interview conversation, for example, with that question of, you know, what are your weaknesses. What do you say about that?\par \par \uc2 LAURA GASSNER OTTING (CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Yes, so, the worst answer you can give is like, "Oh, I work too hard," right. That's not really\u160\'00\'A0a weakness. So, let's talk about what you really did. Now, in 20 years of executive search, when I listen to people tell me about a weakness, I always listen to see if they actually could turn the mirror back on themselves. So, are they just blaming other people, or can they tell me about here's what I did, and here's what I learned so that it wouldn't happen again, and I can get better.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what's the one word people should never use?\par \par \uc2 LAURA GASSNER OTTING (CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 You never want to hear the word deserve because I'm guessing your manager also thinks they deserve a raise or a promotion, too. So, let's talk about how maybe you've earned that through very specific, quantitative results.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW YEAR CAREER TIPS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Laura, thank you so much, as always.\par \par \uc2 LAURA GASSNER OTTING (CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250127ekcu0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 2 RESCUED, 179 DEAD IN SOUTH KOREA PLANE CRASH OFFICIALS: PILOT DECLARED 'MAYDAY' SHORTLY BEFORE CRASH\b0\par\par\uc2 1,517 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2024 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 PLANE, CRASH, BOEING, SOUTH KOREA, CAUSE, SURVIVORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CRASH\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have breaking news as we come on the air this morning. A plane crash in South Korea has taken the lives of 179 people, that's all but two of the people on board, as it made a runway crash landing. For the very latest on this tragedy, we turn to ABC News transportation correspondent, Gio Benitez. Gio, what, what do we know about the cause of this crash?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2 RESCUED, 179 DEAD IN SOUTH KOREA PLANE CRASH\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, Jon, this is just an unspeakable tragedy, and there's a lot that we don't know right now. That's the problem. But we know that there were 181 passengers and crew on this plane, and like you said, nearly all of them lost their lives in this. You're, you're seeing the images right there. This is really the only part of this plane that's still recognizable. It's really the tail . And, and this happened in South Korea because they actually had to, to land there. There was some sort of distress signal that was sent before the landing, and we know that local transportation officials were saying that there was a warning about a bird strike.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS: PILOT DECLARED 'MAYDAY' SHORTLY BEFORE CRASH\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But at, at, this point when you look at this, it's, it's hard to imagine how a bird strike alone could have caused something like this, but we just don't know. And, and we're not going to show you the full video here because it's really, really disturbing, but basically this plane, this \uc2 Boeing\uc2  737 from \uc2 Jeju Air\uc2  was actually able to land on its belly without the, that landing gear deployed. And so the big question is, why did it not have that landing gear deployed? Why did it not slow down when it was landing on its belly, and then why there was this wall. There was this wall at the airport near the runway.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAUSE OF CRASH UNCLEAR AS INVESTIGATORS ARRIVE ON SCENE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When it veered off course, the plane actually hit that wall. That's when it exploded. So, there are so many questions about all of this. And, and the sad part about this, there's so many sad parts about this, but what's really tragic about this is, if that wall hadn't been there, they likely would have been able to survive this.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and this was a \uc2 Boeing\uc2  737-800. That is one of the most common airplanes in the world. I believe there are more than 4,000 of them currently in operation. That's about 15 percent of all commercial passenger planes in the world. What, what does this mean for the rest of those \uc2 Boeing\uc2  737-800 around the world?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, well, you know, Jon, I know that a lot of people online, when they're look at this, they're saying, wait a minute. It's a \uc2 Boeing\uc2  plane. We saw what happened in January with that door plug on the \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2  plane. Is this somehow related to being a \uc2 Boeing\uc2  problem? At this point, there's no indication of that. This is a 15-year-old plane, and like you said, it is one of the most popular models in the world. So many people fly this plane. And when you look at \uc2 Jeju Air\uc2 , right? This is the airline. They actually have an incredibly strong safety record. They only have one incident almost two decades ago, and it was a plane that actually went off the runway and six people were injured in that, but everyone survived there.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In this case, it's very, very different because when it landed, we still don't know why it wasn't able to slow down. Sometimes they have these crush pads at the end of airport runways to slow planes down. We don't know if that was there, but certainly you see how fast it was moving. And then, of course, that wall. And so, that's the biggest factor here is that wall there. But, no doubt, we want to know about that distress signal. Why did that happen? Why was there a mayday call? And so, that investigation is going to take some time.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gio Benitez, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Turning back to politics, while many of us were celebrating Christmas and Hanukkah, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  ignited what the "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " is calling a, quote, "MAGA civil war." It started with a Christmas Day post by Musk on his X platform saying that the United States needs to quickly let in more foreign workers, specifically highly-educated engineers to work for American tech companies. "The number of people who are super talented engineers and super motivated in the US is far too low," Musk declared. "Think of this like a pro sports team. If you want your team to win the championship, you need to recruit top talent wherever they may be."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOCIAL MEDIA POST FROM ELON MUSK\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) On one hand, there was nothing unusual about what Musk was saying. American companies have been complaining for years about how hard it is to get visas for the most highly skilled workers. And in a podcast last summer, Trump himself told tech entrepreneur David Sachs that the US needs to recruit top talent from around the world, and he reiterated his support for H-1B foreign visas just yesterday in an interview with "The New York Post."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOCIAL MEDIA POST FROM \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Shortly after Christmas, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  chimed in to agree with Musk, saying that American culture is to blame for the shortage of American workers. "Our American culture has venerated mediocrity over excellence for way too long," Ramaswamy posted on X. "A culture that celebrates the prom queen over the math Olympiad champ, or the jock over the valedictorian, will not produce the best engineers." But the call for letting in more foreign workers ran smack against the beliefs of some of Trump's most hardcore supporters. They take America first to mean restricting immigration of all kinds.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOCIAL MEDIA POST FROM LAURA LOOMER\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Laura Loomer, who traveled with Trump for a while during the fall campaign, blasted the call for more foreign workers and the influence of Musk and other tech billionaires on Trump, saying, quote, "Allowing big tech executives into Mar-a-Lago is going to be the death of our country." And there's more. Musk hit back on his pro-Trump critics with a series of profanity-laced posts saying, quote, "I will go to war on this issue the likes of which you cannot possibly comprehend."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOCIAL MEDIA POST FROM \uc2 STEVE BANNON\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That outburst prompted \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  to hit back at Musk, saying, "Someone please notify Child Protective Services' need to do a wellness check on this toddler." Yep, that's Trump's former chief strategist calling \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  a, quote, "toddler." If it is a MAGA civil war, the opening salvos may have been fired a few days earlier at the big Turning Point USA event in Arizona that featured speeches by Trump and his biggest MAGA supporters. Check out what his son, Don Jr., had to say in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM DECEMBER 19\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP JR. (\uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 'S SON)\par \par \uc2 In DC, it's not just the Democrats that are our foes. It's a vast majority of the Republicans. Call them out. Call their offices. Put on that pressure. Make them feel the pain.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Bannon was a featured speaker out there too. He took a shot right at Republican Speaker of the House, Mike Johnson.\par \par \uc2 STEVE BANNON\uc2  (FORMER TRUMP STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 Clearly Johnson's not up to the task. He's got to go, right? He's got to go. Should Johnson be speaker of the House?\par \par \uc2 SUPPORTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 No!\par \par \uc2 SUPPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Get rid of him!\par \par \uc2 STEVE BANNON\uc2  (FORMER TRUMP STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 President Trump, these are your people.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) By the way, Mike Johnson will stand for reelection as speaker of the House in just five days, in an election where he cannot afford to lose more than a single House Republican. In just a few minutes, we're going to talk with a House Republican and a Trump supporter about how these fights will play out before Trump is sworn in again as president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020250107ekct00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  WORKERS BACK ON THE JOB AFTER FIVE-DAY STRIKE AMAZON STRIKE ON PAUSE AFTER WEEK-LONG WALKOUT\b0\par\par\uc2 622 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POST-CHRISTMAS TRAVEL RUSH\par \par \uc2 WINTER, SNOW, RAIN, WINDS\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, TRAVELERS, AAA, ROADS, HOPPER, FLIGHTS\par \par \uc2 KAZAKHSTAN, PLANE, CRASH, SURVIVORS, VIDEO, BIRD, STRIKE, RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 TAXI, STRIKES, PEDESTRIANS, \uc2 MACY'S\par \par \uc2 COSTCO\uc2 , EGGS, FDA, RECALL, SOUTH, SALMONELLA, SYMPTOMS\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SPENDING, ECOMMERCE, IN-STORE, MASTERCARD, POLLS, GIFTS, VALUE\par \par \uc2 CHRISTMAS, \uc2 NFL\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , BEYONC\u201\'00\'C9, \uc2 DISNEY\uc2 , CAREY, NETFLIX, CHIEFS, RAVENS, \uc2 KNICKS\uc2 , SPURS\par \par \uc2 LIVELY, BALDONI, "IT ENDS WITH US", LAWSUIT, TEXTS, JONES, SLATE\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "IT ENDS WITH US"\par \par \uc2 FIRE, RESCUE, HOME, FIRE, COOKING, ALARM, DOOR, SAFETY, KERBER\par \par \uc2 POST-HOLIDAY, SALES, STORES, ITEMS, GIFTS, DECOR, TOYS, TARGET, OLD NAVY, ATHLETA\par \par \uc2 TIMES, SQUARE, NEW, YEARS, EVE, BALL, DROP, NUMBERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORMS\par \par \uc2 STRIKES, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZONS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the latest on the high-profile strikes during the holiday season. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers are back now on the job while the strike impacting Amazon is on you pause. Elizabeth Schulze is back with the very latest there. Hey, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  WORKERS BACK ON THE JOB AFTER FIVE-DAY STRIKE\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Janai. Well, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employees are back at work this morning after a five-day strike that the union is calling the biggest in its history.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Starbucks United Union says 5,000 baristas demanding higher wages walked off the job on Christmas eve, shutting down more than 300 stores across 43 states. Now, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  points out that is just a fraction of the more than 10,000 locations that it owns across the US. And the coffee chain accuses the union of walking away from the bargaining table saying, "We are ready to continue negotiations over pay and benefits." Meantime, that week-long Amazon strike is also now on pause.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON STRIKE ON PAUSE AFTER WEEK-LONG WALKOUT\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  tells us that delivery workers picketed at more than 200 Amazon locations nationwide, seeking better pay and better working conditions. Amazon insists that the strike didn't have any impact on operations and delivery of holiday packages.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But big picture, both of these unions say their fight is not over. There were already more strikes last year than in any year since 2000 and that trend does appear to be intensifying, guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, something to watch. Elizabeth Schulze, thank you so much. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:12, HOLIDAY RETURNS 101\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up here on our "GMA Morning Menu," returns 101. What you can do about the holiday gifts that you don't want, including those gift cards.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Why are you looking at me?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:35, GETTING FINANCIALLY FIT FOR THE NEW YEAR\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also ahead here, getting financially fit for the new year. Moves to make the most of your money before January 1st and beyond.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:19, POP NEWS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And, hey, I'm going to let you finish but we have more on Beyonce's gift to her fans, her spectacular \uc2 NFL\uc2  halftime performance. That's coming up with Will in "Pop News."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:30, SEASONAL SKIN CARE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And we have a winter glow-up guide for all skin types. Expert Maya Allen is here with advice for making your skin look and feel amazing this time of year. You don't want to miss that. That's coming up right here on "GMA." Stick around.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250120ekcq00039\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 EXPANDING STRIKES AMAZON & \uc2 STARBUCKS\b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY DEEP FREEZE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHITE CHRISTMAS?\par \par \uc2 STORMS, WIND CHILL, SNOW, RAIN, ICE\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, TRAVEL, AMTRAK, AIRPORTS, ROADS\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, THOMPSON, CHARGES, STATE, FEDERAL, BRAGG\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, COMMUTED, INMATES, SHUTDOWN, TRUMP, MUSK\par \par \uc2 DRONES, FALL, HOLIDAY, INJURED, LUMSDEN, \uc2 FAA\par \par \uc2 NAVY, PILOTS, EJECTS, SHIP, FRIENDLY FIRE\par \par \uc2 STRIKES, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, EXPANDING, WORKERS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Very, very complex. Okay, Stephanie, thank you. We turn now to workers picketing at two major US companies, Amazon and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , expanding just before Christmas. Elizabeth Schulze has the latest. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. Workers for both \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and Amazon are out on the picket lines this morning trying to leverage this busy holiday shopping time to make their case for better pay and working conditions. The \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  union now says that it strike will expand through Christmas Eve to a dozen metro areas, including Boston, Dallas, Fort Worth and Portland, Oregon.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The union tells us that these strikes shutdown nearly 50 stores on Sunday, though that is a small fraction of about 11,000 locations that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  owns in the USA and in Canada. The big issue here is wage increases. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  says it already offers a competitive average pay of $18 an hour plus benefits.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meantime this weekend, the teamsters union said that Amazon workers at a major airport in Southern California joined other delivery workers on strike in New York, Illinois and Atlanta. Amazon has rejected employee's efforts to unionize.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It says that these strakes are outside workers and it insist that operations are not affected. So far Amazon has not reported any delays for all of those holiday packages, guys.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Elizabeth, thank you. And, guys, whatever you do, just be kind to the people working so hard over the holidays this week.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250117ekcn00030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEAMSTERS EXPAND AMAZON STRIKE DRIVERS WALK OFF SEVERAL FACILITIES ACROSS FOUR STATES\b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 STORM, ARCTIC, SNOW, HOLIDAYS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 NAVY, JET, SHOT DOWN, PILOTS, RED SEA, MULROY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NAVY JET SHOT DOWN BY "FRIENDLY FIRE"\par \par \uc2 DRONES, LIGHT SHOW, FALL, INJURED, \uc2 FAA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRONES FALL INTO CROWD DURING LIGHT SHOW\par \par \uc2 HIGH-SPEED, CRASH, MALL, SUSPECT, POLICE, INJURIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER CRASHES INTO BUSY TEXAS MALL\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, STRIKE, TEAMSTERS, DELIVERIES, WORKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEAMSTERS EXPAND AMAZON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that youngest victim just six years old. All right, Zohreen, thank you. And just days before Christmas, the teamsters union is expanding its strike against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . They say they represent 10,000 workers and contractors demanding better pay and working conditions. But \uc2 Amazon\uc2  says those on the picket lines are not employees. So what's going on here? Let's bring in ABC's Faith Abubey. Faith, this is becoming a war on words. What impact could this have?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEAMSTERS EXPAND AMAZON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVERS WALK OFF SEVERAL FACILITIES ACROSS FOUR STATES\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Rachel. Delivery drivers here for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  at this location tell me that they have not clocked back into work since last Thursday, choosing instead to be here on the picket lines. They're also losing out on their regular paychecks this holiday season as they try nationwide to bring \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The strike has grown this weekend, since it started coast to coast at seven \uc2 Amazon\uc2  locations. The teamsters union leading the effort saying there are almost 10,000 \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers on the picket lines demanding contracts that offer safer work conditions, higher wages and better benefits. So far, though, the e-commerce giant has refused to even negotiate, calling this is a protest, not a strike.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They claim because there is no work stoppage, a majority of people on the picket lines are not their employees. But, Rachel, the reality here is, we're just three days away from Christmas. \uc2 The National Retail Federation\uc2  estimates more than 20% of holiday shoppers spent the weekend busy buying last-minute gifts. But \uc2 Amazon\uc2  says the teamsters union actions will not affect their deliveries. Rachel.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020241224ekcm00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SOME \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  WORKERS & DRIVERS FOR AMAZON WALK OFF THE JOB AHEAD OF HOLIDAYS\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CAR, ATTACK, GERMANY\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, TRAVEL, WINTER, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 STORMS, SNOW\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SENATE, GOVERNMENT, SHUTDOWN, AVERTED\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This morning, thousands of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers as well as contracted delivery drivers for Amazon, two of the country's most popular brands are picketing, and just days before Christmas. ABC's Zohreen Shah is following developments from California, one of several states impacted this morning. Zohreen, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Janai. I was at a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  nearby just yesterday and protesters there were fired up. They know the holiday season is a critical time for consumers. They're hoping it will move the dial at their company.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 No contract.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WORKERS (CROWD)\par \par \uc2 No coffee.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With just four days to go until Christmas, thousands of workers protesting two major American companies.\par \par \uc2 KAI KRAWCZENIUK (\uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  SHIFT SUPERVISOR)\par \par \uc2 We struggle every month to pay our rent, to afford groceries, and that's unacceptable.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WORKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Don't get it.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WORKERS (CROWD)\par \par \uc2 Shut it down.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  baristas in California, Chicago, and their home base, Seattle, began a five day strike Friday demanding better pay, benefits, and resolution to what they say are unfair labor practices.\par \par \uc2 NAOMI MARTINEZ (UNION SPOKESPERSON)\par \par \uc2 The holiday season is huge for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , and there is an economic aspect to striking that's really important.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Workers say \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  backtracked on an agreement with only 2 percent wage increases now for most baristas. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  says the union is demanding far more, proposing an increase that they claim is, quote, "not sustainable."\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Put it in park. Put it in park.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And it's day three for delivery drivers for Amazon on the picket line in four states after the company ignored the deadline the teamsters union had set for their contract negotiations. One striker speaking to our Matt Gutman.\par \par \uc2 RANDY KORGAN (\uc2 INTERNATIONAL BROTHERHOOD OF TEAMSTERS\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 This is, this is not the peak of what we're doing right now. This is only the beginning.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Amazon claiming most of those protesting are not Amazon employees and insist there's been no impact on deliveries. But the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  says if your package is delayed during the holidays, you can blame Amazon's insatiable greed.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We're hardworking individuals. We work hard every day, and I think a billion dollar company could afford to give us the benefits that we're looking for.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  does not have a contract with Amazon. They're employed by other companies, but the workers on strike say every aspect of their work revolves around Amazon, and the company should take responsibility. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So much going on there. All right, Zohreen, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250117ekcl00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 NEMCOVA, TSUNAMI, ALL HANDS AND HEARTS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go to Ginger.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I am so glad they're down there in North Carolina too. Wonderful, wonderful story. Thank you so much to Diane and everybody. You know, let's check in on the snow that's been falling. My home town, Grand Rapids, Michigan. The temp is 27, so any of those roads that are untreated, that's gonna be slick. That's 196 there. And then look at Pittsburgh this morning, the snow flying. So it is going to make just enough to make the roads not so easy to navigate. And it is not going to go anywhere, not for a couple of days at least. With that arctic air in place, it will feel like the teens in Washington DC, going into early next week. And even into Florida, the wind chills are in the 40s. But don't worry, it warms up. Let's get a check a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRE-CHRISTMAS WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY WEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck00066\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA REVISITS THE TSUNAMI THAT CHANGED HER LIFE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,477 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 NEMCOVA, TSUNAMI, ALL HANDS AND HEARTS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now to supermodel Petra Nemcova's mission. After surviving the deadly tsunami that struck countries throughout southeast Asia 20 years ago, she's turned that pain into purpose, vowing to help victims of natural disasters after most of the world had moved on. She sat down with our Diane Sawyer to talk about putting that experience into action and her life now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PETRA NEMCOVA REVISITS THE TSUNAMI THAT CHANGED HER LIFE\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We've seen her face. That beautiful woman on the cover of magazines. The world renowned supermodel Petra Nemcova. Also a woman with a powerful purpose. Turning a horror she experienced into hope for other people. 20 years ago, she was a 25-year-old on a dream vacation in Thailand with the boyfriend she loved. Then the historic and deadly tsunami savaged southeast Asia. The monstrous wall of water, steel, and metal carried her boyfriend, Simon Atlee, to his death, as he called out her name. Somehow she managed to grab onto the top of a palm tree and she held on for nearly eight hours in searing pain from all her broken bones.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 I think in everyone's life in some point, you know, there's a, there's a tragedy in some way that the tragedy gives us an opportunity to put meaning into our life.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That was Petra Nemcova when I first met her 20 years ago. This is Petra today.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 I feel like everything changed. My, my personal life, my professional life, my values, my purpose in life.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But even as she healed, she kept reliving the screams of the children propelled by that water, just out of reach.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 Children trying to scream for help. I couldn't go and, and swim to them, or try to help them cause I couldn't move, move my legs. I couldn't do anything. That pain, it's, it's with me so strongly every single day. That day of the tsunami, I didn't have a choice to help children. But today and every day, I have a choice, and that keeps moving me every day. And we all have a choice every day.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And that's why two decades ago she had an idea. She would use her own money and time to try to build an army of volunteers to keep helping the victims of natural disasters long after the world's attention has moved on.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 The two, three months after natural disasters, that's usually the time when also different organizations leave. The depression goes deeper, and that's when many suicides happen. And if there is no more support from organizations, you're like, how I ever going to rebuild my life?\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And today, her idea has become a noble nonprofit now called All Hands and Heart. Through the years, 68,000 volunteers deploying in the aftermath of tsunamis, tornados, hurricanes, all around the world, rebuilding schools and homes. Almost two months ago, hurricane Helene smashed into the mountains of North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 In Helene, we were there day 2. And we made commitment to stay for one year.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For one year there will be those people in purple shirts, the healing sight of All Hands and Hearts. Kind strangers who have come to help and to stay.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 Hi, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN YOUNG (CONTRACTOR SUPERVISOR OF VOLUNTEERS)\par \par \uc2 Thanks for coming.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Robin Young is an experienced contractor supervising the volunteers.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 This is incredible, the destruction here. So how high was the debris here?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN YOUNG (CONTRACTOR SUPERVISOR OF VOLUNTEERS)\par \par \uc2 It's insane. At least 30 feet tall. Trees, cars, houses. Across the street there was a cabin wrapped around that tree over there.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They plan to help 500 families in North Carolina. Families like Maggie and Craig Chamberlain. Their home before the hurricane, now still standing but gutted by mud and water.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE CHAMBERLAIN (NORTH CAROLINA RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 But we were not in a flood zone here.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE CHAMBERLAIN (NORTH CAROLINA RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Hence that's why we didn't have flood insurance.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 Most homes here don't have flood insurance at all.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE CHAMBERLAIN (NORTH CAROLINA RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Right.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 You would never expect flooding happening here in such mountainous areas.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE CHAMBERLAIN (NORTH CAROLINA RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Right, yeah.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The volunteers in purple shirts have arrived to help Maggie clear out the wreckage of her home. The black mold, the debris, the despair.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE CHAMBERLAIN (NORTH CAROLINA RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Bedroom, it was actually like a little mini hospital in here because my husband has been on hospice for, I guess, about eight months. He was comfortable here.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 With Helene happening, this is your, you're fighting two big fights.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE CHAMBERLAIN (NORTH CAROLINA RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Two, two big ones, yeah.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, they're calling on everyone watching to join their army of hope.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 In the new year, we will need lots of volunteers, lots of support to come and join us. And we have incredibly experienced staff. You don't need any skills.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jessica Thompson is the CEO of All Hands and Hearts.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA THOMPSON (CEO OF ALL HANDS AND HEARTS)\par \par \uc2 Right now we are responding to hurricanes Helene and Milton in North Carolina and Florida. We still have work in Maui, Hawaii, for the wildfires, and we also have school construction projects in Mexico, Nepal, and the Philippines.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 There's still a lot more to do.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And among the volunteers at Petra's side, there to help, are the family of someone she loved, someone who was lost in the tsunami 20 years ago, photographer Simon Atlee.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 Simon's family became my family and Simon's friends became my friends. I'm so grateful for them because they embraced me with so much love.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And embraced her own new family. In 2019, Petra married entrepreneur Benjamin Larretche. They now have a son, Bodhi.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 And I have a son, and I have a beautiful husband. And, and there are so many blessings to be grateful for, yes. I was lucky because I, I met another twin flame. And Ben is my twin flame, and he's an incredible soul. And I just feel so lucky because I didn't know it was going to happen, and, and he's, they're my two loves, Ben and Bodhi, and they just bring lots of sunshine. And Bodhi means enlightenment.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SAWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And so next week, when we all look back at the 20th anniversary of the tsunami, remember Petra Nemcova and her volunteers who will be lighting candles, not to remember the darkness, but to believe in the power of light.\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 And we will invite everybody to join us to light a candle to bring more light to the world.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Petra's definitely made her pain her purpose and is bringing a lot of light to the world, indeed. And our friends at \uc2 National Geographic\uc2  also recently released a series documenting the events of that day, "Tsunami Race Against Time" is available on \uc2 Disney\uc2 +.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck00065\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP BACKED SPENDING PLAN FAILS IN HOUSE AS SHUTDOWN LOOMS FEDERAL WORKERS' PAYCHECKS IN JEOPARDY WITH SHUTDOWN LOOMING\b0\par\par\uc2 831 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Morgan, thank you. We turn now to Capitol Hill and lawmakers racing to avert a government shutdown ahead of a Midnight deadline. There had been a bipartisan deal to keep the government running, but President-Elect Trump came out against it. And last night a deal backed by Trump failed to pass. Our chief Washington correspondent \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2  is tracking the latest. Good morning, Jon.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP BACKED SPENDING PLAN FAILS IN HOUSE AS SHUTDOWN LOOMS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. In a way, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  got exactly what he wanted, that bipartisan deal that had been negotiated over months with Republicans and Democrats went down, but so did the bill that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wanted to replace it.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight President-Elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doubled down, saying there will be no deal unless Congress extends or eliminates the debt ceiling. This after an 11th hour deal backed by Trump failed badly on the House floor, as a whopping 38 Republicans defied him and voted against it.\par \par \uc2 HOUSE MEMBER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The bill is not passed.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That Republican deal would have temporarily funded the government through March and provided $110 billion in disaster aid. It also meant a last-minute Trump demand, raising the limit on how much the government can borrow for two years. But more than three dozen Republicans refused to go along with it.\par \par \uc2 REP CHIP ROY (REP) (TEXAS)\par \par \uc2 Because you never have any ounce of self-respect to go out and campaign, saying you're going to balance the budget and then you come in here and pass a $110 billion unpaid for.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Before that happened, Congress had been poised to vote on a spending deal with bipartisan support. That is until \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the world's richest man and increasingly one of Trump's closest advisers, started attacking it earlier this week, arguing it was filled with wasteful spending.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then trump weighed in with an entirely different demand, to raise or eliminate entirely the so-called debt ceiling that limits how much money the federal government can borrow. Lifting that debt ceiling would make it possible for Trump to borrow and spend more when he becomes president. As President-Elect Trump told me, "If we don't get that, then we're going to have a shutdown."\par \par \uc2 REP MIKE JOHNSON (REP) (LOUISIANA/SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE)\par \par \uc2 We will regroup and we will come up with another solution, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A looming shutdown comes as an estimated 40 million Americans are expected to fly this holiday season. Any extended shutdown the \uc2 TSA\uc2  administrator warns, could mean longer wait times at airports.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And with funding running out at Midnight tonight, millions of federal employees are wondering if they'll go without a pay check just before Christmas, including military families like Kayla Corbitt. She's an army spouse and runs an organization that helps military families find child care.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL WORKERS' PAYCHECKS IN JEOPARDY WITH SHUTDOWN LOOMING\par \par \uc2 KAYLA CORBITT (MILITARY SPOUSE/FOUNDER & CEO OPERATION CHILD CARE PROJECT)\par \par \uc2 Especially at the holidays, this is just not what our families want to be thinking about when they're already really struggling to get by.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's entirely unclear what happens next, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told me, he doesn't want to see anything passed that doesn't also raise that debt ceiling, the amount that the federal government can borrow. And as we saw last night, Rebecca, there simply aren't the Republican votes to do that, at least not now.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Jon, this intense focus on the debt ceiling is really about delaying or keeping from happening future battles.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Look, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  knows, and when I talked to him yesterday he reiterated this point. The debt ceiling, the government will hit that limit of how much money it can borrow early next year. That means the first part of his administration, his first 100 days, will be overshadowed by the possibility that the government would hit the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And as he told me, going past the debt ceiling could mean dire economic consequences. He said it could be like 1929 style depression. He doesn't want that to happen. He wants it off the table so he has a clear start to his presidency.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Jon, thank you. And the stock markets are certainly paying attention to that as well. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8 am. Holiday strikes. 11,000 workers at over 500 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores set to walk off the job. This as some Amazon workers strike in the heart of the holiday delivery rush. What it means for workers and customers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  AND AMAZON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Army of hope. Supermodel Petra Nemcova's powerful purpose, 20 years after surviving the devastating Indian ocean tsunami.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARMY OF HOPE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIANE SAWYER WITH PETRA NEMCOVA\par \par \uc2 PETRA NEMCOVA (SUPERMODEL & SURVIVOR OF INDIAN OCEAN TSUNAMI)\par \par \uc2 That pain, it's, it's with me so strongly every single day.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She sits down with our Diane Sawyer, talking about her mission to help victims of natural disasters after most of the world has moved on, including hundreds of families in North Carolina devastated by hurricane Helene. Her call to action this morning.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And everybody is waiting for the man with the cake. Cake boss Buddy Valastro is here. He brought cookies, too, and he's saying...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAKE BOSS BUDDY VALASTRO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWEETEST TIME OF THE YEAR\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It is great, always great to have Buddy Valastro here, especially when he brings cookies.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah, all right? He's gonna give us some advice to take some of the stress out of your holiday baking. And parents, go get your little ones. We got that big "Bluey" news we've told you about. The movie earlier this week, well, that was just the beginning.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 This is dance mode time for families. Everybody is very, very excited about "Bluey." Also ahead, our holiday parenting play book. This time of year, it can be tough on routines, so what do you need to do about nap time? We have pediatrician and parenting expert Dr. Mona Amin here with expert advice on that and more.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That is coming up.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck00061\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POP NEWS\b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 NEMCOVA, TSUNAMI, ALL HANDS AND HEARTS\par \par \uc2 "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 "MUFASA: THE LION KING", NORTH POLE EXPRESS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Lara, how about some pop news?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, let's do it, George. Good morning, everybody. We're going to begin this Friday pop with a feel good new song for you. This is an exclusive look at a new song from the movie "Mufasa: The Lion King," which opens today. This is written by the one and only Lin-Manuel Miranda, so you know it's going to be good. Check this out.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXCLUSIVE: "MUFASA: THE LION KING" CLIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FILM CLIP OF "MUFASA: THE LION KING"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "MUFASA: THE LION KING" IS PRODUCED BY A DIVISION OF \uc2 DISNEY\uc2 , ABC'S PARENT COMPANY\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is it wrong that I, like, think they're real? I just, I can't help it. They're so, it's just so lovely.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's such a nice love song.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, and that song is fabulous. It's called "Tell Me It's You," performed by Aaron Pierre and Tiffany Boone in their roles as Mufasa and Sarabi. Aaron was just here earlier this week. He said taking on the same role that was originated by the legendary James Earl Jones was a life-changing experience. And Lin-Manuel said this song is like a joy bomb. It was like a joy bomb to write and a joy bomb to hear. You can see an extended version of the, that clip from "Mufasa: The Lion King" on our website. You just scan that little QR code right there on your screen. "Mufasa: The Lion King" in theaters nationwide starting today.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, big day.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm going.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Big day.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, really excited to see the whole movie. All right, now all aboard for one special Pennsylvania train that's making express stops to the North Pole just in time, since we're just five days away from Christmas. Thank goodness Ike Ejiochi is there. He's in New Hope, Pennsylvania on Santa's North Pole Express with some festive guests. Ike, you look very festive yourself.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL ABOARD! PHILLY'S NORTH POLE EXPRESS DELIGHTS VISITORS\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, I have to dress the part, Lara. And I gotta say something. You can't have a North Pole Express without Santa and Mrs. Claus on board, as well as all these wonderful people. How are we doing, guys?\par \par \uc2 NORTH POLE EXPRESS (CROWD)\par \par \uc2 Woo.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There we go. Now get this, a train has been on this line since 1891. 133 years ago, it was used to transport goods and passengers all throughout Bucks County. And now the line has been transformed into this holiday attraction. Now, listen, this train this winter is being used as Pennsylvania's express train to the North Pole. And as you can see right now, it's been completely transformed with all the holiday decorations. Obviously, Mrs. Claus and Santa Claus here.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's a winter wonderland right outside in Bucks County. And, of course, all of these wonderful sweet treats and hot chocolate that we have for everybody on board. Now I want to say this. Michael, I know you've been a little upset, a little FOMO that you haven't been able to enjoy all of the sweet treats that I've been doing. So how about this? We brought some hot coffee and hot chocolate for all you guys back in the studio. All of us, cheers, Michael Strahan.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cheers.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cheers.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nice (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Merry Christmas, Ike.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Way to step it up and come through. We appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 CREW MEMBER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. So great.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck00068\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FAA IMPOSES DRONE BAN OVER PARTS OF NEW YORK & NEW JERSEY AIR SPACE SHUT DOWN\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Merry Christmas to all. Thank you, Ginger. Now the latest on the mystery drone sightings. The \uc2 FAA\uc2  is taking action. It imposed a ban on drones over parts of New York and New Jersey. And Erielle Reshef is here with the details. Good morning, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAA IMPOSES DRONE BAN OVER PARTS OF NEW YORK & NEW JERSEY\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to, Rebecca. After weeks of those reported sightings in the northeast, overnight the \uc2 FAA\uc2  taking the unprecedented move of shutting down air space to drones over parts of New York and New Jersey due to special security concerns. The ban is meant to police the skies above critical infrastructure. It will last through most of January.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Stretches of both states are now considered national defense air space. The drone ban over President-Elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's Bedminster Golf Club has also been extended through the end of January. Officials warn that flying a drone without government permission in these areas is illegal and authorities may use deadly force against any drones that pose an imminent security threat.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Anyone piloting a drone in the restricted area without permission could face federal charges. The \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  saying again it has assessed that there is no threat to public safety or national security. Officials say these bans are simply a precautionary measure. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRACKING WINTER STORM ON THE MOVE PRE-CHRISTMAS WIND CHILL\b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You heard it. I-95. We're going to turn to Ginger with the forecast and possibly a white Christmas for the I-95 corridor.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, it's like dumb and dumber, so you're saying there's a chance, you know.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're saying there's a chance.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's six days out. But, yes, there's a storm coming. It's just where that rain/snow line is going to set up. Which I will get to. But let's start with where we know there is snow this morning. Chicago, you've got the slick roads, you've got that little dusting of up to an inch or so. More in the suburbs. Vicksburg, Michigan, so in Kalamazoo County, the roads are covered.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so that little system is kind of going through the Great Lakes and now it's going to head to the northeast. You will get some lake effect snow bands in parts of Indiana, Ohio behind that. But look what happened, this is this afternoon, we're getting snow here this afternoon. It is going to be light but it will be impacting I-95.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRE-CHRISTMAS WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So if tonight were Christmas eve I'd say, yep, you're good to go. It's just not. So we're looking at the airports having some impact too. Upstate three to six inches. Then the serious cold come in, we're talking single digit temperatures for a lot of people, teens for Washington, DC. And then that next storm comes in and it looks like the rain/snow line is right along New York and such. So we'll keep an eye on it.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, all right. So it's not the most annoying.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Pretend tonight is Christmas.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STRIKING AMAZON WORKERS PICKET AS HOLIDAY NEARS\b0\par\par\uc2 475 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First we look at the top stories breaking at 8. We start with the two holiday strikes. Two of the best known companies in the country. Some workers are walking out of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  this morning. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers on the picket lines of some facilities as well. Want to go back to Trevor Ault with the latest on both. Good morning, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAST-MINUTE HOLIDAY DEALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRIKING AMAZON WORKERS PICKET AS HOLIDAY NEARS\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning again, George. So we're in the middle of kind of a tense moment here. We have the picketers, at least 50 delivery drivers, who are on strike with \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . And they're essentially negotiating with the \uc2 NYPD\uc2 . We've been watching some \uc2 Amazon\uc2  vehicles that have been coming and going. The \uc2 NYPD\uc2  is threatening to arrest them for disorderly conduct if they continue to block the pathway of some of those vans. So the picketers have been periodically pausing to let them through while still trying to slow those delivery vehicles down.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now a lot of these drivers have joined the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2 . They want to negotiate with \uc2 Amazon\uc2  for better wages, better working conditions. The issue is \uc2 Amazon\uc2  does not recognize the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  as a union that represents their employees, and they refuse to negotiate. Now \uc2 Amazon\uc2  also says the delivery schedule has not been disrupted and all their customers can still count on their packages to arrive on time.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So these picketers think they can cause major issues at a crucial time for deliveries. And as you mentioned, this is not the only strike from a gigantic company that is happening today. Unionized baristas, 11,000 of them, are prepared to go on strike later today, which will likely begin with a few selection of stores, and then it can grow on the coming days. But we are looking at two pretty significant movements from gigantic companies of workers gathering, unionizing together, to try to cause disruptions during the holiday stretch, guys.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep, significant move right around the holidays. Thank you so much for that, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck00062\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MORE BIG "BLUEY" NEWS!\b0\par\par\uc2 495 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 NEMCOVA, TSUNAMI, ALL HANDS AND HEARTS\par \par \uc2 "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...the latest "Bluey" news. Eva, you kept the second secret all week.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE BIG "BLUEY" NEWS!\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, they only told me just recently. I told you earlier this week there was big "Bluey" news, and now I finally know the new "Bluey" news. It's huge. That little Bluey on your screen is about to be your friend in real life too.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP OF "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("BLUEY")\par \par \uc2 For real life?\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Yes, for real life. Now you can meet Bluey in person. \uc2 Disney\uc2  announcing the Heeler family will make its real life debut at its US parks.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("BLUEY")\par \par \uc2 Ready?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "BLUEY" IS COMING TO \uc2 DISNEY\uc2  THEME PARKS & CRUISES\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The preschool show that follows the life and adventures of Bluey, her mom Chilly, her dad Bandit, and her little sister Bingo is a global sensation.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP OF "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("BLUEY")\par \par \uc2 Ooh.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It's been a big week for little Bluey.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP OF "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("BLUEY")\par \par \uc2 I'm ready for movies.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Disney\uc2  and the BBC announcing just days ago the first animated "Bluey" movie.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("BLUEY")\par \par \uc2 One popcorn, please.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("BLUEY")\par \par \uc2 Sure.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That's expected out in 2027.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("BLUEY")\par \par \uc2 Nice one, Bluey.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But you can meet and have fun with Bluey in person before that. Bluey and her sister Bingo will make their debut on \uc2 Disney\uc2  cruises out of Australia and New Zealand starting next month. As for how the Heeler family will appear at Disneyland and Disney World, that will be revealed soon.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP OF "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("BLUEY")\par \par \uc2 Whoa.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So much more to look forward to. And there is something truly magical when you get to watch your child meet their heroes. Ella got to meet them when they were here in studio. She is obsessed. She asks me at least once a week if she can go see Bluey. We call her big Bluey. And now I have to tell her, actually, yes. Guys?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's exciting.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) With a big smile for a Christmas present. Thank you, Eva.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck00067\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPIN