r \uc2 (OC) Yes, so 79 percent of Americans drink coffee. So this is a great one to give.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIXED ROAST COFFEE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMETEER $84\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) 100 percent of "GMA" staffers, I think, drink coffee. This is from the \uc2 Cometeer\uc2 . What's different about this is that you don't need to know what kind of machine your gift recipient has, what kind of coffee machine.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really?\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because what they do that's so brilliant is they brew the coffee fresh and then flash freeze it in these little pucks. So all you're gonna do is, you're gonna take it out, you're gonna pop it in. Here we go. Pop out. And then get some hot water.\par \par \uc2 CREW MEMBER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Whoa.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Your, pour it in. Michael, we made you a cup there.\par \par \uc2 CREW MEMBER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You can do this. You can make iced lattes. You can make just a regular cup of coffee and you just stir, stir, stir. This comes from all of the best breweries, coffee breweries around the country.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow that's good.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's really good, you guys.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, yeah.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It tastes really fresh. And all of these have, like, special deals. So you can get them in time. You want to order it today and save a little money and give a good gift.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Gary told me he stirred this with his finger. Thank you, Gary. I appreciate it. Thank you, bud. Lori, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROMOTIONAL CONSIDERATION PROVIDED BY\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you. Happy holidays, my friend.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Happy holidays, my dear. And coming up, you know the wait for "Squid Games" season 2 is almost over. We sit down with the show's stars and creator when we come back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0006a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CEO MURDER SUSPECT RETURNS TO NYC, FACES FEDERAL CHARGES SUSPECT APPEARS IN COURT\b0\par\par\uc2 957 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right now to the man accused of murdering the United Healthcare CEO. He arrived back in New York and now faces federal charges that could lead to the death penalty. Dan Abrams is standing by. First senior investigative correspondent Aaron Katersky here with the latest. Good morning, Aaron.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CEO MURDER SUSPECT RETURNS TO NYC, FACES FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Luigi Mangione is waking up this morning in federal custody, actually at the same jail housing Sean Combs. It was his last stop after a day of court appearances, aircraft rides, and a long perp walk under heavy guard.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It was a whirlwind day for the accused killer Luigi Mangione starting in Pennsylvania, where police loaded him into a van and drove him to the airport for a flight to New York. A helicopter delivered Mangione to Manhattan, shackled and surrounded by an entourage of officers. New York Mayor Eric Adams there waiting.\par \par \uc2 MAYOR ERIC ADAMS (DEM)\par \par \uc2 This act of terrorism and the violence that stems from it is something that will not be tolerated in the city.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Mangione appeared in Manhattan federal court where prosecutors charged him with stalking and murdering United Healthcare Chief \uc2 Brian Thompson\uc2 . If convicted as charges, Mangione would be eligible for the death penalty.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FRIEDMAN AGNIFILO (DEFENSE ATTORNEY FOR LUIGI MANGIONE)\par \par \uc2 We're going to respectfully decline to make any comment at this time. Mr. Mangione appreciates everyone's support.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Outside courts in New York and Pennsylvania, small groups of people carried signs of support for the suspect. But to prosecutors what Mangione allegedly did was an act of terrorism.\par \par \uc2 PROSECUTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 It was targeted, premeditated and meant to sow terror.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Prosecutors said Mangione's hand written notes express hostility towards the health insurance industry and wealthy executives in particular. In one passage Mangione allegedly wrote, "The details are finally coming together. The target is insurance because it checks every box." Prosecutors said "The notebook describes an intent to whack the CEO of one of the insurance companies at its investor conference."\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The criminal complaint includes images of the suspect traveling to and from the scene of the crime. One walking while wearing a gray backpack, another riding a bike toward the \uc2 Hilton Hotel\uc2 . Despite the evidence, Mangione supporters are not wavering.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And in court, Mangione answered yes to a few questions. Otherwise he appeared rather subdued. We saw him in civilian clothes. A federal marshal carried a brown paper bag containing his orange jumpsuit. Mangione faces charges in state and federal courts. His attorney called that very confusing, highly unusual and, George, signaled Mangione will fight every charge he faces.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Aaron, thanks very much. Let's bring in our chief legal analyst Dan Abrams. Dan, several experts have raised questions about this terror charge.\par \par \uc2 DAN ABRAMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, so this is a way to get first degree murder in New York state. Typically in New York State, if you murder someone, you'd be charged with second degree murder. Here they're trying to elevate it to first degree murder.\par \par \uc2 DAN ABRAMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There wasn't a killing of a police officer, which would typically be the kind of first degree murder charge. But if it's also in connection with an act of terror, you can charge a first degree murder. The challenge is going to be being able to prove that that was the motivation.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So is that where the writings come in?\par \par \uc2 DAN ABRAMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. And so they'll use the writings that he did. But the question becomes, was he trying to coerce the civilian population into fear? Or was he doing it to punish United Healthcare and the insurance companies? And that actually may end up becoming one of the legal issues that's argued in this case. What exactly was he doing it for?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How about his lawyer's point, that this combination of federal and state charges is unusual.\par \par \uc2 DAN ABRAMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well what's unusual here is that it almost seems like there's a competition between the feds and the state prosecutors here as to who's going to get to try him first. And typically you have much more coordination between the two, where it's clear, okay, the feds are going to go first or the state's gonna go first. Here it almost feels like there's a race to who's gonna be able to get him to trial first as to who's gonna get the first shot at him.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Who wins the race?\par \par \uc2 DAN ABRAMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whoever gets to trial first. Really. And typically - federal courts move faster than state courts. So if you're asking me to bet, I would bet on the federal case moving faster, but we'll see.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dan Abrams, thanks very much. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PLAY OF THE DAY\b0\par\par\uc2 616 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're back with our "Play of the Day." Kylie Kelce coming to the rescue of some young Eagle fans in Philadelphia. Lara back with the story.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Kelce family at it again, everybody. Yeah. So if it's always sunny in Philadelphia, then some of that sun comes straight from the Kelce family. They're at it again, this time because a local high school English teacher named Bonnie Giberson realized that many her students couldn't afford to pay for a planned field trip to Eagles stadium.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So she posted a cry for help on TikTok, and that's when Kylie came to the rescue, calling the school herself and paying the cost of the bus, even arranging so that everything else on the field trip would be covered for every single kid. Here's Bonnie and her excited students on the way to Lincoln Financial Field where they were given the royal treatment, including walking through the stadium tunnel into the press room.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A big highlight was visiting the locker room where they met Eagles defensive man - Brandon Graham. He was more than happy to chat with the kids, sign autographs. What a good guy. They even got to walk onto the field, see their school name, Penn Treaty, up on the big screen. Here's Bonnie, guys, on her students' reactions.\par \par \uc2 BONNIE GIBERSON (TEACHER)\par \par \uc2 They were all smiles. There were lots of like oohs and aahhs, especially going out on the field, meeting B.G. And then on our way out, you know, I got like a couple hugs, I got like thank you, best trip ever. Which is just an amazing feeling. So I would just say to Kylie, that you really have made this, like, a week and a year to remember.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I mean, that's a big deal. They will not forget that. Giberson says many of those students will be graduating, so this was a chance to share some priceless memories together during their senior year. Thank you, Kylie.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, what a great story.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, the only thing that went through my head too when I watched that, an incredible story, that she has created...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Don't say anything about the Eagles.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, she created more Eagles fans.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I knew it was coming, America.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Kylie, come on.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Lara, you're just channeling them in green this morning too.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I am.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, excuse moi.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Fly Eagle fly. And, Lara, you're coming back with more later?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, of course.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We can't wait. Shopping, last minute deals and, of course, "Pop News" as well. More Lara, more "GMA" when we come back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 7:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Ready?\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Ladies and gentlemen, I'm doing this for my kids.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA." Parents and kids are in dance mode this morning with brand new big "Bluey" news. That is coming up in our next hour. We are very excited for it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We are. We're also following a lot of headlines right now including delivery drivers at Amazon who are on strike with less than a week to go before Christmas and Hanukkah. It's organized by the teamsters union. Workers are picketing outside seven facilities.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE SALMONELLA CASES FROM CUCUMBERS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, 32 more cases of salmonella related to tainted cucumbers have been reported. That brings the total to a hundred, including 25 people who were hospitalized. Several companies have recalled whole and sliced cucumbers provided by a grower in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAR SEAT RECALL\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also right now more than 608,000 child seats are being recalled over fears debris could enter the front harness adjuster and cause it to fail. The affected products are Nuna Baby Essentials Rava child seats, manufactured between July 2016 and October 2023. Nuna says they'll provide owners with a remedy kit free of charge.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE FOOTBALL PLAYOFFS KICKS OFF\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the first ever 12 team college football playoff kicks off tonight. Number seven Notre Dame hosts number 10 Indiana in-state showdown. It's the first of four big games this weekend. And you can see it right here on ABC at 8:00 PM Eastern.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hoosiers.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hoosier. Let's go. All right. And we got a lot more ahead including the spinal cord injury game changer. Will Reeve is gonna tell us about that, that is coming up later in the show. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BEST LAST MINUTE DEALS FOR GIFTS CHRISTMAS COUNTDOWN\b0\par\par\uc2 770 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And with just five days left to shop before Christmas and Hanukkah, if you're worried about potential delays, Lara has a look at some of the best last minute deals if you want to shop in person.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEST LAST-MINUTE DEALS FOR GIFTS\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. Exactly. So, guys, if you are still looking for gifts, there are still some great deals out there. \uc2 Walmart\uc2  has deep discounts on hundreds of items like the Nutribullet Blender combo for $49. That is almost 60 percent off the regular price of 119. That's a great gift. And then for the kiddos, Target is offering up 40 percent off select Squishmallows. Is it Squishmallows?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAST MINUTE DEALS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Squishmallows.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And those, I hear from Kelly Hagan, the producer, are very popular with the kiddos.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have a big orange one at home. Yes. They're very popular.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so that's, you guys, there you go. Just letting you know. If you spend $40 on beauty and health, Target Circle members will get a $10 gift card. That's a nice little stocking stuffer. And then over at \uc2 Home Depot\uc2 , you can save up to 35 percent on appliances like the four, this GE four burner electric range. Now $598, down from $899. But, I'm being serious, you do not want to put off your shopping any longer.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have been telling you, and now we really mean it. Many stores, including \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , Target, \uc2 Home Depot\uc2 , and Lowe's will be closed. Did you hear me? They will be closed on Christmas Day. Some will close earlier than usual on Christmas Eve. \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , for example, shutting its doors at 6 pm across the nation on Christmas Eve. That is five hours earlier than its typical 11:00 pm close. I'm gonna give you another option for getting your gifts in time because I really want to try to help you.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Please.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Including buying online and picking up in store. In fact, you can order online, pick up same day in Target stores through 6:00 pm on Christmas Eve if you really want to push it.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those are all great deals. And if you really want to push it, say honey, I bought you a range for Christmas.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good move. Wonder how that would work out.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nothing says I love you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I got a great deal.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Let me know how that works out for you.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's a great gift. Come on.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up in our "GMA" morning menu, supermodel Petra Nemcova's mission working to help other victims of natural disasters. Well, she sat down with Diane Sawyer.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PETRA NEMCOVA'S MISSION\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, our holiday parenting playbook. How to manage screen time with the kids who are home from school.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY PARENTING PLAYBOOK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're back in Philadelphia this morning. Ike is taking us aboard this federal holiday train transporting passengers to a winter holiday wonderland.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PHILLY'S NORTH POLE EXPRESS\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus gifts and sweets. What more could you ask for around the holidays? Lori B has got the right stuff, baby. She's got our gift guide. Buddy Valastro is also here helping us out with our holiday baking. He's solving some of the most common problems in the kitchen. All of that coming up on "Good Morning America." Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY BAKING TIPS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck00063\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AIRPORT PARKING HACKS FOR THE HOLIDAYS HOW TO SAVE TIME & REDUCE STRESS WHEN PARKING AT THE AIRPORT\b0\par\par\uc2 661 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now on "GMA" helping you with the big holiday rush. Finding airport parking that's easy, affordable and safe can be a serious challenge this time of year. But Eva Pilgrim has some simple strategies and reminders. And, Eva, it's great to see you. Around this time, at Thanksgiving, people were talking about all these car thefts at airports. Where does all of this stand?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: :AIRPORT PARKING HACKS FOR THE HOLIDAYS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, yeah. In the rush to make your flight, you now also need to think about making sure that your car is safe. Some things to keep in mind. First, lighting. Check to see if the lot or garage has good lightning. We always say this, but make sure you put your valuables away, your windows are up, doors locked.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If you can park close to a booth or an elevator that's also a good tip. And find out if the location has 24/7 security. That could make a really big difference this time of tear.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, but definitely it's busy. So how do you ensure you get a parking spot?\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it's really busy. First, you have to decide what's most important to you, parking at the airport or saving money. If you're willing to park off site there are websites that offer cheaper parking near many airports, like spotheroway.com and globalairportparking.com.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Pro tip, hotels. You can park in some of their lots even if you aren't staying there and take their shuttle. Call the hotel yourself. You can get the best rate directly from them.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's a good point there. But what about parking at the airport?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO SAVE TIME & REDUCE STRESS WHEN PARKING AT THE AIRPORT\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. So if you really want to park at the airport, there are some ways to ensure you get a spot. No, there's just fewer spots, right, because there's so many people. First, book ahead. A lot of airports are now allowing you to reserve a parking spot. Philadelphia International, get this, is now offering valet parking if you book in advance, it's $50 a day. $60 if you pull up day of.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And they monitor your return flight and have your car waiting for you at the baggage claim when you get back. Wherever you park, don't forget to search for promo codes, because you know we like a discount.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Waiting at baggage claim.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Waiting at baggage claim, it's a new service they're offering at PHL.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIG "BLUEY" NEWS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow. I had no idea. Eva, thank you. And you're not going anywhere, Eva's coming back, because we got that big "Bluey" news she couldn't share the other day. Well, she's sharing it today.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And next, we have our "Play of the Day" on this Friday morning on "GMA." We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SHOP THIS BOOK BESTSELLING AUTHOR JENNIFER LYNN BARNES TALKS NEW BOOK\b0\par\par\uc2 908 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 NEMCOVA, TSUNAMI, ALL HANDS AND HEARTS\par \par \uc2 "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 "MUFASA: THE LION KING", NORTH POLE EXPRESS\par \par \uc2 GIFTS\par \par \uc2 "SQUID GAME", SEASON 2\par \par \uc2 "THE GRANDEST GAME", BARNES\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm here now with Jennifer Lynn Barnes, the number one "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " bestselling author behind the "Inheritance Scheme" series. It sold over 4 million copies. Her latest novel, "The Grandest Game" is our "GMA" YA book club pick for December. Thanks for coming in.\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LYNN BARNES (AUTHOR OF "INHERITANCE SCHOLE")\par \par \uc2 Oh, I am so happy to be here. Thank you for having me.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOP THIS BOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BESTSELLING AUTHOR JENNIFER LYNN BARNES TALKS NEW BOOK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It's great to have you. Tell us about "The Grandest Game."\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LYNN BARNES (AUTHOR OF "INHERITANCE SCHOLE")\par \par \uc2 So "The Grandest Game" is about a teenage heiress who holds a yearly competition full of puzzles, and riddles, and codes where the players have the chance to win a multi-million dollar prize. So this year seven players are whisked away to a private island for the game of a lifetime. The book is basically like an escape room in book form.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow. And it's different from what you've written before.\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LYNN BARNES (AUTHOR OF "INHERITANCE SCHOLE")\par \par \uc2 It is different in some ways. I think, for me, the most different thing about the writing process was just how explicitly I wrote this book to be an escape for me and for readers. So, yes, it's full of the puzzles, and the riddles, and the codes, but you've also got an elaborate mansion on this private island, cliff side encounters, the ocean at night time. You know, a masquerade ball, romantic tension between these rivals for the prize. And it was just so much fun to write.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you experience the escape when you're writing it?\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LYNN BARNES (AUTHOR OF "INHERITANCE SCHOLE")\par \par \uc2 I do. I, you know, I'm a mom to three small children, and so my normal life is nothing like the life in the book, so it's nice to be able to escape into it.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's great. Let's, let's get some questions for your fans. First person wants to know, who has been your favorite POV character to write in "The Grandest Game?"\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LYNN BARNES (AUTHOR OF "INHERITANCE SCHOLE")\par \par \uc2 So, in "The Grandest Game," my favorite point of view character is Gigi. She is my sunshine character who's kind of just this random ball of big-hearted chaos. And I think the reason she's my favorite character to write is, one, she's very funny and fun. But also she's a character that other people tend to underestimate. And I always love writing characters, particularly female characters, where being underestimated is almost their super power.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's terrific. Next person wants to know how many journals you went through when making this series.\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LYNN BARNES (AUTHOR OF "INHERITANCE SCHOLE")\par \par \uc2 I would say, for the entire series, at least 25. I am never happier as a writer than when I am brainstorming and just kind of floating in a sea of possibilities, saying, what about this? What if this? What if this?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So do you get that all done before you sit down and write?\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LYNN BARNES (AUTHOR OF "INHERITANCE SCHOLE")\par \par \uc2 Yes. So I don't sit down with an outline, but I sit down with probably 1 1/2 full journals where I've just brainstormed all of these possibilities, lived in the what if, gotten to know the characters. And so by the time I start, I have a pretty good idea of things that might not even appear on the page and I've just gotten myself really excited about the book.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What are you excited about next?\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LYNN BARNES (AUTHOR OF "INHERITANCE SCHOLE")\par \par \uc2 Well, right now I am putting the finishing polishes on "Glorious Rivals," which is the sequel to "Grandest Game." And kind of my rule of thumb as a series writer is that with each book, the world gets bigger, the stakes get higher, and the relationships get more complicated. So that's been really fun.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cannot wait to see it. Thank you. "Grandest Game" is available now. You can shop this book by scanning the QR code right there on your screen. And coming up, cake boss Buddy Valastro here to help take the stress out of your holiday baking. That was great. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LYNN BARNES (AUTHOR OF "INHERITANCE SCHOLE")\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0006d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SPECIAL DELIVERY FOR FAMILIES HIT HARD BY HELENE\b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Ian, thank you so much for that. We're gonna turn now to the families that are still recovering from hurricane Helene in western North Carolina. Well this morning they're getting a helping hand. And Lara is here with what that is. Good morning, Lara.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPECIAL DELIVERY FOR FAMILIES HIT HARD BY HELENE\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, happy to bring this story. Good morning to you and to you all. Hurricane Helene hit western North Carolina in September and the area is still recovering from the widespread damage. Now as we head into the holidays, Lowe's has stepped in to provide some relief to those who are still rebuilding there.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The home improvement company partnering with local builders to help make the holidays a little brighter, delivering tiny homes ahead of Christmas. And it was a special delivery, NASCAR haulers, guys, taking those homes to their new owners. A real team effort here.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Home Builders Association of Greater Charlotte, Habitat for Humanity and Advanced Roofing and Exteriors, have all been working together build the homes over the last week, with more set to be delivered today. The goal being to donate 100 tiny homes to western North Carolina. And these homes make a huge impact in a community that still needs so much help, guys.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is great.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DEVELOPMENTS IN CEO MURDER CASE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Great story. Thank you, Lara. Coming up, the new developments in the United Healthcare CEO shooting. The suspect now faces federal charges that could lead to the death penalty. Aaron Katersky is gonna break it down.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPINAL CORD INJURY BREAKTHROUGH\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus the newly cleared device giving new hope to Americans with spinal cord injuries. Will Reeve is here to tell us all about the game changer. Hey, Will.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael. This new device has the power to change daily life for people with spinal cord injuries. And coming up, you'll learn what it does and meet this woman whose story will inspire and move you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIRPORT PARKING HACKS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just remarkable, Will. Also ahead, what you can do before you take off and even before you get to the airport to make traveling easier. But first back over to you, Ging.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 NEMCOVA, TSUNAMI, ALL HANDS AND HEARTS\par \par \uc2 "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 "MUFASA: THE LION KING", NORTH POLE EXPRESS\par \par \uc2 GIFTS\par \par \uc2 "SQUID GAME", SEASON 2\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're gonna go to Ginger.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, and it's perfect binging weather, at least for the cold weekend in a lot of places. But Chicago O'Hare Airport just came in with delays already because they've had this burst of snow. 2.1 inches already. Some of the suburbs like Naperville, closer to four, but the city around one. You know where you don't see it? Where the record highs are falling. Phoenix, Tucson again today will go for records. And look, even into Olympia, Washington in the mid-50s. That warmth is going to slide east. You're going Christmas, to almost the new year, and much above normal right in the middle of the country. But really, everybody is warm. Let's get a check now a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0006c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW HOPE FOR PATIENTS WITH SPINAL CORD INJURIES FDA CLEARS GAME CHANGING NEW SPINAL CORD INJURY DEVICE\b0\par\par\uc2 887 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, George. Now a new device just cleared by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  that could be a game changer for the roughly 300,000 Americans will spinal cord injuries. Will Reeve sat down with one of the first patients to use this new spinal stimulation technology and he's here with more. And, Will, good morning to you. I know this story is near and dear to your heart, my friend.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS NEW HOPE FOR PATIENTS WITH SPINAL CORD INJURIES\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is, Michael, yeah. It means a lot to me personally as the son of a man with a spinal cord injury. And I know that being able to regain any movement is a massive development for a person with a spinal cord injury. And that's what this device showed it can do.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It brings back certain mobility and with it a new level of freedom and hope. And in one terrible moment, the woman you are about to meet lost her parents, her ability to move and she thought her future. But now the future is here.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning a breakthrough for people living with spinal cord injuries.\par \par \uc2 JESSIE OWENS (THERAPY STUDY PARTICIPANT ARC-EX THERAPY)\par \par \uc2 This is one of the most meaningful steps I can think of for the spinal cord injury community, and it works. And it gives us hope.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Based on the results of a pivotal trial published in "Nature Medicine," the \uc2 FDA\uc2  announcing it has cleared a spinal cord stimulation technology from Swiss company Onward. The device called, ARC EX, helps paralyzed people regain some mobility in their arms, hands and fingers, and freedom. Freedom to go from this to this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA CLEARS GAME CHANGING NEW SPINAL CORD INJURY DEVICE\par \par \uc2 CHET MORITZ PHD (PROFESSOR DEPT REHABILITATION MED UNIV OF WASHINGTON)\par \par \uc2 Oh, yeah. That's crazy. So ARC EX is simply electrodes attached to the skin on the back of the neck. It runs all the time, and it makes it easier for people to move. We found that the majority of participants improved strength, sensation and hand function to a significant degree.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jessie Owen was paralyzed 12 years ago when a tree fell and crushed the car she was riding in with her parents. ARC EX now offering her life changing possibilities.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What can you do now that you couldn't do prior to this?\par \par \uc2 JESSIE OWENS (THERAPY STUDY PARTICIPANT ARC-EX THERAPY)\par \par \uc2 I can paint with my hands now. I can open a jar of peanut butter. I can feed my kids because the amount of function I have in my hands changed. It wasn't, you know, perfection, but it was enough to make meaning in my life.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What hope does this device provide to you?\par \par \uc2 JESSIE OWENS (THERAPY STUDY PARTICIPANT ARC-EX THERAPY)\par \par \uc2 The future of spinal cord injury treatment is being written right now. This is the moment. And this provides the hope and the stepping stone to start that journey.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And full disclosure. I am a board member of the \uc2 Christopher and Dana Reeve Foundation\uc2  which has partnered with Onward, the makers of this device. The ARC EX will be available in some rehab clinics early next year and they'll continue ramp up production to get it out further.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And in mid-2025 Onward hopes for \uc2 FDA\uc2  clearance to get this into people's homes. And, guys, progress in spinal cord injury research is usually measured in decades. So this is a long time coming. And to be to say this is here and it's getting out to people who need it is a big moment.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There have been a lot of advances lately.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, the technology is really accelerating everything, most of all hope.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're happy to see that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIRPORT PARKING HACKS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such a hopeful message. Thank you for bringing it to us, Will. We really appreciate. Coming up, getting to the airport is stressful enough as it is, but Eva Pilgrim has strategies and safety tips. Hey, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, yeah, Rebecca. Adding parking to the mix only adds to the pressure. So let's take the turbulence out of the experience with the secret at some hotels, and one airport that will have your car waiting for you when you get home. That's just ahead here on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STRESS-FREE HOLIDAY BAKING WITH BUDDY VALASTRO JOLLY HOLIDAY COUNTDOWN\b0\par\par\uc2 1,693 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, LOWE'S, FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 NEMCOVA, TSUNAMI, ALL HANDS AND HEARTS\par \par \uc2 "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 "MUFASA: THE LION KING", NORTH POLE EXPRESS\par \par \uc2 GIFTS\par \par \uc2 "SQUID GAME", SEASON 2\par \par \uc2 "THE GRANDEST GAME", BARNES\par \par \uc2 VALASTRO, "BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE"\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, I can see the sign out there for our next guest because he has a store right next door. Back now with our Jolly Holiday Countdown, the holiday baking season is in full swing, and there are bound to be problems, of course. So we brought in one of the best bakers that we know, Buddy Valastro, the host of "Buddy's Holiday Recipe Rumble," and this morning he's answering your last minute baking questions. You know, where else would I have a stress free holiday? And welcome to the show, by the way. Got a stress free holiday, but baking mistakes happen. I'm sure people hit you up about this all the time. What are the two biggest ones you always hear about and how can you avoid the mistakes?\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 All right, so, great question. Baking is a science. When you get a chef, they can put a little bit more salt, a little bit more pepper. But when you bake, you have to measure. If it says one egg, you can't add two. You gotta weight it. It's a science. You gotta be precise. Sometimes, like, you have a batter here that's a little bit thicker. Okay. Now, not always, but you can add just a little bit of milk, okay, and try to loosen it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIGGEST BAKING MISTAKES: MISREADING MEASUREMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BAKING IS A SCIENCE, ACCURACY IS KEY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, let it loosen up a little bit.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIGGEST BAKING MISTAKES: OVERMIXING BATTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRY ADDING MILK OR EXTRA EGG YOLK TO BALANCE IT OUT\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Or maybe an egg yolk.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, it's already working.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Or if it's too loose, maybe a little flour.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, okay.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 So everything comes down to that.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. I like that. Okay.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 All right. That's a pretty easy tip. Baking, measure and what always?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Baking, measure, and weigh. You gotta be precise when you come to baking.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 It's a science.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, so we, you know, we have viewers who sent in their dilemmas, their questions. Our first one is from Laura. So let's check it out.\par \par \uc2 LAURA (HAS BAKING QUESTION)\par \par \uc2 Hi, Buddy. What can you do if your cake cracks or breaks when you take it out of the pan? Do you have to start over?\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Well, I get that a lot, okay? My kids are usually the ones that want to dump the cake too hot and then it'll break.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUDDY'S BAKING TIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IF YOUR CAKE CRACKS OR BREAKS, USE FROSTING & SPRINKLES TO COVER UP IMPERFECTIONS\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Like we got here. But this is what we're gonna do. We're gonna take a little bit of butter cream. We're gonna kind of squeeze it inside. Okay? We're gonna squeeze that together. We're gonna go like this, all right. Little bada bing bada boom. Go a little like this, Michael, spin this around, you know?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep, smooth it out.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 And then, and go back and forth with the knife. And then what I always say...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow. Sprinkle.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 ...This is nature's cover up. Sprinkles. All right? If you're a bad baker and you make a mistake, cover it in sprinkles. It's gonna look good.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, there is, there, there is no starting over.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 That's it. Okay. Next question.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, so next question is from (PH) Kamela. Kamela, what you got?\par \par \uc2 KAMELA (HAS BAKING QUESTION)\par \par \uc2 Hi, buddy. I have a baking dilemma. What if you run out of frosting and icing for your cake and the ingredients to make more. Thanks.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Okay, if you don't have enough items, always, maybe a little heavy cream, you can turn into some whipped cream. If you have a little Nutella in the pantry, if you have a little bit of chocolate syrup. So this is just a little bit of whipped cream that I whipped up. Okay? Take that. We'll go like that, like, this, Michael. Like this. You know.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IF YOU RUN OUT OF FROSTING USE WHIPPED CREAM, NUTELLA OR POWDERED SUGAR\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Lara is over there amazed. I'm amazed too, I ain't gonna lie to you, Buddy.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 All right, and then we'll just hit it with a little bit of chocolate sauce here.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nice. Wow.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, our staff is excited because they know they get to eat this when we're done with this segment.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. We are waiting.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Quick and easy.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Not bad. Not bad. Okay.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, now we got, we have Helene. Helene.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 All right, Helene. Let's do it.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What do we got?\par \par \uc2 HELENE (HAS BAKING QUESTION)\par \par \uc2 Hi, Buddy. Help. My cookies are dark on the bottom and not cooked in the middle. What am I doing wrong? Any way to keep them and not throw them out?\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Okay, so that's a cardinal sin. When baking chocolate chips, always middle rack, bake them a little bit lower, and take them out. They're gonna look raw because they're gonna still continue to cook on the pan. But, like, let's take this pie here. You have a pie here that you burnt. Okay?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IF COOKIES BURN ON THE EDGES, OVEN TEMP MAY BE UNEVEN OR BAKING SHEET IS OVERCROWDED\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 I try to scoop out the filling in the middle. And then we'll make it into, like, a parfait. Okay? You try to, like, don't use burntest parts or the same thing with the cookie, right?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 So we'll take off the edges. This guy went maybe a little too much, do you know what I'm saying, Michael?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRIM OFF BURNT EDGES & PAIR COOKIES WITH ICE CREAM OR COFFEE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 But, you know, and then you just kind of, like, crumble it in. And bada bing bada boom, you got a parfait.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We got it. We're done. (inaudible) real quick, we only have a few seconds, but there, is there, some people who don't have time to bake at home, but you have some things to help them.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. So we have these new DIY kits that is a reindeer and a snow man. You get the cake base, the (PH) fonda, and the video instruction on how to turn a regular cake into that. So if you go to Carlos Bakery, check it out. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Carlos Bakery.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Dot\uc2  com.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dot com and check it out. Buddy, you're the best, man.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 Oh, we love you guys.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you can see "Buddy's Holiday Recipe Rumble," that's his show, it's streaming now.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 On Hulu.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) On Hulu, that's right.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 That's it.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You guys stay there. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 BUDDY VALASTRO ("BUDDY'S HOLIDAY RECIPE RUMBLE")\par \par \uc2 You got it.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Enjoy.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm eating.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hi, Buddy.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is so good.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Run on in here. There we go.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Get in here. Get in here.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Lara makes it just in time.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I can't really run.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you all for watching.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. Have a great weekend, everybody.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Delicious.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, everybody.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bye.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0006e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "SQUID GAME" CAST & CREATOR TALK SEASON 2\b0\par\par\uc2 1,179 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 NEMCOVA, TSUNAMI, ALL HANDS AND HEARTS\par \par \uc2 "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 "MUFASA: THE LION KING", NORTH POLE EXPRESS\par \par \uc2 GIFTS\par \par \uc2 "SQUID GAME", SEASON 2\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "GMA." The wait is finally almost over. Finally and almost. It's been more than three years since "Squid Game" premiered. Now season 2 is set to arrive for the holidays. Juju sat down with the cast and the creator. A lot of people jealous of this assignment.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. This trio, they are a dazzling set of creatives. They absolutely are. And, you know, "Squid Game" became the most watched \uc2 Netflix\uc2  series in 94 countries. It is an absolute juggernaut that defies description. It's artistic, it's sadistic, it's a super dark, and I mean super dark social commentary, and yet you're standing up rooting for the good guys. And guess what, season 2, guys, guys, buckle up.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP OF "SQUID GAME"\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's back. After an agonizing three year wait, "Squid Game" is returning with a vengeance. A lot has changed since the Korean language thriller became a worldwide phenomenon. \uc2 Netflix\uc2 's most popular show of all time, spawning a reality competition and a traveling popup experience where fans can come try their luck at games inspired by the show.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Does it surprise you that there's a reality show and that people want to come and play these games?\par \par \uc2 HWANG DONG-HYUK (CREATOR & DIRECTOR OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 (speaks foreign language)\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNLIKE THE ACTUAL SQUID GAME UNIVERSE, AT LEAST IF YOU LOSE HERE, YOU WON'T DIE. SO MAYBE THAT'S WHY \u8211\'20\'13 PEOPLE CAN COME WITH A LIGHT HEART AND ENJOY THESE GAMES.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The show's creator and stars sworn to secrecy. But what we do know is season 2 picks up with our hero, Gi-hun, played by Lee Jung-jae. Now a multi-million dollar winner, obsessed with stopping the games.\par \par \uc2 LEE JUNG-JAE (PLAYER 456 OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 (speaks foreign language)\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HE COULDN'T SIMPLY PRETEND NOT TO SEE THESE ATROCIOUS THINGS HAPPENING TO PEOPLE... THAT'S WHY IN SEASON 2, HE'S GOT THIS FIRM DETERMINATION TO STOP THE GAME AND PUT THE PEOPLE BEHIND THE GAME TO JUSTICE. THAT'S WHERE HIS REVENGE BEGINS\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're the ultimate good guy.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP OF "SQUID GAME"\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) His nemesis, the mysterious front man, played by action star Lee Byung-hun, who shocked Korean audiences when his face was revealed beneath the mask in season one.\par \par \uc2 LEE BYUNG-HUN ("FRONT MAN" OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 You will see his back stories and even, you can see his real character. You will know everything about front man.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The brutally violent show comes from the mind of director Hwang Dong-hyuk, who famously toiled for more than a decade before \uc2 Netflix\uc2  bought his idea.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we spoke last time, you told me that you lost a half dozen teeth. Did you pay with your body in a similar way in season two?\par \par \uc2 HWANG DONG-HYUK (CREATOR & DIRECTOR OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 I think I lost, like, at least a few years of my life expectancy.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Playing an evil character, what is that like as an actress to portray that?\par \par \uc2 LEE BYUNG-HUN ("FRONT MAN" OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 (Speaks foreign language)\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: I HAD SO MANY QUESTIONS IN MY MIND THAT THE DIRECTOR HAS OFTEN SAID THAT HE NOW HAS TWO TOOTHACHES AND I BELIEVE ONE OF THEM IS BECAUSE OF ME AND ALL MY QUESTIONS I BOMBARDED HIM WITH AS I WAS ACTING.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The pain may have been worth it. Season 2 already nominated for a Golden Globe award.\par \par \uc2 LEE JUNG-JAE (PLAYER 456 OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 (Speaks foreign language)\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WE AS ACTORS TALK AMONGST OURSELVES, LIKE, WHAT KIND OF CHOICE WE WOULD MAKE IF WE WERE IN THAT SITUATION.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This season features chilling new games and a new cast of doomed contestants meant to reflect real world conflict and current events.\par \par \uc2 HWANG DONG-HYUK (CREATOR & DIRECTOR OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 (speaks foreign language)\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE ELEMENT OF THE O-X VOTE AFTER EACH ROUND THAT YOU SEE IN THE SECOND SEASON, HOW DEPENDING ON THAT PATCH, PEOPLE DIVIDE AMONGST ONE ANOTHER, BECOME EXTREMELY HOSTILE AGAINST ONE ANOTHER. ALL OF THESE THINGS, WE HAVE ALREADY SEEN HAPPEN IN SO MANY PLACES AROUND THE WORLD AND WE WILL CONTINUE TO SEE IT HAPPEN.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's next for you? Please tell me romantic comedy?\par \par \uc2 HWANG DONG-HYUK (CREATOR & DIRECTOR OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 Not really. My next one is actually more darker.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What?\par \par \uc2 HWANG DONG-HYUK (CREATOR & DIRECTOR OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 More crude and more violence.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You can't get more cruel or violent. That's impossible.\par \par \uc2 HWANG DONG-HYUK (CREATOR & DIRECTOR OF "SQUID GAME")\par \par \uc2 It will be the darkest one of my, all work.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (speaks foreign language))\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNBELIEVABLE, REALLY? WHAT TO DO!\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh my goodness.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Seriously, right? Honest, honestly, people don't just like "Squid Game" though, they're obsessed with it. And, remember, it's based on director Hwang's own down and out struggles when he was living with his mom and in debt.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yet it feels like an art house film when you're watching, and yet there's nothing like watching desperate people making moral, life and death decisions that, you know, makes the hair on the back of your head stand up.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and your teeth fall out, apparently.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, exactly. It really makes you think though. But you know what, guys? Season 2 of "Squid Game" begins streaming next week, December 26th.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Depending on where my kids will be.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, that's gonna be good.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Let the binging begin.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I'm in.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thanks, Juj.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0006b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMAZON, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  WORKERS STRIKE AHEAD OF THE HOLIDAYS STRIKING AMAZON WORKERS PICKET AHEAD OF THE HOLIDAYS\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First the two holiday strikes at two of the best known companies in the country. Some workers are walking out of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  this morning. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers are on the picket lines at some facilities as well. We're covering both. Trevor Ault starts us off from one of the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facilities here in New York. Good morning, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  WORKERS STRIKE AHEAD OF THE HOLIDAYS\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, George. So there are already picketers back out here this morning here in Queens. This is one of several strike sites outside \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facilities all across the country. Now, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  insists their delivery schedule has not been disrupted, but these demonstrators believe they can cause issues at a critical time for package delivery and force \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to the negotiating table.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRIKING AMAZON WORKERS PICKET AS HOLIDAY NEAR\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Hey hey ho ho corporate greed has got to go.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, delivery drivers for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  on strike with less than a week to go before Christmas and Hanukkah.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We don't have any Christmas presents under the tree this year because the wages, the hours that we get working for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  just simply aren't enough to get by in today's economy.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The drivers picketing outside seven facilities.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 There is no job security within the warehouse right now. And there are little to no benefits in the warehouse right now for us to be able to take care of our families.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From California\par \par \uc2 STRIKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Who are we?\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) To Georgia.\par \par \uc2 AMAZON WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Most of us wouldn't be here if we didn't like the job, right? We're just asking for you to like meet us in the middle somewhere.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) To New York. Two people arrested, given a ticket for disorderly conduct at the demonstration in Queens. The strike is organized by the teamsters union hoping to pressure \uc2 Amazon\uc2  for better benefits, higher wages and safer working conditions.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We are trying to hit \uc2 Amazon\uc2  where the pocket book will be most felt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONCERN AMAZON STRIKE COULD DELAY SOME HOLIDAY SHIPPING\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But \uc2 Amazon\uc2  doesn't recognize the teamsters as a union representing their employees and says it won't negotiate with them. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  also saying in a statement, "What you see here are almost entirely outsiders, not \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employees or partners, and the suggestion otherwise is just another lie from the teamsters."\par \par \uc2 AMAZON SPOKESPERSON (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Christmas is on track and we fully expect to be able to fulfill our delivery promises for our customers.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So there are a few dozen delivery drivers here. They are not technically \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employees, but many of them, most of them work for third party companies that exclusively deliver \uc2 Amazon\uc2  packages.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There are also these barricades that are set up by police to ensure delivery vehicles can continue going in and out here. And \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is in steadfast their customers can count on their holiday packages arriving on time. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WINTER STORM ON THE MOVE AS HOLIDAY TRAVEL RAMPS UP BUSIEST TIMES TO FLY & HIT THE ROAD\b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Rebeca. We're gonna turn now to the winter storm and its impact on early holiday travel. Take a live look at Minneapolis St. Paul International Airport right now, expected to be the busiest travel day of the year. We start with Alex Perez in Madison, Wisconsin. Good morning, Alex.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINTER STORM ON THE MOVE AS HOLIDAY TRAVEL RAMPS UP\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, George. The snow is piling up here in Madison and in parts of the Midwest. This storm is expected to create a lot of problems for many through the weekend.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, a winter storm on the move from the Midwest to the northeast on what's expected to be the busiest air travel day before Christmas. Minnesota declaring a snow emergency after more than six inches of snow falling. This semi-truck jack knifing. Plows out trying to keep up with the conditions. A ground stop issued at the airport due to the weather.\par \par \uc2 TRAVELER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm keeping my fingers crossed. I'm thinking that there's probably going to be a delay. But maybe we'll get out since we're early.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This car struggling to get traction, then giving up and backing down. Salt trucks out in force in Wisconsin, miles of roads and highways proactively treated with a liquid brine. People pitching in, doing their part to keep sidewalks safe and clear.\par \par \uc2 RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I just see the sidewalk. Some people are working, and I see someone a little bit about to slide.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plows in Fargo working to clear the interstate.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the snow is now moving east and expected to be followed by a blast of arctic air, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What does this all mean for holiday travel?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUSIEST TIMES TO FLY & HIT THE ROAD\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, George, according to the \uc2 TSA\uc2 , today is expected to be one of the busiest days at airports this travel season. In fact, the top three busiest airports will be Atlanta, Dallas Ft. Worth and Denver, with the most crowded times coming between 8:00 AM and Noon.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Experts say the busiest highways will be I-95 southbound near Washington, DC, I-5 southbound, south of Los Angeles, and also I-75 northbound between Orlando and Gainesville. The worst times to drive are between 1:00 PM and 8:00 PM today and tomorrow between 4:00 and 8:00.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAS PRICES EXPECTED TO KEEP DROPPING\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As far as gas prices, according to AAA, they are expected to keep dropping, in part because of the colder weather and more people working remotely. The national average could drop below $3 for the first time since 2021. Gear up, because it's going to be a busy travel holiday season, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Alex, thanks very much. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW DETAILS ON KING CHARLES' CANCER TREATMENT KING CHARLES' CANCER TREATMENT "WILL CONTINUE INTO NEXT YEAR"\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good to know. Okay, Erielle, thanks very much. We're gonna get the latest now on the health of King Charles as he continues his cancer treatment. Chief foreign correspondent Ian Pannell is at Buckingham Palace. Good morning, Ian.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ON KING CHARLES' CANCER TREATMENT\par \par \uc2 IAN PANNELL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, good morning, George. A royal sources telling ABC News today that King Charles is going to be continuing with his cancer treatment into next year, saying that it's a managed condition. The source also adding that the treatment is heading in a positive direction and that King Charles will continue with his busy schedule too. Obviously positive signals.\par \par \uc2 IAN PANNELL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He's been very visible this Christmas season, he's even out and about again today with the Queen. This is their last engagement before the holidays. The King announcing his cancer diagnosis back in February of course, when it was discovered during an operation on his prostate. He hasn't disclosed the type or stage of his cancer, or the sort of treatment that he's been receiving.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KING CHARLES' CANCER TREATMENT "WILL CONTINUE INTO NEXT YEAR"\par \par \uc2 IAN PANNELL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But I think it's worth noting the prolonged treatment isn't unusual for quite a few forms of canner. Of course it's been a tough year for the Royals with both the King and Princess Kate diagnosed with cancer. The Princess announcing in September that her treatment had ended. I can tell you there are thousands of well-wishers out here today wishing the King and the Queen all the best for the holiday season. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 126 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 NEMCOVA, TSUNAMI, ALL HANDS AND HEARTS\par \par \uc2 "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 "MUFASA: THE LION KING", NORTH POLE EXPRESS\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA," live from Times Square.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck00069\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLIDAY PARENTING PLAYBOOK DR. MONA AMIN\b0\par\par\uc2 918 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, LOWE'S, FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "BLUEY"\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, CHARGES, NYC, THOMPSON, AGNIFILO\par \par \uc2 SPINAL CORD, ARC-EX, MORITZ, OWENS, MOBILITY, THERAPY\par \par \uc2 PARKING, AIRPORTS, SAFETY, PRICE, HOTELS\par \par \uc2 GIBERSON, STUDENTS, EAGLES, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , AMAZON, WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LAST MINUTE, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 PARENTING, PLAYBOOK, AMIN\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now with our "GMA" cover story. Our holiday parenting playbook. Tis the season for overindulgence and overscheduling. Pediatrician and parenting expert Dr. Mona Amin is here with some tips on keeping everyone healthy and happy during the holidays. It's great to see you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY PARENTING PLAYBOOK\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You are also a mom of a 5-year-old and 18-month-old. So your hands are full. A lot of parents at this time of year, we default to screen time because everything is so chaotic, but you say don't do that.\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 Well, it's gonna be a reality that screens are gonna be a part of our life, especially during the holidays. But balance it and set expectations with your child. It's really important to remember that the holidays are about social gatherings, so rather than having your child on an iPad, maybe do a holiday movie together and talk about those characters to make it a social experience. And also maintain screen free zones. So try to minimize screens at the dining table or during certain social gatherings so that the children can enjoy the social experience.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAINTAIN SCREEN-FREE ZONES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANAGING SCREEN TIME, SLEEP & SWEETS DURING THE HOLIDAYS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love the idea of having something together, to experience together.\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're getting great questions from our viewers. This is one from Michelle.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE (PARENT)\par \par \uc2 When the whole family's together having fun, it's impossible to get my toddler to impossible to get my toddler to take a nap. Should we skip it altogether or try for an earlier one?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What are we doing here?\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 So I think every toddler parent can understand that their child has FOMO, a fear of missing out. Everything is so exciting.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. Yes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SKIP NAPS OR STICK TO A SCHEDULE?\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 So recognize that. Do a mini bed time routine during their nap. So get in the bedroom 15 minutes before. Make it dim, make it cool. Talk to them, sing to them. And if they don't take the nap, which is a reality, because everything is exciting, try to move the bed time earlier so they're not dealing with an overtired situation. And the next day, try to get back on schedule so that we can balance fun and also sleep needs.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So try to go back the next day. That's really important advice.\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Karen has this question.\par \par \uc2 KAREN (PARENT)\par \par \uc2 How can I help my 5-year-old develop a healthy self-control around sweets?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ah, yes. At the sweet, at the sweet table, you just see the kids picking every cookie off the table.\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 And this is important not just for the holidays, but year around. Right? So the first thing is don't vilify sweets. They're a part of our life.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY SWEETS SUCCESS\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 And when we do that, it can lead to feeling out of control when there's actually access. So balance it, pair it with other nutrient rich foods, like protein rich foods and fiber so that we're encouraging that balance, and moderate and practice that moderation as well in front of them. And also, don't, don't vilify it and also encourage them to explore different things. If they are reaching for that sugary cookie, the fourth one, say, hey, we can have it with dinner later or we can have it tomorrow so that we're not using judgment towards those sweets.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you.\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 And the last thing is don't bribe them with sweets. Don't say, eat the broccoli and then you'll get a sweet. Don't call it a treat or a surprise. Call it a cookie, pair it with another favorite meal, and enjoy.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Thank you so much, Dr. Mona.\par \par \uc2 DR. MONA AMIN (BOARD CERTIFIED PEDIATRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And by the way, I spoke with parents.com about parenting around the holidays and how to handle burnout. You can find out more about that on their website. They did such a nice job. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Thank you, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck00064\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPENDING, ROY, JOHNSON, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, CORBITT\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, TRAVEL, ROADS, AIRPORTS, GAS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 DRONES, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BAN, SECURITY, PRECAUTIONARY\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, SCHEDULE\par \par \uc2 HELENE, HOMES, \uc2 LOWE'S\uc2 , FAMILIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMEST YEAR TO DATE\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, you said you were going to Minnesota, and I said by Christmas you'll be warming up above average. A lot of people had a very, very warm year. Like year to date, warmest in New York, Philadelphia, back to Houston and to Phoenix, Arizona. So a lot of people in top five, which are all marked by that yellow. We'll have more coming up, but your local weather in 30 seconds.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have just five shopping days left before the holidays. You guys done?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Never started.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're gonna help everyone, including these guys, when we come back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORKERS AT SOME UNIONIZED \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  GO ON STRIKE PLANNED FIVE DAYS OF ESCALATING STRIKES\b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY STRIKES\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, WORKERS, DELIVERIES, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , EMPLOYEES, UNION\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know for a lot of people that's great news there. Trevor, thank you so much for that. Now to the workers at some unionized \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores walking off the job this morning. Morgan Norwood is at a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  here in New York. Good morning, Morgan.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORKERS AT SOME UNIONIZES \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, Michael. That's right, this morning 11,000 unionized baristas at more than 530 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  going on strike at company owned stores. It's happening in Los Angeles, Chicago, Seattle after negotiations broke down. The union hitting the company on the final weekend of the holiday shopping season and walking off the job later today.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) While the strike will begin relatively small, the number of stores will grow over the planned five days of escalating strikes. Workers say \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  back tracked on an agreement about future organizing and fair pay. Now this latest offer from \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  offers up a 2% wage increase and a guaranteed 1.5% in future years.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The union saying that's simply not enough. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  claims the union prematurely ended bargaining sessions this week saying in a statement, "We are ready to continue negotiations to reach agreements. We just need the union to return to the table." Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekck0005n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STRIKES BEFORE THE HOLIDAYS WORKERS FOR AMAZON & \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  WALK OFF THE JOB\b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GERMANY, TERRORISM, CHRISTMAS MARKET, ARREST\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAYS, TRAVEL, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINTER BLAST MAKES TRAVEL TREACHEROUS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, SNOW, RAIN, WIND CHILLS\par \par \uc2 SPENDING BILL, JOHNSON, JEFFRIES, MCCONNELL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER GOVERNMENT SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AMAZON, \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , KORGAN, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRIKES BEFORE THE HOLIDAYS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next tonight with days until the holidays some \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers going on strike and threatening to expand the walkout as drivers with the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  are picketing outside Amazon facilities. What did workers want? And will these strikes interfere with the holidays? Here's our chief national correspondent Matt Gutman.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORKERS FOR AMAZON & \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  WALK OFF THE JOB\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, just days before Christmas, thousands of workers at some of the nation's largest companies going on strike.\par \par \uc2 PICKETER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 No contract.\par \par \uc2 PICKETERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 No coffee.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  baristas here in Los Angeles as well as Chicago and Seattle, where the company is headquartered, kicking off a five-day strike today, demanding better pay and benefits.\par \par \uc2 PICKETER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We know our worth. And we know how to get there.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  says the demands are, quote, "unsustainable." And it's day two of the strike involving delivery workers for Amazon.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why are you striking now just a few days before Christmas?\par \par \uc2 RANDY KORGAN (\uc2 INTERNATIONAL BROTHERHOOD OF TEAMSTERS\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Well, consumers may, next time that they look at their phone and push something, try to empathize and recognize that when they hit that order button that there's a person on the other end of it and how they're impacted.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Amazon says it has 800,000 operations employees and disputes the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  claims that 10,000 people have walked off their job. And Amazon says most of those protesting aren't Amazon employees, insisting the strike is having no effect on deliveries.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Whit, I'm told we could see multiple rounds of these in the coming months. And just moments ago, the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  announcing that workers from the facility in Staten Island are now joining this nationwide strike beginning at midnight. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Something to watch closely in the days ahead. Matt Gutman, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241224ekck00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEAMSTERS LAUNCH LARGEST STRIKE AGAINST AMAZON IN U.S. HISTORY THOUSANDS OF AMAZON WAREHOUSE WORKERS GO ON STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHUTDOWN SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GOV, SHUTDOWN, BILL, JOHNSON, SCALISE, TRUMP, MUSK, PRICE, JEFFRIES, DEBT\par \par \uc2 TEAMSTERS, STRIKE, AMAZON, WAREHOUSE, WORKERS, STATES, SHIPPING, PACKAGES\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, TRAVEL, RUSH, FLYING, TSA, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , ROADS, AAA\par \par \uc2 TX, UNION, PACIFIC, TRAIN, SEMI, DERAILMENT, CRASH, HAZMAT, LINO, INJURIES, FATALITY\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, EXTRADITED, CHARGES, THOMPSON, MURDER, TERRORISM\par \par \uc2 NEW JERSEY, LASER, STRIKES, DRONES, PLANES, PILOTS, BLINDNESS\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK, BAN, BYTEDANCE, CHINA, SCOTUS, USERS, ACCOUNTS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM NOVEMBER 22\par \par \uc2 ROYAL, CARIBBEAN, CRUISE, PASSENGER, VIRGIL, OUTBURST, DEATH, MIKHAIL\par \par \uc2 HILTON, BILL, HOUSE, CHILD, ABUSE, ACT, TROUBLED, TEEN, PROGRAMS\par \par \uc2 GIFT, CARDS, RESELLERS, DISCOUNTS, SCAMS, WARNINGS, TIPS\par \par \uc2 INGALL, LIPSCOMB, BASKETBALL, SCHOLARSHIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM STOWE, VERMONT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHRISTMAS WEEK RAIN/SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, STRIKE, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First, a look at the top stories "Breaking at 8."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We start with the breaking news on \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  launched what it calls the largest ever strike against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . The stroke started here in New York. Let's go to Raegan Medgie from our station WABC. She's on the scene. Good morning, Raegan.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEAMSTERS LAUNCH LARGEST STRIKE AGAINST AMAZON IN U.S. HISTORY\par \par \uc2 RAEGAN MEDGIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right, George. So, want to take you kind of through what exactly is going on. We're in Maspeth, Queens. This is one of the fulfillment centers for \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . The people you see behind me, they are drivers with \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . And we all know these drivers. They deliver all the goods, the holiday gifts to you and me. So, take a look. They're right here in the driveway area. If we pan to the left, you can see that there are some vans waiting to leave. The \uc2 NYPD\uc2  is also on scene and trying to get these drivers to get loads that are in the trucks to get through. But we have the other drivers who are striking. Every now and again, you'll hear honks and horns from driving vehicles, you know, residents in the area seem to support this strike.\par \par \uc2 RAEGAN MEDGIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, basically, each worker reports 10,000 striking workers across the country working for \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , which is a non-union company. The \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  here started setting up unions at fulfillment centers on Staten Island and Maspeth, Queens. \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  organized the strike, accusing \uc2 Amazon\uc2  of ignoring a clear deadline of come to the bargaining table to negotiate a contract, a union contract with workers here at the Maspeth facility, among others. The demands, higher pay.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS OF AMAZON WAREHOUSE WORKERS GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 RAEGAN MEDGIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And \uc2 Amazon\uc2  says \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  are not in charge, that they are. And that \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  are organizing this illegally. So, you can see, right now, we have this truck, a Prime, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Prime truck trying to get out. We have the striking workers in front preventing that from happening. And this is not just, this is part of the story because we have even more workers. And we're going to walk around this way. You can see they're even striking more vans. Look at all of these vans that are trying to get out of the fulfillment center here in Maspeth, Queens, as the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers strike to get a contract and a fair deal. They want higher pay. Reporting for "GMA," Raegan Medgie, back to you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Raegan, thank you so much. We appreciate you. We've been watching your fine reporting, your fine reporting on WABC. Good to have you here on "GMA" with us. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekcj0003a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEAMSTERS LAUNCH LARGEST STRIKE AGAINST AMAZON IN US HISTORY THOUSANDS OF AMAZON WAREHOUSE WORKERS GO ON STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHUTDOWN SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GOV, SHUTDOWN, BILL, JOHNSON, SCALISE, TRUMP, MUSK, PRICE, JEFFRIES, DEBT\par \par \uc2 TEAMSTERS, STRIKE, AMAZON, WAREHOUSE, WORKERS, STATES, SHIPPING, PACKAGES\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Thank you, Robin. Now to breaking news, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  launching what it is called the largest ever strike against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . Chief business correspondent Rebecca Jarvis is here with the story for us. Good morning, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEAMSTERS LAUNCH LARGEST STRIKE AGAINST AMAZON IN US HISTORY\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAP: AMAZON STRIKE, DRIVERS AND WAREHOUSE WORKERS STRIKING\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. Good morning, guys. And this strike, it started more than an hour ago right here in New York, and according to the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2 , it will also include about 10,000 \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers at facilities all across the country, Scosche, Illinois, Atlanta, San Francisco, and Southern California. The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  say in a statement the nationwide action follows \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's repeated refusals to follow the law and bargain with the thousands of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers who organize with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 . But according to \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  don't actually represent their workers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS OF AMAZON WAREHOUSE WORKERS GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The retail giant telling us, "For more than a year now, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have continued to intentionally mislead the public, claiming that they represent thousands of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employees and drivers. They don't. And this is another attempt to push a false narrative." The big question for consumers right now with this action coming less than a week before Christmas and Hannukah, will there be any delays in shipping gifts purchased on \uc2 Amazon\uc2 ? At this point, organizers have not said how long the strike is expected to last. But the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 ' president says if your package is delayed during the holidays, you can blame \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's insatiable greed. And George, just be kind to the workers out there right now. They are hustling from every company.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They are going through a lot right now.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250115ekcj0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMAZON STRIKE DAYS BEFORE HOLIDAYS TEAMSTERS ACCUSE COMPANY OF "INSATIABLE GREED"\b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, AGNIFILO, ADAMS, EXTRADITION, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 SPENDING BILL, MUSK, TRUMP, JEFFRIES, KENNEDY, PAUL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER GOVERNMENT SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, WIND CHILLS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW EMERGENCY SNARLS TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, TEAMSTERS, STRIKE, CIANCIOTTO, SOREFF, NANTEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON STRIKE DAYS BEFORE HOLIDAYS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the protests at Amazon facilities coast to coast tonight and, of course, just days before Christmas. Striking drivers now targeting facilities in New York, Atlanta, Illinois, and California. What they're now demanding. And, of course, the question, will it affect your gifts getting there on time? Here tonight, Trevor Ault.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEAMSTERS ACCUSE COMPANY OF "INSATIABLE GREED"\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, many outside drivers hired by Amazon coast to coast walking off the job just days before Christmas and new year's. Workers who deliver packages from seven Amazon facilities now on strike.\par \par \uc2 LUKE CIANCIOTTO (DRIVER)\par \par \uc2 We don't have Christmas presents under the tree this year because the wages, the hours that we get working for Amazon just simply aren't enough to get by.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Our Matt Gutman in California.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You can see these picketers are blocking this Amazon facility. They say they'll stay as long as it takes because they are overworked and underpaid.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  is accusing Amazon of insatiable greed, saying the company ignored a December 15th deadline to come to the bargaining table for better pay and working conditions. Faith Abubey in Georgia speaking to driver Thomas Hickman (PH) who says he fractured his ankle on the job.\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY DRIVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 They didn't care about the well-being and they was more worried about the packages being delivered.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Amazon does not recognize the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  as a union representing their employees. It says it won't negotiate with them, accusing many demonstrators of being outsiders. While most of the drivers we spoke with do work for third-party delivery companies hired by Amazon, they say they wear Amazon uniforms, drive Amazon vehicles, and many exclusively deliver boxes from Amazon.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN SOREFF (DRIVER)\par \par \uc2 I dress in Amazon uniform. I ride in an Amazon van, and I deliver Amazon packages.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Amazon, tonight, insists the strike has had no impact on their deliveries.\par \par \uc2 KELLY NANTEL (AMAZON SPOKESPERSON)\par \par \uc2 Christmas is on track. And we fully expect to be able to fulfill our delivery promises for our customers.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  arrested two picketers here today in Queens for blocking delivery vehicles. This picketing is still going on. They say they'll be back tomorrow. David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Trevor Ault reporting tonight. Trevor, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241223ekcj00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMAZON BRACING FOR POTENTIAL STRIKE WORKERS AT NYC FACILITIES AUTHORIZE WALKOUT\b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRONE MYSTERY DEEPENS\par \par \uc2 DRONES, MYSTERY, RESIDENTS, GOVERNMENT, MAYORKAS\par \par \uc2 MURELLO, DRONES, COMMUNITIES, SIGHTINGS, MYSTERY\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, THOMPSON, EXTRADITION, BRAGG, ATTORNEY\par \par \uc2 SYRIA, ISRAEL, STRIKES, ASSAD, REBELS, BLINKEN, FRANCE\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, TRUMP, SENATE, VACCINES, SANDERS\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , MAHOMES, DUBOSE, INJURIES, BILLS, LIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOMORROW AFTERNOON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "THE LION KING"\par \par \uc2 MOSS, CANCER, SURGERY, TREATMENT, THIELEN, O'CONNELL, \uc2 NFL\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER, CHARGED, SEX TRAFFICKING, WILLIAMS, DENARO\par \par \uc2 CHRISTMAS, THIEVES, SANTAS, DECORATIONS, OAS, MILNER\par \par \uc2 TIPPING, HOLIDAY, SERVICE, AMOUNT, CASH\par \par \uc2 LOOKALIKES, KELCE, CONTESTANTS\par \par \uc2 DRONES, SIGHTINGS, MYSTERY, SAFETY, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMMUNITIES ON EDGE OVER DEEPENING DRONE MYSTERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. DEPLOYING "ADDITIONAL RESOURCES"\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, STRIKE, AUTHORIZATION, HOLIDAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON BRACING FOR POTENTIAL STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORKERS AT NYC FACILITIES AUTHORIZE WALKOUT\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Going to turn now to Amazon\u160\'00\'A0facing potential strike just nine days before Christmas and Hannukah. Elizabeth Schulze has the latest for us. Good morning to you, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, Robin. The threat of this strike comes during the mad dash to deliver all of those holiday gifts. The \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  says that it gave Amazon a deadline of yesterday, December 15, to come to the bargaining table over new contract terms for more than 5,000 workers at two of its warehouses in New York, the union writing in a statement, "Amazon is pushing its workers closer to the picket line by failing to address concerns about low wages and dangerous working conditions."\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Amazon tells us, "For more than year now, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have misled the public, calling this another attempt to push a false narrative." Amazon operates hundreds of warehouses across the US, so even if a strike at two of these facilities starts in the coming days, it could have a limited impact nationwide on the shipment of holiday gifts, especially if they're already out on the truck for delivery. So, bottom line, Amazon packages should still arrive on time, but for all of the last-minute shoppers, still want to keep an eye on your tracking information, guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is key. All right, Elizabeth, thank you. Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," going thrifting for great gifting, how secondhand stores could help you save.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, our parenting playbook. With the holidays right around the corner, we are looking at gift giving and receiving and how to focus the kids on gratitude and joy.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Lori Bergamotto here with the right stuff, the presents that are trending online. Lara is upstairs with a special guest.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hi, George, yeah. Hakuna matata, no worries because this guy is here. There he is. Billy Eichner, everybody making his return as the voice of Timon in "Mufasa: The Lion King." We're going to talk to him and have a lot of fun coming up on "GMA," so stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250114ekcg0000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PLAY OF THE DAY THANK YOU, TONY BARRETT\b0\par\par\uc2 753 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEATHER ALERT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RARE CALIFORNIA TORNADO\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, DOUBEK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADO TOUCHES DOWN IN SCOTTS VALLEY, CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERAL INJURED & EXTENSIVE DAMAGE IN AREAS OF SANTA CRUZ MOUNTAINS\par \par \uc2 DRONES, SIGHTINGS, HOCHUL, MASTRONARDY, SMITH, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE MYSTERY DRONE SIGHTINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRIEF SHUTDOWN OF STEWART INTL AIRPORT RUNWAYS\par \par \uc2 MANGIONE, FRIEDMAN, EXTRADITION, MURDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CEO MURDER SUSPECT HIRES HIGH-PROFILE ATTORNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LUIGI MANGIONE REMAINS IN PENNSYLVANIA JAIL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , VANCE, HEGSETH, DESANTIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT-ELECT TO MEET WITH HOUSE REPUBLICANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROBERT F. KENNEDY, JR. TO MEET WITH SENATORS\par \par \uc2 SYRIA, ASSAD, TICE, TIMMERMAN, BLINKEN, AL-SHARAA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. DIPLOMATS HAVE DIRECT CONTACT WITH SYRIA REBELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE DEPARTMENT CONSIDERS HTS GROUP A TERRORIST ORGANIZATION\par \par \uc2 SOUTH KOREA, IMPEACHMENT, YOON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOUTH KOREANS CELEBRATE IMPEACHMENT OF PRESIDENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARLIAMENT VOTE FOLLOWS YOON SUK YEOL'S FAILED MARTIAL LAW DECLARATION\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, CUTS, INFLATION, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OBSERVERS EXPECT NEW INTEREST RATE CUT THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL RESERVE DECISION COMPLICATED BY INFLATION RATE\par \par \uc2 HUNTER, HEISMAN TROPHY\par \par \uc2 OBESITY RATES, EMERGENCY C-SECTION, RISKS\par \par \uc2 DISCOUNT STORES, HUTCHINSON, SILVA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOPPERS FLOCKING TO DISCOUNT STORES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTING DOWN BARGAINS FOR THE HOLIDAYS\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , MATCHUPS, EDWARDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NFL\uc2  MATCHUPS PREVIEW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLS VS. LIONS\par \par \uc2 BARRETT, RETIREMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now with our "Play of the Day," and it is a very, very special one. It is a huge thank you to a lifelong ABC-er, Tony Barrett, retiring after more than four decades?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Three decades. Three-plus, right?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Three-plus, yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Amazing. Tony, congratulations. Calm, collected, poised, and patient from the control room with all of us. We couldn't do it without you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look at these graphics just for him. A legend and so many are wishing him well. Take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THANK YOU, TONY BARRETT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Big congratulations to one of the people behind the controlled chaos of "Good Morning America," director Tony Barrett.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DAN HARRIS (FORMER "GMA" ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 Tony Barrett, you are retiring. Congratulations.\par \par \uc2 PAULA FARIS (FORMER "GMA" ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 You are the wizard behind the curtain. You had our backs and you made us look good.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Congratulations, Tony, from all of us here at "World News Tonight," wishing you all the best on your retirement after more than 40 years here at ABC News.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Tony, thank you for making my weekends enjoyable.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Okay, Tony. Yep. You're just missing pod 3. We're going to miss you.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm going to miss you.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm really going to miss you, Tony.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (MALE) (CONTINUED)\par \par \uc2 Hi, Tony. Congratulations.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Tony, you know we're going to miss you because there's no one quite like you.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 You have an exceptional gift for timing. You're always calm and clear under pressure. It's not often you can have a friend that's joyful at 3:00 in the morning.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I just want to say the outpouring of love and affection throughout this building and afar was simply phenomenal.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I just want to thank you for all of your guidance, your support, and your dedication that you poured into me, a young guy who was in well over his head.\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We're really going to miss that smile and that leadership in the control room, but I could say that I am the last person that got to sit next to you for your final show and what a pleasure that is.\par \par \uc2 NEWS ANCHORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Tony.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Congratulations, Tony.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wishing you the very best in your retirement.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Farewell, my dear.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're going to miss you. But you know what, this is your best next chapter, right? Congratulations.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Congratulations. Tony, we absolutely...\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A round of applause in the studio.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...cherish the work that you've done for us here in ABC News. The very best in retirement, Tony.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241219ekcf0000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MCKINSEY & COMPANY AGREES TO PAY $650 MILLION SETTLEMENT OVER ROLE IN HELPING FUEL OPIOID EPIDEMIC\b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 COLD, WIND CHILLS, SNOW\par \par \uc2 TEMPERATURES, PRECIPITATION\par \par \uc2 CEO, MURDER, THOMPSON\par \par \uc2 TIMMERMAN, ASSAD, SYRIA\par \par \uc2 PELOSI, INJURED\par \par \uc2 COUPLE, KILLED, MEXICO, CARDONA, AMBRIZ\par \par \uc2 DUKE UNIVERSITY\uc2 , RAPE, CASE, ACCUSER, LIED, MANGUM\par \par \uc2 MCKINSEY & COMPANY\uc2 , OPIOID, EPIDEMIC\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the agreement between federal prosecutors and the global giant \uc2 McKinsey & Company\uc2 , the firm agreeing to pay hundreds of millions of dollars for its role in the opioid epidemic. ABC's Perry Russom joins us from Washington with those details. Perry, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 MCKINSEY & COMPANY\uc2  AGREES TO PAY $650 MILLION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SETTLEMENT OVER ROLE IN HELPING FUEL OPIOID EPIDEMIC\par \par \uc2 PERRY RUSSOM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Janai, good morning to you. With this deal, \uc2 McKinsey & Company\uc2  will pay $650 million to settle a federal investigation into their work tied to the opioid epidemic. McKinsey is an international consulting firm. They were being investigated for their role in helping \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2  sell OxyContin and other painkillers, fueling the drug crisis. The CDC has linked opioids to the deaths of more than 80,000 people just last year. Federal investigators say McKinsey worked with \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2  to turbocharge their sales. At the time, there was concern among doctors OxyContin was being abused so Purdue's sales went down.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL PROSECUTORS SAY MCKINSEY "KNEW THE RISKS"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTHORITIES SAY COMPANY DEVISED WAYS TO "TURBOCHARGE" OPIOID PRESCRIPTIONS\par \par \uc2 PERRY RUSSOM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Prosecutors say McKinsey advised Purdue to target sales to high volume prescribers, including those who were prescribing the drugs for reasons that were unsafe and medically unnecessary. That often led to drug abuse and addiction. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  said McKinsey would even do ride-alongs with Purdue so they could get even more scripts written.\par \par \uc2 PERRY RUSSOM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) With this financial agreement, the $650 million, McKinsey avoids prosecution in the criminal and civil investigations, and McKinsey is accepting responsibility for their conduct. In a statement, the company says they are deeply sorry, and as a part of the agreement, they will do any work related to marketing or selling controlled substances. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. A major agreement there. Perry, thank you so much for your reporting.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250108ekce00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JOBS REPORT OUT THIS MORNING EXPECTED TO SHOW BIG HIRING REBOUND IN NOVEMBER\b0\par\par\uc2 407 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 December 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW IMAGES\par \par \uc2 THOMPSON, MURDER, SUSPECT, MANHUNT, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 STORM, ARCTIC, SNOW, WINDS, ROADS, WHITEOUTS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, WIND CHILLS, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 EARTHQUAKE, MAGNITUDE, AFTERSHOCKS, RESIDENTS, TSUNAMI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CABINET, HEGSETH, SENATORS, BIDEN, PARDONS\par \par \uc2 JOBS, REBOUND, HIRING, ECONOMY, UNEMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, George, thank you. We go now to the economy and the new jobs numbers. Elizabeth Schulze is here with those details. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOBS REPORT OUT THIS MORNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPECTED TO SHOW BIG HIRING REBOUND IN NOVEMBER\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. This report is really critical for anyone who's on the job hunt. It is expected that 214,000 jobs were added to the work force in November. That would be a big rebound from the dismal 12,000 jobs in October. Hurricanes Milton and Helene and the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike were key reasons for that slowdown.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But with most of those impacted workers now back on the job, we are expecting to see strong hiring in manufacturing, construction and hospitality. Big picture here, the unemployment rate at 4.1%, still near an historic low. But employers aren't hiring at the superfast pace that they were at the start of the year, so it is taking a little bit longer now to land a job. Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BITCOIN'S MAJOR MILESTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRYPTOCURRENCY TOPS $100,000 FOR THE FIRST TIME\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The other major headline people are talking about is this Bitcoin headline, now trading above $100,000 for the first time, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and this has just been a meteoric rise. The price of a single Bitcoin going from $68,000 on election day to just above $100,000. That is up 51%. Investors really are optimistic that the Trump administration will take a friendly approach to our crypto currency.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Of course the President Elect helped launch his own crypto venture before the election and he just nominated a crypto supporter to lead the SEC, which is Wall Street's top watch dog. Keep in mind, though, this is a volatile investment. Just as fast as prices go up, they can come back down too. Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, euphoria always can breed volatility. Thank you, Elizabeth. Whit.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020250101ekc600007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMAZON WORKERS IN MORE THAN 20 COUNTRIES TAKE TO T DEMONSTRATING OVER WORKING CONDITIONS, PAY & RIGHT TO UNIONIZE\b0\par\par\uc2 126 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CANADA, TRUMP, TARIFFS\par \par \uc2 SYRIA, CIVIL WAR\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, WORKERS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers are making their voices heard during one of the busiest shopping weekends of the holiday season. Workers in more than 20 countries, including right here in America, of course, are demonstrating over increased wages, improved working conditions, and the right for employees to be permitted to unionize. They're calling it the make \uc2 Amazon\uc2  pay days of resistance, and it's scheduled to last all weekend long through Cyber Monday. Whit?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON WORKERS IN MORE THAN 20 COUNTRIES TAKE TO THE STREETS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMONSTRATING OVER WORKING CONDITIONS, PAY & RIGHT TO UNIONIZE\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241225ekbu00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 23 AND ME ANNOUNCES LAYOFFS PRIVACY CONCERNS AS GENETIC TESTING COMPANY FACES UNCERTAIN FUTURE\b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE TRUMP TRANSITION\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BIDEN, ADMINISTRATION, HEGSETH, MUSK NOEM\par \par \uc2 SMITH, TRUMP, DOJ, INVESTIGATIONS, MANDATE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, BIDEN, GOP, UKRAINE, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 TEN COMMANDMENTS, LAW, LOUISIANA, CLASSROOMS\par \par \uc2 WILD FIRES, DRY, WINDS, RESIDENTS, EVACUATIONS, BRAY, FRANEK\par \par \uc2 EXPLOSION, CHEMICALS, KILLED, INJURED, O'NEILL, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 SPIRIT AIRLINES\uc2 , BANKRUPTCY, PASSENGERS, NOTEHOLDERS\par \par \uc2 23 AND ME, LAYOFFS, PRIVACY, GENETIC, DATA\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you so much for that, Gio. And now to trouble for genetic testing firm 23 And Me. The company is laying off nearly half of its workers and it's raising privacy concerns among customers. Erielle Reshef is here with the story. Good morning, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 23 AND ME ANNOUNCES LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRIVACY CONCERNS AS GENETIC TESTING COMPANY FACES UNCERTAIN FUTURE\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Michael. Revolutionary genealogy company 23 And Me is planning to lay off roughly 40% of its work force. Their CEO announcing over 200 staffers will be let go. The company also shuttering its drug development arm. The move comes after revenues dipped 12% last quarter, and share prices have plummeted.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Millions around the world have used 23 And Me to connect to their roots, sending in their saliva then receiving a detailed report about their DNA and their ancestry. Experts caution that because it is not a medical company, your personal information is not afforded the same privacy protection as your health records. It's considered a commercial transaction, not a medical one.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Last year 23 And Me fell victim to a massive security breach, exposing roughly 6.9 million users' data, including ancestry information and personal details, paying out roughly $30 million in a settlement. With its financial future in kind of turmoil here, we reached out to 23 And Me about where that leaves your DNA. The company told us, they have no further comment. Guys.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241206ekbd00031\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, breaking news as we come on the air. The wildfire emergency in the northeast and the fire in New York City. Some train service halted. Also breaking, the major factory explosion, multiple injuries. Workers rushed to the hospital. Residents urged to shelter in place.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RED FLAG WARNINGS ACROSS NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 First, tonight, firefighters battling multiple fires in and around New York City. And an electrical fire forcing \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  to suspend some service. Also, the red flag warnings from New York all the way up to Boston. Army National Guard helicopters now being used for water drops. Winds gusting up to 40 miles per hour fanning the flames. And the major change now coming in the weather tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS AFTER MASSIVE EXPLOSION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, tonight, the massive factory explosion in Louisville. Witnesses say it felt like an earthquake. The blast heard for miles, at least 11 people hurt. Part of the facility collapsing. A shelter in place order for a time.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLIGHT BAN AFTER U.S. PLANES HIT BY GUNFIRE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  now says one of its planes was shot at, too, while flying in and out of Haiti. And this evening, the \uc2 FAA\uc2  now banning all US flights to Haiti.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP BUILDS NEW INNER CIRCLE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The news coming in at this hour on President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's new team. Trump now expected to name South Dakota Governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  to head the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 . And sources telling ABC News, Senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  will likely become secretary of state. And just in tonight, Trump's pick to head the CIA and the big meeting tomorrow, President-elect Trump and President Biden at the White House.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE DELAYS 'HUSH MONEY' DECISION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 In New York City tonight, the judge in President-elect Trump's hush money conviction delaying the immunity ruling in that case. Trump's attorneys now arguing his felony convection should be tossed out because of the Supreme Court's decision on presidential immunity. So, what happens now?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE CRACKDOWN ON ANTISEMITIC ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Overseas tonight, he alarming scene in Amsterdam. Protesters setting off explosives inside a tram. Authorities believe some targeting Jews. Some of the attackers yelling antisemitic slurs. Police bracing for my violent clashes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTHORITIES: MISSING FATHER FAKED HIS DEATH\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Here in the US tonight, the father and husband missing who was presumed dead. Tonight, the stunning twist. After searching for 54 days, authorities now believe he may have faked his own death, and where they believe he is now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JACK TEIXEIRA SENTENCING\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, a Massachusetts National Guard member who pleaded guilty to leaking highly classified military documents is now sentenced. And tonight here, remembering the singer called the first lady of children's music. Her unforgettable songs that had the children singing.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight with David Muir."\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241115ekbc00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOW TO LAND THE JOB YOU WANT TIPS TO BUILDING A RESUME & NAILING AN INTERVIEW\b0\par\par\uc2 1,584 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 ASSASSINATION, ATTEMPT, TRUMP, IRAN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TRANSITION, MUSK\par \par \uc2 TEXTS, RACIST\par \par \uc2 WISCONSIN, TEEN, ARRESTED, THREATS\par \par \uc2 DIDDY, BAIL\par \par \uc2 DOW, S&P 500, NASDAQ, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 TODD\par \par \uc2 "COLLEGE GAMEDAY", \uc2 LSU\uc2 , ALABAMA\par \par \uc2 PRINCESS KATE, CANCER, QUEEN CAMILLA, ENGLAND\par \par \uc2 GRAMMY, NOMINATIONS\par \par \uc2 DISNEY\uc2  D23, "LILO AND STITCH", "ICE AGE"\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, SNOWSTORM, EMERGENCY, WEATHER\par \par \uc2 MUSK, TRUMP, ZELENSKYY, TRANSITION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP TRANSITION PICKS UP SPEED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRES-ELECT & ELON MUSK SPEAK WITH UKRAINE PRES\par \par \uc2 STABBING, SEATTLE, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEATTLE STABBING SPREE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NINE PEOPLE INJURED OVER TWO DAYS, MAN ARRESTED\par \par \uc2 INSURANCE FRAUD, CAR CRASH, MARTINEZ, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER CHARGED IN BEL PARKWAY CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NYC MAN ACCUSED OF STAGING CRASH\par \par \uc2 BLACK FRIDAY, SALES, SHOPPING, EARLY, DEALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EARLY BLACK FRIDAY SALES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAILERS OFFER BIG SALES & CASH BACK\par \par \uc2 GRAMMY NOMINATIONS, HOUSTON, SWIFT\par \par \uc2 PANS, KNIVES, GRILL TOOLS, TOWELS, COOLER, REMOTE\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "MUFASA"\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, BLIZZARDS, MONKEYS,\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRES & BLIZZARDS\par \par \uc2 JOBS, INTERVIEW, RESUME, ADVICE, DURHAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO LAND THE JOB YOU WANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIPS TO BUILDING A RESUME & NAILING AN INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, the latest, moving on now, the latest poll from the New York Federal Reserve shows 28.4 percent of respondents are looking for a job. So, this morning, "GMA" is on the job and helping you. We are breaking down tips to landing the role that you really want. So, joining us now is career coach Emily Durham, also known as Emily the Recruiter. Emily, good morning to you. It's great to have you.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, thanks for having me. I'm excited to talk a little job hunting.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, so that number, first of all, nearly 30 percent, is pretty staggering in how many people are dissatisfied with where they are. But let's start with these, like, temporary, seasonal jobs. Those are starting to come out right now. What do people need to know if they're interested?\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 It really is that time of year, so December, January, amazing time for people to start looking for those seasonal jobs. I think what it really comes down to is if you haven't already applied, today is your day. We're going to go home, we're going to start applying for those jobs. We're no longer in a job market where you can apply for something and start two weeks later. Like, that's not the world we operate in anymore. So, apply quickly. And whether you're looking for fulltime, part time, seasonal, whatever it is, the trick isn't having a perfect resume. Nothing's ever going to be perfect. The trick is getting that resume opened because there is so much competition with that 30 percent of people looking for work.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 So, what you actually need to do is follow up. Like, that's the secret sauce in this little recipe. So, after you apply for that job, I want you in store. Get in there, schmooze, put on your good polo. Go say hi. If you've applied to a corporate role, fantastic, hit \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 . Let's send the recruiter a message. Let them know that you're interested and that you've applied. It's also a good time, let's phone a friend, let's ask for referrals, let's start networking. This job market, in my perspective, is one that is entirely ruled by who you know not what you know. Whether that's right or wrong, I can't comment on it. I just want y'all to get hired.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just is what it is.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 It is what it is. I didn't cook it this way.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I wasn't sure what you meant when you said before that this isn't the kind of job market where you apply and start two weeks later because you mean people are starting sooner than that. That's what you meant.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 I mean, actually mean they're going to start later.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, really?\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 Yes, and I'm happy you asked that. So, think four years ago, right, like, a pre-pandemic world, there was, the job market was hot. You could apply for a job. Oh my gosh, you're like, "Can you start Monday? By the way, you're gorgeous, you're perfect, thank you, let's double your salary." That's not the world we're working in today. Now we have, for the most part, more job seekers than jobs available. Competition is tough. So, why won't they throw in the extra round of interviews? No, we're not going to take that negotiation, we're going for the first person that says yes. So, that process extends a little bit longer than we would like it to. Yeah, it's a funky world we're living in.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's interesting. Okay, so what do you recommend for those coming out of high school or college who don't have much work experience? And that's the thing. You need the experience to get the experience, but how do you get it?\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 Have you seen that meme where it's, like, the toddler in a construction hat, saying, "This is when I should have started working"? That's how I feel about this. First things first, we have all been there. Stop panicking. There is no need to panic. But I think we really need to fundamentally redesign what experience looks like. Your academic experience, I don't care if that's high school, maybe that's volunteer, maybe that's projects, internships, hopefully paid internships, all of that is legitimate experience. So, let's repackage how you sell yourself.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 Like, I don't want young people walking into interviews saying, "Oh, by the way, I don't have this," "Oh, I'm really smart, but I don't have any experience doing this." Let's stop putting a spotlight on the stuff maybe we're not perfect at. Let's focus on what you have, even if it's unpaid work, that's A-okay, and let's focus on how you're a great learner. And I'll say it all the time, if you're struggling to get noticed, network, network, network. Let's ask for help, ask for feedback, ask for referrals. There is so much amazing information online about how to do that, as well.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, like you said, who you know, who you know.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 It's who you know. All it is is a phone call.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you were talking about how, you know, not everybody has the perfect resume or cover letter. But what about AI? Because I'm sure a lot of people are going to turn to AI, and they're going to say, "Hey, this will just do it for me, and it'll create the perfect resume."\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 Yes, the same way AI maybe shouldn't exclusively be doing your taxes, let's think about your resume in the same light. So, AI, I think we first need to start off by saying assume everybody's using it, assume the employer, assume you as a job seeker. What does that mean? That means everyone has a good resume. So, having a good resume isn't going to be a showstopper anymore. What it means is all of our resumes sound and look the exact same. So, how are you standing out? Good, unfortunately, isn't good enough.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 What I recommend doing when it comes to your, like, relationship with AI, use it as a starting point. Let's use that as a template, but we need a human touch, otherwise it's not going to work. We actually asked AI, I thought this was really interesting, to put together a generic resume for us. And I was like, "Show me a generic marketing resume." A couple of things that are interesting. Miss AI loves a buzzword. So, they are saying things like digital marketing, data and analytics. Okay, like what does that mean? What do you mean? Digital marketing is a lot of things. Analytics, that's a lot of things.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And if somebody is asking you the questions, you better know the answer.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 You better know. AI also will start putting buzzwords in there, where you're like, "Honey, I'm going to have to \uc2 Google\uc2  that, as well. I don't know what that means." Data is going to be on there, great, but you're not telling me what campaigns and that...\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Fantastic, and you break it down so well. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DURHAM (CAREER COACH)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And coming up, the women of NASCAR, meet the voices who are advocating for change on and off the track. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241203ekb90003m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HIGHWAY NEAR MISS CAUGHT ON CAMERA WORKER SPEAKS OUT AFTER NARROWLY AVOIDING ONCOMING BOX TRUCK\b0\par\par\uc2 640 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRE EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, WINDS, DAMAGE, EVACUATIONS, FRYHOFF, MCHALE, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, WINDS DROUGHT, WARNINGS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TRANSITION, WILES, IMMIGRATION, BIDEN, GOVERNORS\par \par \uc2 HACKERS, CHINA, BLANCHE, TEXTS, CALLS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, VICTORY, REACTION, PUTIN, UKRAINE, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 PHILLY, TRANSIT, STRIKE, AVERTED, SEPTA\par \par \uc2 TEXTS, RACISTS, SLAVERY, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 HIGHWAY, TRUCK, ELLERSON, VIDEO, DOMINQUEZ\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Pierre, thank you for your reporting on that. We turn now to an ABC News exclusive with the highway worker who narrowly avoided being hit by an oncoming box truck. Trevor Ault is here with the story. Incredibly troubling, scary images there. Trevor, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGHWAY NEAR MISS CAUGHT ON CAMERA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORKER SPEAKS OUT AFTER NARROWLY AVOIDING ONCOMING BOX TRUCK\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. You know, we often see signs about traffic fines doubling in work zones because crashes like these can be really dangerous. And this morning we are hearing from that road worker who narrowly avoided disaster.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Watch the dramatic moment a truck narrowly misses a road worker on a New York highway.\par \par \uc2 CHARLES ELLERSON (HIGHWAY MAINTENANCE WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I looked out at the right time and got out of there at the right time.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) 61-year-old Chuck Ellerson tells ABC News in an exclusive interview, how he averted what could have been a tragedy.\par \par \uc2 CHARLES ELLERSON (HIGHWAY MAINTENANCE WORKER)\par \par \uc2 Tried to get out of the way the best I can. I thought for sure it was close enough where it would have done a lot more than what it did.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ellereson is a highway maintenance worker. He says he'd been collecting trash on that road when a box truck darted in his direction.\par \par \uc2 CHARLES ELLERSON (HIGHWAY MAINTENANCE WORKER)\par \par \uc2 Next thing I know, I said this guy is not going to miss me.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dash cam video from one of the two work vehicles shows the truck crashing into the work area, demolishing one of the vehicles. Ellerson narrowly escaping uninjured.\par \par \uc2 CHARLES ELLERSON (HIGHWAY MAINTENANCE WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I dived into the ditch a little bit and grabbed my hard hat, put it back on, and sat there and tried to catch my senses for a long time.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Department of Transportation tells ABC News, New York State Police are investigating the incident and tweeted "Our highway workers put their lives on the line every day to keep New York roads safe. And this recent crash on I-81 near Whitney Point is a frightening reminder of the dangers they face."\par \par \uc2 COMMISSIONER MARIE THERESE DOMINQUEZ (NEW YORK STATE DEPT OF TRANSPORTATION)\par \par \uc2 Look, it's horrifying. Their job is to make sure that the roads and bridges in our state are safe so that everybody can use them.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And last year the New York Department of Transportation reported more than 200 work zone intrusions. They've since made some changes like adding work zone cameras to try to detect speeding. But drivers really have to pay attention, move over and slow down. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIAM PAYNE DEATH INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Trevor, thank you. Coming up, charged in the investigation into the death of One Direction star for Liam Payne.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAMES VAN DER BEEK ON CANCER DIAGNOSIS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, "Dawson Creek's" star James Van Der Beek shares new details about his cancer diagnosis and how he's getting through this challenging time.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAST MINUTE THANKSGIVING TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the points guy is here with last minute savings on Thanksgiving escapes. But first we head back over to you, Sam.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241203ekb800009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PHILADELPHIA TRANSIT STRIKE AVERTED FOR NOW BOTH SIDES AGREE TO KEEP TALKING, KEEP MORE THAN 5,000 SEPTA WORKERS ON THE JOB\b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRE EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, WINDS, DAMAGE, EVACUATIONS, FRYHOFF, MCHALE, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, WINDS DROUGHT, WARNINGS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TRANSITION, WILES, IMMIGRATION, BIDEN, GOVERNORS\par \par \uc2 HACKERS, CHINA, BLANCHE, TEXTS, CALLS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, VICTORY, REACTION, PUTIN, UKRAINE, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 PHILLY, TRANSIT, STRIKE, AVERTED, SEPTA\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Ian, thank you so much for that. We're gonna turn now to breaking news overnight from Philadelphia about a potential strike that would bring mass transit in the city to a halt. Stephanie Ramos is in Philly with the latest. Good morning Stephanie.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PHILADELPHIA TRANSIT STRIKE AVERTED FOR NOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOTH SIDES AGREE TO KEEP TALKING, KEEP MORE THAN 5,000 SEPTA WORKERS ON THE JOB\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Michael, good morning. A strike avoided for now. SEPTA and the transport workers union local 234, which represents more than 5,000 SEPTA workers, agreeing to continue talks after the contract agreement between the two entities ended at Midnight last night.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Here's what the president of the union said in a statement overnight. "We're willing to go the extra mile and grant additional time to reach a fair agreement. However, let me be clear, if SEPTA's managers fail to meet our demands, we will be on the picket line."\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now if the union were to strike, about 5,300 transit workers would take to the picket lines, bringing mass transit in Philadelphia to a halt while also affecting commuters in south Jersey and Wilmington, Delaware. Here's what employees are fighting for, better wages with safety and security issues at the center of their concerns.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're asking for bulletproof vests, bulletproof enclosures for operators and more police presence, citing on going violence in the city. It is unclear how long a strike could last, but commuters are breathing a sigh of relief this morning, as this strike has been avoided for now, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241203ekb800007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BOEING STRIKE ENDS UNION ACCEPTS NEW CONTRACT OFFER\b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, ELECTION, POLLS, EARLY VOTES\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, EXPLOSIVE DEVICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, SECURITY, YATES, RAFFENSPERGER, SKINNER, KRASNER\par \par \uc2 ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DECISION DAY IN THE RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS & TRUMP FIGHT TO THE FINISH AS POLLS OPEN\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLEGROUND NORTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE HELENE'S AFTERMATH NOT STOPPING VOTERS IN KEY STATE\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLEGROUND ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF THE TEN STATES WHERE ABORTION IS ON THE BALLOT\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOTING RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO KNOW BEFORE HEADING TO THE POLLS\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, ELECTION, PENNSYLVANIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS SPRINTS TO THE FINISH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VICE PRESIDENT MAKES FINAL PITCH TO VOTERS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ELECTION, PALM BEACH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S FINAL PUSH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT HITS THREE BATTLEGROUNDS\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE, NEGOTIATION, OFFER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING STRIKE ENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION ACCEPTS NEW CONTRACT OFFER\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're going to turn from politics now to the breaking news overnight. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  machinists voted to accept the company's contract offer in their\u160\'00\'A0strike. The walkout lasted 53 days. Let's bring back to our transportation correspondent, Gio Benitez, who has been tracking this for us. Good morning again, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning again. Yeah, this is big news for \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , which hasn't been able to build its most popular planes in nearly two months. That is now over, and those workers can go back to work as early as tomorrow. The new deal calls for a 38 percent general wage increase and a 401k match increase to 100 percent of the first eight percent of pay. Now, the new \uc2 Boeing\uc2  CEO, \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2 , said this was the biggest priority before handling \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's other issues, and this morning he sent the employees a message, saying the past months have been difficult but, quote, "We are part of the same team. We will only move forward by listening and working together. There is much work ahead to return to the excellence that made \uc2 Boeing\uc2  an iconic company." Of course, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has been in the spotlight after that door plug flew off the plane in January.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good to know that the strike is over after 50-plus days. Thank you, Gio.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241122ekb50003a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FINAL JOBS REPORT BEFORE THE ELECTION ONLY 12,000 JOBS ADDED IN OCTOBER, THE IMPACT OF WEAKER THAN EXPECTED NUMBERS\b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, TRUMP, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 FAKE, VIDEOS, RUSSIA, CHINA, IRAN\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Whit. And the economy remains one of the top issues in this campaign, so what impact will a weaker than expected jobs report, with just 12,000 jobs added, have on voters and the economy? Let's bring in ABC's Alexis Christoforous with more on this. Good morning, Alexis.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINAL JOBS REPORT BEFORE THE ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONLY 12,000 JOBS ADDED IN OCTOBER, THE IMPACT OF WEAKER THAN EXPECTED NUMBERS\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Gio. Those 12,000 jobs the economy added last month may seem shockingly low, especially when you consider estimates were for about 100,000 jobs added. But October was no usual month. The Labor Department says hurricanes Helene and Milton coupled with a major strike at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  likely distorted the numbers leading to the weakest month for job growth since December of 2020, but there was little impact from the strike or the hurricanes on the unemployment rate, which held steady at 4.1 percent, as wages rose slightly. Now the most jobs were added in health care and government last month, but more than 40,000 jobs were lost in manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's thanks in large part to that \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike. Now the report did give Wall Street a reason to rally. The Dow jumping nearly 300 points to kick off November. The NASDAQ climbing more than 140 and the S&P 500 added more than 20 points. Traders are betting the weak jobs report will keep the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  on track to cut interest rates by a quarter point at next week's meeting and give the fed a little room to continue lowering borrowing costs. Now this last jobs report before the election quickly becoming political fodder. The Biden administration saying the economy remains strong. The Trump campaign calling this report a catastrophe. Guys?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Alexis, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241121ekb200006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BOEING WORKERS REJECT CONTRACT OFFER SIX-WEEK STRIKE HAS ALREADY COST JET MAKER BILLIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 451 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 12 DAYS TO GO\par \par \uc2 2024, HARRIS, VOTERS, WALZ, KELLY, TRUMP, FASCIST, HITLER, MUSK, BACON, OSBORN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, KELLY, SHOOTINGS, CYBERATTACK, GEORGIA, VOTER, WEBSITE\par \par \uc2 WAR, UKRAINE, PUTIN, RUSSIA, KOREA, SOLDIERS, AUSTIN, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 BOEING, CONTRACT, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All right, Martha. Our thanks to you for your reporting. Now to breaking news overnight. Striking \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers have rejected the company's, company's latest contract offer. The vote comes as the aircraft maker reports a multibillion dollar loss in its most recent quarter. Trevor Ault joins us with those details. Good morning, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING WORKERS REJECT CONTRACT OFFER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX-WEEK STRIKE HAS ALREADY COST JET MAKER BILLIONS\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. So, this strike has already been ongoing for six weeks, and \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has lost billions of dollars in the process. This is the machinist union and overnight its 33,000 members voted at 64 percent to reject this most recent offer from \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , a 35 percent raise over the course of the four year contract and a $7,000 bonus for each member. The union said that they want 40 percent and they want pensions to be reinstated. And with this strike on going, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has already announced plans to soon lay off 17,000 workers. That is 10 percent of their global work force.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And as on top of that, in an earnings call they announced more than $6 billion in losses yesterday with executives saying that they expect the company is gonna be bleeding cash over the course of the next year. Now, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is still under an \uc2 FAA\uc2 -mandated manufacturing slowdown with added inspections after that door plug blew off an \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2  flight earlier this year. This, the CEO said public trust in the company has eroded and they have made serious mistakes and they need a culture change, but their machinists are still not going back to work. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: 7:32, DEADLY MCDONALD'S OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Trevor, thanks very much. Coming up, the E. coli outbreak at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's linked to its Quarter Pounder with the CDC warning there will be more cases.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7:34, MENENDEZ BROTHERS RESENTENCING\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, what the LA District Attorney is saying now about the Menendez brothers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7:41, LIAM PAYNE'S FINAL DAYS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Liam Payne's father in Argentina helping investigators determine what happened. But first, let's go to Sam who's in for Ginger. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241105ekao0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BLOCKBUSTER JOBS REPORT FUELS WALL STREET 254,000 JOBS ADDED, MUCH HIGHER THAN EXPECTED JOBLESS RATE FALLS\b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HELENE, AFTERMATH, SEARCH AND RESCUE\par \par \uc2 STORM\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, TRUMP, HARRIS, JOBS REPORT, LABOR\par \par \uc2 WAR, MIDDLE EAST, \uc2 IDF\par \par \uc2 WAR, MIDDLE EAST, IRAN, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 PASSENGER, PLANE\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the economy and Wall Street celebrating a much better than expected jobs report. ABC's Alexis Christoforous is here now with the details and what this could mean for interest rates. Alexis, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLOCKBUSTER JOBS REPORT FUELS WALL STREET\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 254,000 JOBS ADDED, MUCH HIGHER THAN EXPECTED, JOBLESS RATE FALLS\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. Wall Street cheered that blockbuster jobs report, giving investors confidence about the health of the economy. The Dow industrials shot up more than 340 points to close at a record high,, and the S&P 500, which is tied to many Americans' retirement plans, climbed 219 points. The Labor Department said the economy added 254,000 jobs last month, significantly more than the 150,000 expected, and the largest increase we've seen since March.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT JOBS REPORT SHOWS ABOUT ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE EFFECT ON FEDERAL RESERVE'S NEXT INTEREST RATE MOVE\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The unemployment rate ticked down to 4.1 percent. Employers added the most jobs at bars and restaurants, construction, health care, and government. Now, that strong jobs report suggests the US may be headed for that soft landing after all in which inflation returns to normal levels while the economy avoids a recession. It may also slow the pace of rate cuts from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 . Investors are now betting the fed will reduce rates by just a quarter point at November's meeting instead of that half point cut we saw last month. Guys?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Aiming for that soft landing. Alexis, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241022eka500008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOCKWORKERS GOING BACK TO WORK UNIONS SAYS THEY'VE REACHED A DEAL TO SUSPEND STRIKE THROUGH JANUARY 15TH\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK TO WORK\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, UNION, DOCKWORKERS, CONTRACT, PORTS, SUPPLY\par \par \uc2 NICHOLS, OFFICERS, CONVICTED, CRUMP, LOZIER\par \par \uc2 HELENE, AFTERMATH, MISSING, DEATHS, VOLUNTEERS, ADKINS\par \par \uc2 CAMPAIGN, CHENEY, HARRIS, RALLY, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, LEBANON, AIRSTRIKES, DEAD, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 METS, COMEBACK, BREWERS, MLB\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, RESENTENCING, GASCON, MURDERS, EVIDENCE, GERAGOS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MEDICAL, CRUISE, PARKER, WEISS, AIRLIFTED\par \par \uc2 AIR TAXIS, \uc2 JOBY\uc2 , BEVIRT, UBER, GOLDSTEIN, WHITAKER\par \par \uc2 HELENE, VOLUNTEERS, CLARKSON, PILOTS, FOOD, COLEMAN, BEECHAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC HEAT\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're gonna start with the top stories breaking at 8 right now, including that breaking news overnight on the dock workers strike. The union has reached a deal to suspend the walkout until January 15th to allow time to negotiate a new contract. Elizabeth Schulze is in Bayonne, New Jersey with the details. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCKWORKERS GOING BACK TO WORK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION SAYS THEY'VE REACHED A DEAL TO SUSPEND STRIKE THROUGH JANUARY 15TH\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George. Ports like these that bring in more than half of the nation's imports are now back up and running after they were at a standstill for three days. This tentative agreement between the union and the shipping industry group will suspend the dock workers strike and keep negotiations going until January 15th. Sources familiar with these negotiations tell us that wages will go up by 62 percent over the new six year contract. It's not as much as the union wanted, but a lot more than the shipping companies had originally offered.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So base pay for a top dock worker will go from $39 to $63 an hour. This deal means that all of those shipments of fresh fruit, clothes, car parts, medicine should soon be off of container ships and onto trucks to be delivered. That is a win for consumers and businesses. We shouldn't expect to see any major shipping delays or higher prices because of this strike during the holiday shopping season. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Elizabeth. That's gonna make everybody happy with that news. Thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241023eka40000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOCKWORKERS GOING BACK TO WORK UNION SAYS THEY'VE REACHED A DEAL TO SUSPEND STRIKE THROUGH JANUARY 15TH\b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK TO WORK\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, UNION, DOCKWORKERS, CONTRACT, PORTS, SUPPLY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to begin though with that breaking news overnight. The dock workers strike. The union has reached a deal to suspend the walkout until January 15th. They'll have time to renegotiate a contract. Elizabeth Schulze starts us off in Bayonne, New Jersey. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCKWORKERS GOING BACK TO WORK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION SAYS THEY'VE REACHED A DEAL TO SUSPEND STRIKE THROUGH JANUARY 15TH\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Ports like all along the East and Gulf Coast are back up and running after they shut down for three days during that massive dock workers strike. The union and the shipping industry group reaching a tentative agreement to suspend the strike until January 15th. Sources familiar with the negotiations tell us that wages will go up by 62% in this new six year contract.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is not as much as the union wanted, but a lot more than shipping companies originally offered. In dollar amounts, base pay for a top dock worker will go from $39 an hour to $63. And that's about $131,000 per year. Many dockworkers earn more than that after bonuses and overtime. President Biden is applauding this agreement. We're told he called the union's leader Harold Daggett this week to express support for the workers.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Both sides will now have until January to negotiate other sticking points like protections against the use of automated machines. But cargo will be start to be loaded off and on all of those ships were piling up, that were piling off. This is welcome relief for consumers and businesses who escaped the threat of delayed shipping times and higher prices during the holidays. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241023eka400002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JOBS REPORT BEATS EXPECTATIONS HARRIS ADDRESSES UNION WORKERS AFTER PORT STRIKE ENDS\b0\par\par\uc2 927 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HARRIS, BIDEN, TRUMP, JOBS REPORT, ECONOMY, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening. And it's great to have you with us. We made it to Friday. We have a lot to get to tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The devastation after Hurricane Helene. We are watching yet another system tonight that could bring up to a foot of rain. Meteorologist Cecily Tynan is here are. And what Dolly Parton has done in the storm zone tonight, the whole effort remarkable.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOBS REPORT BEATS EXPECTATIONS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we begin tonight with the economy and this blockbuster new jobs report. The new numbers blowing past expectations. The stock market tonight hitting a new all-time record.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOBS REPORT SEPTEMBER\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) 254,000 new jobs created in September, unemployment now falling to 4.1%. The July and August jobs numbers already revised, up by 72,000 new jobs. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  celebrating with union workers today in the key battleground state of Michigan, fueled by the economic news in these final 32 days of the campaign. Former President Trump visiting the storm zone in battleground Georgia. How he responded when asked about the encouraging jobs numbers.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ABC's Rachel Scott leading us off from the battleground of Georgia tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS ADDRESSES UNION WORKERS AFTER PORT STRIKE ENDS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With 32 days until the election and the economy the number one issue, tonight, the new jobs report beating expectation. The stock market gaining over 300 points, closing at another record high late today. Americans' 401 (k) s are growing with the market hitting dozens of record highs this year. All of this coupled with the news that inflation is slowing and the Fed is lowering rates. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in front of union workers in battleground Michigan making the case she will be the president for American workers.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's track record is a disaster for working people. And he's trying to gaslight people all over our country. But we know the facts and we know the truth. He is an existential threat to America's labor movement.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Harris, fueled by the economic news at the development overnight, the Biden administration working to the dockworkers strike that could have raised prices for American families in the coming weeks. Tonight, that crisis also averted.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN TAKES VICTORY LAP IN RARE WH BRIEFING APPEARANCE\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Hey, folks.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a rare moment, President Biden surprising recorders in the briefing room, taking a victory lap on an improving economy.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Once again, outside experts were wrong. Inflation has come down. Wages have gone up faster than prices. Interest rates are down.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The new blockbuster jobs report showing stronger-than-expected hiring across the US Economy. Restaurants, health care, state and local governments, and construction, adding tens of thousands of workers with wages going up, too. The unemployment rate ticking down to 4.1%. Economists say another very encouraging sign. I asked Trump today about the state of the economy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ASKED IF ECONOMY IS IMPROVING, TRUMP SAYS "NO"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Jobs are up, the stock market hit that all-time high. Do you acknowledge that the economy is improving?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 No, it's not. It's, inflation has devastated our economy. It's one of the big problems we have.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The former president back in the battleground state of Georgia. This time side-by-side with Republican Governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , who he once attacked for refusing to help him overturn the results of the 2020 election in Georgia. Their first public appearance together in four years. Tonight, President Biden was pressed if he's concerned about whether this election will be peaceful.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you have confidence that it will be a free and fair election and that it will be peaceful?\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Two separate questions. I'm confident it will be free and fair. I don't know whether it will be peaceful. The things that Trump has said and the things that he said last time out when he didn't like the outcome of the election were very dangerous. If you notice, I noticed that the vice presidential Republican candidate did not say he'd accept the outcome of the election. They haven't even accepted the outcome of the last election. So, I, I'm concerned about what they're going to do.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Today, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he can only hope that this election would be free and fair. He would not answer if he believes it would remain peaceful. Tomorrow, the former president heads to Butler, Pennsylvania, that exact rally location where there was an attempt on his life nearly three months ago.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As for the Harris campaign, next week, former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  gets out on the campaign trail for Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . He'll be doing a blitz through the battleground states starting in all-important Pennsylvania. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott leading us off on a Friday night. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241009eka400002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOCKWORKER STRIKE AGREEMENT TO SUSPEND STRIKE UNTIL JANUARY 15\b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NICHOLS, VERDICT, BEAN, HALEY, SMITH, WELLS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MELANIA TRUMP DEFENDS ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, CHENEY, SPRINGSTEEN, ENDORSEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHENEY CAMPAIGNING WITH HARRIS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, SHORES, SCHUMACHER, INGRAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT RELIEF EFFORTS; OVER 200 DEATHS\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, STRIKE, AGREEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, there's also breaking news at this hour involving that dock workers strike that has crippled shipping all along the East Coast and the Gulf, in fact. There is late word coming in at this hour that the union is suspending the strike until at least January 15th. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze live with us tonight. Elizabeth, what have you learned?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCKWORKER STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGREEMENT TO SUSPEND STRIKE UNTIL JANUARY 15\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, sources familiar with these negotiations tell us that the union and the shipping industry group have reached a tentative agreement that will suspend this strike until January 15th.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This agreement covers wages. Both sides would then return to the negotiating table to resolve their outstanding issues in January. We've seen this strike stretch three days, 47,000 dockworkers walked off the job for the first time in nearly 50 years. And shipping at more than a dozen ports all along the eastern gulf coast has been at a standstill.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those shipments should now be able to resume. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, hopefully that's relief for both the workers and the millions of Americans who are bracing for higher prices in the coming weeks. Elizabeth Schulze with the breaking news. Thank you, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241007eka30002y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MASSIVE STRIKE SHUTS DOWN U.S. PORTS DOCKWORKER WALKOUT THREATENS TO CRIPPLE SUPPLY CHAINS NATIONWIDE\b0\par\par\uc2 670 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP DEBATE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, WALZ, VANCE, JAN 6TH, ABORTION, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 WALZ, VANCE, DEBATE, TAKEAWAYS, CAMPAIGNS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, MISSILES, RETALIATION, CRATERS, TERRORISTS\par \par \uc2 IRAN, MISSILES, ATTACK, ISRAEL, TROOPS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, MISSILES, RESPONSE, ESCALATION\par \par \uc2 HELENE, MISSING, SEARCH, DEATHS, BIDEN, DAMAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OCTOBER HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 COMBS, ALLEGATIONS, BUZBEE, LAWSUITS, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 AMOS, "GOOD TIMES", "ROOTS", LEGACY, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 MICROSOFT\uc2 , AI, CO-PILOT, QUI, EMOTIONAL\par \par \uc2 WNBA, PLAYOFFS, LYNX, SUN, LIBERTY, ACES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 WALZ, VANCE, DEBATE, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 WAR, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 DOCK WORKER, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're gonna turn now to the port strike that threatens to cripple US supply chains. Tens of thousands of dock workers walked off the job Tuesday at ports from Texas to Maine, and the ripple effects will be felt nationwide. Elizabeth Schulze is at the port of New York and New Jersey. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE STRIKE SHUTS DOWN U.S. PORTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCKWORKER WALKOUT THREATENS TO CRIPPLE SUPPLY CHAINS NATIONWIDE\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. We are now in day 2 of this massive strike. And union dock workers here tell us they will stay on the picket line for as long as it takes to get a fair contract. This is one of 14 major shipping hubs where no cargo right now is moving in or out. This strike could cost the economy billions of dollars a day. Containers full of products like fresh fruit, clothes, auto parts, even medicine cannot be loaded on or off ships. One supply chain analyst at \uc2 Everstream Analytics\uc2  tells me that there are now at least 45 vessels waiting to dock along the eastern Gulf Coast. There were just three on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have already seen some major retailers like \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 Costco\uc2  divert shipments to other ports on the west coast to make sure that their shelves stay stocked during the holidays. The Biden administration is now ramping up the pressure on shipping companies to offer higher wages to the union. Members here tell us that they are also demanding limits on the use of automated machinery that they fear could replace their jobs. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Elizabeth, thanks. Coming up on our "GMA" Morning Menu, the new warning about possible severe health issues for kids who take medications for ADHD and anxiety.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also the new movie about Patrice and Garry. They want to get married, but if they do, the government benefits they need to live on would be cut. You do not want to miss their story.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "PATRICE: THE MOVIE"\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus Lori Bergamotto getting our denim look on point for the fall. And Will Reeve is with a special guest. Hey, Will.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FALL DENIM GUIDE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PETER KRAUSE LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey there, Michael. I'm here with Peter Krause, the star of 911. He's played a firefighter, a funeral director, a lawyer, a teacher and a sports anchor. Of those jobs, which would you want in real life?\par \par \uc2 PETER KRAUSE ("9-1-1")\par \par \uc2 Sports anchor.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sports anchor\par \par \uc2 PETER KRAUSE ("9-1-1")\par \par \uc2 Certainly over funeral director.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it's a good one.\par \par \uc2 PETER KRAUSE ("9-1-1")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You should talk to Robin about being a sports anchor. She knows some people.\par \par \uc2 PETER KRAUSE ("9-1-1")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's coming up right here on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "GMA," everybody. Tomorrow, Tory Johnson is here with a Deals and Steals fan favorite. Everything is $20 and under. So make sure you get ready for that. George?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOMORROW ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS: $20 & UNDER!\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241019eka20000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOCKWORKERS GO ON STRIKE THOUSANDS WALK OFF THE JOB, SHUTTING DOWN PORTS\b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, VELOZ, DAGGETT, RHEE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, OWENBY, NORWOOD, CRISWELL, RAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESPERATE SEARCH & RESCUE MISSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE'S DEATH TOLL RISES WITH HUNDREDS STILL UNACCOUNTED FOR\par \par \uc2 STORM, TRACK, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TROPICAL THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE STORM FORMING THAT COULD HIT THE GULF COAST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BIDEN, HARRIS, HURRICANE HELENE, ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES RESPOND TO HURRICANE DISASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS BRIEFED BY FEMA OFFICIALS; PRESIDENT BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 WALZ, VANCE, DEBATE, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO THE VICE PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO EXPECT WHEN WALZ & VANCE FACE OFF TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, BIDEN, NETANYAHU, HAGARI\par \par \uc2 ROSE, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BASEBALL GREAT PETE ROSE PASSES AWAY AT 83\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MLB'S ALL-TIME HITS LEADER WAS BANNED FOR GAMBLING ON THE GAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, JOHNSON, BONE CANCER, SHIP\par \par \uc2 KORS, MERGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LUXURY MERGER LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FTC\uc2  FIGHTS PLAN TO BRING UPSCALE FASHION BRANDS TOGETHER\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SALES FORECAST, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY SHOPPING SALES FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHEN & WHERE TO SCORE THE BIGGEST DEALS\par \par \uc2 KNUDSEN, BREAST CANCER, STATISTICS, REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS ON BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY RELEASES NEW STATISTICS REPORT\par \par \uc2 JONES, MARQUEZ, WEDDING, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWER IN PINK, 8:14\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First a look at the top stories breaking at 8:00. We start with the tens of thousands of dock workers who walked off the job just after midnight. The strike threatens the nation's supply chains, could lead to higher prices, possible shortages. Ports from Maine to Texas are impacted. Want to go back to Elizabeth Schulze at the port of New York and New Jersey. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, George. This is the first time in nearly 50 years that tens of thousands of those union - dock workers all along the east and Gulf Coast have gone on strike. Workers here told us they showed up just at midnight when the \uc2 International Longshoremen's Association\uc2  announced the strike and the union president says they will not leave until they get a fair deal. Despite these 11th hour negotiations, there was not a deal between the US Maritime Alliance and the union over a six year contract. The union wants a 77% wage increase, limits on the use of automated machines.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTL LONGSHOREMEN'S ASSOCIATION DEMANDS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The alliance has responded with a nearly 50% pay hike. So what this means is that 14 ports that handle more than half of the cargo that comes into the US are now at a virtual standstill. That means products like groceries, clothes, machinery, will not be loaded on or off container ships. This strike could be crippling for the US economy depending on how long it lasts. A weeklong strike expected to cost $7.5 billion. Many companies have been stock piling and rerouting their shipments to west coast ports to make sure their shelves are stocked ahead of the holiday shopping season. Every day the strike goes on, it could take six days to clear the backlog. The White House said it is closely working with both parties trying to negotiate a deal fairly and quickly. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it's a little bit, a lot of disruption there. Thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241010eka10003a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOCKWORKERS GO ON STRIKE THOUSANDS WALK OFF JOB, SHUTTING PORTS FROM NEW ENGLAND TO TEXAS\b0\par\par\uc2 584 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, VELOZ, DAGGETT, RHEE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we're going to begin with breaking news overnight. Tens of thousands of dockworkers walking off the job just after midnight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCKWORKERS GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OFF JOB, SHUTTING PORTS FROM NEW ENGLAND TO TEXAS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike threatens the nation's supply chain and could lead to higher prices and possible shortages. Ports from Maine to Texas, like the ones you're see live right now, are being impacted. Elizabeth Schulze starts us off at the vital Port of New York and New Jersey. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Michael. Hundreds of union workers tell us they are demanding a fair contract, and the union's president says that they will stay on strike until they get that. Until then, busy shipping hub likes the Port of New York and New Jersey here, the busiest one East Coast, are at a virtual standstill.\par \par \uc2 HAROLD DAGGETT (PRESIDENT INTERNATIONAL LONGSHOREMEN'S ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 Nothing's going to move without us. Nothing.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, tens of thousands of union dockworkers in more than a dozen ports from Maine to Texas are off the job and on the picket line.\par \par \uc2 YAKELIN VELOZ (STRIKING WORKER)\par \par \uc2 We're here to support for going forward the future. No automation. We want to secure our jobs.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At midnight, the International Longshoreman's Association announcing its first strike in nearly 50 years after it failed to reach a new contract agreement with the US Maritime Alliance. During 11th hour negotiations, the union insisting on a 77% pay increase over six years, and limits on the use of automated machines. The shipping industry group responding with a nearly 50% pay hike.\par \par \uc2 HAROLD DAGGETT (PRESIDENT INTERNATIONAL LONGSHOREMEN'S ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 I want to tell you all what you're doing is right. This is going down in history, what we're doing here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCKWORKERS STRIKE\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fourteen vital ports that absorb more than half of the cargo shipped to the US from other countries are now at a standstill. Fresh fruit, clothes, machinery and medicine won't be loaded on or off container ships, potentially costing the American economy up to $7.5 billion in one week.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORK STOPPAGE COULD COST THE ECONOMY BILLIONS & RAISE PRICES\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Analysts say, for every day the strike lasts, it could take six days to clear the backlog. An echo supply chain bottlenecks during the pandemic. Retailers, like executive Kevin Rhee, says a strike lasting more than a couple weeks could force businesses like his to raise prices for customers.\par \par \uc2 KEVIN RHEE (FINANCIAL PLANNING EXECUTIVE)\par \par \uc2 If all the East Coast and the Gulf Coast ports are closed, businesses will be bringing things in from the West Coast, which will cause more congestion there. And you have to transport that all the way across the country. Ultimately, what that means is higher costs for consumer.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The union says it will still handle military cargo and cruises will run on schedule during the strike. The White House has just released a staple saying President Biden and Vice President Harris are closely monitoring any supply chain impacts. Robin?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Elizabeth, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241010eka10002u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PORT STRIKE COULD DRIVE PRICES HIGHER RETAILERS DIVERTING SHIPMENT WEST TO AVOID DISRUPTIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, BIDEN, AIRSTRIKE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, AIRSTRIKES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: IRANIAN MISSILE BARRAGE "DEFEATED"\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ISRAEL, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST CASTS SHADOW OVER VP DEBATE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, VELOZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PORT STRIKE COULD DRIVE PRICES HIGHER\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the meantime, we turn to the economy tonight, and to this crippling strike. Tens of thousands of union dockworkers up and down the East Coast and the Gulf walking off the job, threatening the nation's supply chain and, of course, then the prices you could potentially pay. Elizabeth Schulze from New Jersey again tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAILERS DIVERTING SHIPMENT WEST TO AVOID DISRUPTIONS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, crucial ports that fuel the American economy from new England to the Gulf Coast at a standstill, after tens of thousands of union dockworkers walked off the job.\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 If it's a fight they want, it's a fight they're going to get.\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 It's a fight they're going to get.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 International Longshoremen's Association\uc2  and the US Maritime Alliance failing to reach a deal, leaving ships sitting offshore in Texas, and shipping containers at some of the busiest hubs in the US idle just weeks before the holiday season. The impasse could cost the US billions of dollars a day and drive up consumer prices. Experts say, for every day the strike lasts, it could take nearly a week to clear the nearly a week to clear the backlog. Under the old contract, a dockworker could earn a typical salary of $100,000 per year. The union wants to boost pay to $177,000 annually over six years, and add protections against automated machines. Yakelin Veloz is a single mother working at the docks in New Jersey. Her three little girls joining her on the picket line.\par \par \uc2 YAKELIN VELOZ (DOCKWORKER)\par \par \uc2 Everything that comes into this country comes in through us. The supply that everyone, everyone receives daily, it comes through us. And we're not appreciated.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ahead of this strike, we have already seen major retailers like \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 Costco\uc2  divert some of their shipments to ports on the West Coast to avoid shortages during the holidays. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Elizabeth Schulze back with us tonight. Elizabeth, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241003eka10002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MASSIVE PORT STRIKE THREATENS U.S. SUPPLY CHAIN UNION SAYS DOCKWORKERS COULD WALK OFF JOB\b0\par\par\uc2 752 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUNNING AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 HELENE, DEVASTATION, COOPER, MISSING, RESCUES, SMATHERS\par \par \uc2 HELENE, COMMUNITIES, COASTAL, DEBRIS, DAMAGE, POWER\par \par \uc2 HELENE, REMNANTS, RAIN, FLOODING, TROPICS\par \par \uc2 EVACUATIONS, CHEMICAL, SMOKE, LEVETT, EVANS, MCDANIEL\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, CAMPAIGN, TRUMP, ATTACKS, HOGAN\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, STRIKES, LEBANON, YEMEN, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 NFL, RAVENS, BILLS, BADE, CHIEFS, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT POSSIBLE THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM: "JURASSIC PARK"\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, HELENE, BASCOME, DOG, COAST GUARD, HUDSON\par \par \uc2 KRISTOFFERSON, SINGER, SONGWRITING, ACTING, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 KEOUGH, PRESLEY, GRACELAND, "PEOPLE", MEMOIR\par \par \uc2 WNBA, PLAYOFFS, LIBERTY, ACES, CONNECTICUT, MINNESOTA\par \par \uc2 HELENE, SEARCH, RESCUE, DEVASTATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEATH TOLL RISING AMID HELENE'S DEVASTATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH EFFORTS UNDERWAY\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE, HELENE, SEARCH, MISSING, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTH CAROLINA REELING IN HELENE'S WAKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIRE NEED FOR SUPPLIES AMID URGENT SEARCH EFFORTS\par \par \uc2 PORT, STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, UNION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE PORT STRIKE THREATENS U.S. SUPPLY CHAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION SAYS DOCKWORKERS COULD WALK OFF JOB\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now with our "GMA" cover story, the impending port strike along the East Coast and Gulf that would force tens of thousands of dockworkers off the job and will potentially severely impact America's supply chain. Elizabeth Schulze is in Baltimore, has the latest for us. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. This could be the first time in nearly 50 years that the union representing dockworkers at ports like this one in Baltimore goes on strike, and it could have ripple effects across the supply chain, just in time for the holiday shopping season.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning ports from New England to Texas are bracing to grind to a standstill, at midnight tonight, up to 47,000 union dockworkers from the International Longshoremen's association set to walk off the job and go on strike.\par \par \uc2 HAROLD J. DAGGET (INTERNATIONAL LONGSHOREMEN'S ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 When my men hit the streets from Maine to Texas, every single port will lock down.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The union demanding a 77-percent wage increase over six years and limits on the use of automated machinery like cranes. The United States Maritime Alliance has responded, offering a 40 percent pay hike. With negotiations at an impasse, President Biden saying he won't get involved, saying unions have the right to strike and negotiate a fair deal.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Mr. President, would you intervene in the dockworkers strike if they go on strike Tuesday?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) If the strike moves forward, 14 ports along the East and Gulf Coast would be unable to load cargo on or off container ships, from autos arriving into Boston to fresh fruit ports in New York and Delaware to imports of machinery, appliances and electronics in Houston. In all, it could cost the American economy up to $7.5 billion per week. Lisa Ripken and her son, Eli run, a small toy store in Maryland. They generate a majority of their sales over the holidays.\par \par \uc2 LISA RIPKIN (FAIR DAY'S PLAY)\par \par \uc2 We have dolls coming in and more LEGO and lots of games. Just, it's just we go into a certain mode for Christmas.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They've already stocked shelves but rely on last-minute shipments for games or toys that sell faster than expected and fear a strike could increase those costs.\par \par \uc2 ELI RIPKIN (FAIR DAY'S PLAY)\par \par \uc2 If shipping costs go up, which they probably will, you know, we may have to raise our prices up even more. That's tough because the higher prices are, the less people want to buy our stuff.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You don't want to raise prices?\par \par \uc2 ELI RIPKIN (FAIR DAY'S PLAY)\par \par \uc2 We don't want to, but if it comes to that, we will have to.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The potential impact on your shipping times and cost depends how long this strike would last. A week-long strike could be resolved pretty quickly because retailers have had some time to prepare for this, with some diverting their shipments to West Coast ports, guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Someone letting you know what they feel about it. All right, hey.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot of activity already.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We can see that, Elizabeth. Thank you so much. Hope everything works out for everyone.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For sure.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241018ek9u0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TENSIONS RISING OVER LOOMING STRIKE DOCKWORKERS ACROSS 36 PORTS SET TO WALK OFF THE JOB\b0\par\par\uc2 522 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 HELENE, AFTERMATH, POWER, DEATHS, COOPER, FLOODING, DAMAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOWNS CUT OFF, 1M+ WITHOUT POWER\par \par \uc2 HELENE, REMNANTS, RAIN, FLOODING, TROPICS\par \par \uc2 FIRE PLANT, EVACUATIONS, SMOKE, CHEMICAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS AFTER CHEMICAL PLANT FIRE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, YEMEN, STRIKES, HEZBOLLAH, HOUTHI, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL LAUNCHES LARGE SCALE AIR OPERATION\par \par \uc2 IDF\uc2 , TARGETS, HEZBOLLAH, CONFLICT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 IDF\uc2  TARGETS DOZENS OF HEZBOLLAH SITES\par \par \uc2 SYRIA, \uc2 ISIS\uc2 , KILLED, MILITANTS, US\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 37 ISIS MILITANTS KILLED\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, HARRIS, ATTACKS, HOGAN, GRAHAM, FLAKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ATTACKS HARRIS FOR BORDER VISIT\par \par \uc2 SPACEX, STARLINER, ISS, WILSON, ASTRONAUTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS:: SPACEX MISSION TO RETRIEVE ASTRONAUTS\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, PORTS, STRIKE, DAGGETT, KIDD, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENSIONS RISING OVER LOOMING STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS ( ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ike for us. Thanks so much, Ike. Top Biden administration officials are urging the dock workers union and shipping industry to return to the negotiating table ahead of a looming strike. If the union does walk out at Midnight on Tuesday, the impact on the US economy could be catastrophic. Here's ABC's Reena Roy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENSIONS RISING OVER LOOMING STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCKWORKERS ACROSS 36 PORTS SET TO WALK OFF THE JOB\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, 45,000 dock workers on the East and Gulf Coast are preparing to walk off the job, and it could be devastating for the US economy. 14 ports from New England to Texas could shut down Tuesday at Midnight, up to 36 could be affected. Those crucial hubs responsible for nearly 35% of all US imports and exports.\par \par \uc2 HAROLD J DAGGETT (PRESIDENT INT'L LONGSHOREMEN'S ASSOC)\par \par \uc2 When my men hit the streets, from Maine to Texas, every single port are locked down.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 International Longshoremen's Association\uc2 , demanding higher hourly wages in their new contract and a ban on automated cranes, gates, and trucks. A prolonged strike could mean delayed shipping and higher prices for Americans on things like clothes, electronics, cars, and food like canned goods and fresh produce. The US economy would take a direct hit.\par \par \uc2 MARGARET KIDD (PROGRAM DIR SUPPLY CHAIN LOGISTICS TECH UNIV OF HOUSTON)\par \par \uc2 It's estimated that a strike would cost somewhere around $5 billion a day.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The US Maritime Alliance representing the shippers and ports says it's committed to negotiating, but claims the union is not bargaining in good faith. The Biden administration urging both sides to negotiate fairly and quickly.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Both sides have got to settle the strike. Support the collective bargaining effort, and I think they'll settle the strike.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, according to a senior White House official, Transportation Secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  and other top officials met with the alliance to deliver that message. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS ( ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Reena, thank you. There's still much more ahead on "World News Tonight" this Sunday, including late details on a deadly plane crash near the site that honors the Wright brothers' famous first flight. And a remarkable sight in the sky over the Golden Gate Bridge.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020241002ek9t0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PORT WORKERS SET TO STRIKE? POTENTIAL EFFECT ON SUPPLY CHAIN IF 45,000 WALK OUT, DEADLINE TUESDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 599 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE'S DEVASTATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CATASTROPHIC DAMAGE\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, FLOODING, PINDER, RESCUES\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE'S RAIN MOVES NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TROPICAL THREATS IN ATLANTIC OCEAN\par \par \uc2 NASRALLAH, HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, HAGARI, AIRSTRIKES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL & LEBANON TRADE AIRSTRIKES OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 33 PEOPLE KILLED IN BEIRUT, HEZBOLLAH CONFIRMS DEATH OF LEADER HASSAN NASRALLAH\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, NASRALLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAELI STRIKE KILLS HEZBOLLAH LEADER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEIGHTENED FEARS OF WIDER CONFLICT IN MIDEAST FOLLOWING DEATH OF HASSAN NASRALLAH\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, WALZ, ELECTION, IMMIGRATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP APPEARS AT GEORGIA VS. ALABAMA GAME, TIM WALZ HITS THE STANDS IN MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DAGGETT, KIDD, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PORT WORKERS SET TO STRIKE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POTENTIAL EFFECT ON SUPPLY CHAIN IF 45,000 WALK OUT, DEADLINE TUESDAY\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to 45,000 dock workers threatening to strike from Texas to Maine at some of the biggest ports in America. Their deadline is just after midnight into Tuesday. The big concern now, how much could this affect the supply chain? ABC's Reena Roy is in Bayonne, New Jersey right now with more. Good morning, Reena.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Gio, good morning to you. That's right. This strike could cost the American economy billions of dollars per day and potentially lead to massive shortages ahead of the holiday shopping season.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the clock is ticking with the potential strike looming at ports along the east and gulf coasts. 45,000 dock workers threatening to walk off the job Tuesday at midnight, which could have a major impact on the US Economy.\par \par \uc2 HAROLD J DAGGETT (PRESIDENT INTL LONGSHOREMAN'S ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 When my men hit the streets from Maine to Texas, every single port will lock down.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCK WORKERS DEMANDING\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The International Longshoreman's Association demanding higher hourly wages over the course of a new contract and a ban on automated cranes, gates, and trucks.\par \par \uc2 HAROLD J DAGGETT (PRESIDENT INTL LONGSHOREMAN'S ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 We have to fight for what we rightfully deserve. Let's get a contract, and let's move on with this world.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The US Maritime Alliance representing the ports says it is committed to negotiating, but claims the union is not bargaining in good faith.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POTENTIALLY IMPACTED PORTS\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) If both sides remain deadlocked, several of the nation's highest grossing ports could shut down, causing severe supply chain disruptions, and potentially costing the US economy billions of dollars a day.\par \par \uc2 MARGARET KIDD (SUPPLY CHAIN & LOGISTICS TECHNOLOGY UNIV OF HOUSTON)\par \par \uc2 It's estimated that a strike would cost somewhere around $5 billion a day. I mean, that would be the economic impact.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The east and gulf ports account for more than half of US container imports, facilitating the transport from everything from toys and fresh fruit to nuclear reactors. A weeks'-long strike could create supply chain challenges, driving up prices for things like produce, seafood, pharmaceuticals, electronics, and cars.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EFFECTS ON A LONG-TERM STRIKE\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And just to give you an idea of the impact, a 30-day strike could cost the New York-New Jersey port here alone, $640 million a day. Guys?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, my gosh. The numbers from those strikes and what it costs the economy. Reena, thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241002ek9t0002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BOEING WAGE TALKS BREAK OFF WITHOUT PROGRESS UNION REMAINS OPEN TO TALKS WITH BOEING, EITHER DIRECTLY OR MEDIATED\b0\par\par\uc2 155 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, DAMAGE, GEORGIA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, DAMAGE, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, DAMAGE, NORTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, LEADER, NASRALLAH\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meanwhile, negotiations to end the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers strike took a turn for the worse Friday. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  saying talks are at a standstill as the strike enters its third week. The Machinists Union negotiation team and \uc2 Boeing\uc2  representatives were in federal mediation Friday, but no new contracts that both sides could agree on came out of those talks. Economists estimate the strike has cost \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers and shareholders more than a billion dollars so far, and there is no end in sight. Major impacts.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING WAGE TALKS BREAK OFF WITHOUT PROGRESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION REMAINS OPEN TO TALKS WITH BOEING, EITHER DIRECTLY OR MEDIATED\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241016ek9s00030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UNION REJECTS BOEING OFFER STRIKING MACHINISTS DEMAND BETTER PAY AND BONUSES\b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, STORM SURGE, FLASH FLOODING, TRACK, WIND\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, AIRSTRIKES, LEBANON, NETANYAHU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEARS OF WIDER MIDEAST WAR ESCALATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNDREDS KILLED, THOUSANDS FLEE AS ISRAEL INTENSIFIES STRIKES ON HEZBOLLAH IN LEBANON\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, HEZBOLLAH, AIRSTRIKES, LEBANON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEARS OF WIDER MIDEAST WAR ESCALATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ADDITIONAL U.S. TROOPS DEPLOYING TO REGION AS ISRAEL & HEZBOLLAH TRADE STRIKES\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, UKRAINE, UNITED NATIONS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE HEATS UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP KICKS OFF BATTLEGROUND BLITZ AS HARRIS HEADS TO SOUTHERN LEBANON\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ROUTH, LETTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ASSASSINATION ATTEMPT SUSPECT IN COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROSECUTORS SHARE CHILLING NEW EVIDENCE FROM GOLF COURSE INCIDENT\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , AIR TRAFFIC CONTROLLERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION REJECTS BOEING OFFER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRIKING MACHINISTS DEMAND BETTER PAY AND BONUSES\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the latest on the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike. The union rejecting the latest offer. Trevor Ault is tracking this for us. Good morning, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. This is a really big deal. We believe this has already cost \uc2 Boeing\uc2  about half billion dollars, and it's still ongoing. They might be at an impasse. The union for the machinists on strike has rejected \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's offer.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It includes a 30% raise over four years. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  calls this its best and final offer. But the union had asked for 40%. And they say this supposed final offer misses the mark. So, this strike has halted production on many \uc2 Boeing\uc2  jets. It's now on day 11. It's estimated to cost $50 million per day.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And who knows when it might end.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Who knows? Who knows?\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we do know that there's some news when it comes to the air traffic controllers shortage.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FAA\uc2  HITS AIR TRAFFIC CONTROLLER HIRING GOALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGENCY SAYS IT STILL NEEDS MORE STAFF TO COVER SHORTAGE\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Air traffic controllers. Absolutely, yeah. It's something we've been reporting on for some time. The \uc2 FAA\uc2  had said, way back in the spring, they were short about 3,000 air traffic controllers, which is a huge number.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But they say they've made major progress here and exceeded their hiring goals. They've hired more than 1,800 in 2024 so far. In April, of course, Congress passed a plan to help increase controller pay. That's a big reason behind being able to hire so many more people.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But this shortage had been linked to delays and a number of close calls on airport runways. There's still a shortage, but it is smaller than what it used to be.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, it's encouraging.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Trevor, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241009ek9o0008k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INVESTING ON A TIGHT BUDGET GROWING YOUR WEALTH LIVING PAYCHECK TO PAYCHECK\b0\par\par\uc2 984 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENSIVE STRIKES\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, LEBANON, HEZBOLLAH, STRIKES, HAGARI\par \par \uc2 ISRAELI, HEZBOLLAH, TENSIONS, STRIKES, DEATH TOLL\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, VICTIMS, INJURED, THURMOND, ESLAMI, WOODFIN\par \par \uc2 TROPICAL, RAIN, WINDS, GULF\par \par \uc2 CAMPAIGNS, HARRIS, TRUMP, DEBATE, POLLS, ROBINSON\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, ILLNESS, TRIP, EVENTS\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , MAHOMES, EAGLES, RAVENS, VIKINGS, BRONCOS, SEAHAWKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRONG TO SEVERE STORMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "FROZEN"\par \par \uc2 COMBS, ARREST, VIDEO, AGNIFILO, LINDSAY\par \par \uc2 SLEEPWALKING, PEYTON, WOODS, RECUE, THERMAL, PARKER, KLOBER\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, SMART HEART, CPR, AEDS, YOUTH, ATHLETES\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , DOUBLEHEADER, BENGALS, JAGUARS, BILLS, COMMANDERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTUMN HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOT WEEK AHEAD\par \par \uc2 ATTACKS, ISRAEL, LEBANON, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL LAUNCHES "EXTENSIVE STRIKES" INTO LEBANON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 IDF\uc2  TARGETS HEZBOLLAH STRONGHOLDS AFTER ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 JUDGE, SHOOTING, CHAMBER, FUNERAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR MOTIVE IN SMALL TOWN MYSTERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FUNERAL HELD FOR JUDGE GUNNED DOWN IN CHAMBER\par \par \uc2 WILSON, \uc2 WNBA\uc2 , CLARK, PLAYOFFS, BASKETBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WNBA PLAYOFFS TIP OFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAITLIN CLARK MAKES PLAYOFF IN QUEST FOR THREE-PEAT\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTARY, TEENS, SOCIAL MEDIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DOCUMENTARY ON TEENS & SOCIAL MEDIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW IT HAS RESHAPED CHILDHOOD FOR A GENERATION\par \par \uc2 MUNN, MULANEY, TV, SPARKS\par \par \uc2 SKINCARE, HAIRCARE, BEAUTY, SHOPPING, DEALS\par \par \uc2 "NOBODY WANTS THIS", BELL, BRODY, TV\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KRISTEN BELL & ADAM BRODY LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 INVESTING, BUDGET, ECONOMICS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INVESTING ON A TIGHT BUDGET\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING YOUR WEALTH LIVING PAYCHECK TO PAYCHECK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with our "Money Smart" series with ways to plan financially for the future. This morning, how to invest to make your money work for you no matter your income. Rebecca, you're going to start us off with people because sometimes, you know, it's really tight for a lot of folks.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is really tight for a lot of folks, Robin, and guys, I get this question all the time for viewers. Their biggest question is, "How do I get started, especially when I am on a budget?" Well, this is how.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When a mother of four thought about investing, she was living on a tight budget.\par \par \uc2 ALYSHIA RUSHING (INVESTOR)\par \par \uc2 Living paycheck to paycheck was a normal thing, so finding time or the extra money to save was, like, a hard thing to do.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, she started slow, with just $20, and gradually increased it as her income went up.\par \par \uc2 ALYSHIA RUSHING (INVESTOR)\par \par \uc2 I think a lot of people are always, are sitting back and thinking, like, "I need hundreds of thousands of dollars," and that's definitely not the case when it comes to investing.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Alyshia used the app Acorns to start. It's one of many available to consumers. Another, \uc2 Robinhood\uc2 . Their head of investment strategy, Stephanie Guild, gave us some tips. She recommends building at least three months of emergency savings before you start investing. Next, figure out your goals.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE GUILD (ROBINHOOD)\par \par \uc2 Write down, like, what you want this to do for you. That can be, I'm going to save for a home, I'm going to save for a vacation or even something longer term, like I want to save for my retirement. And once you have an account open, you can start even with a small amount.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And finally, diversify by not investing everything in one company.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE GUILD (ROBINHOOD)\par \par \uc2 An exchange-traded fund is sometimes a good way to get started. When you go buy the 10-pack of multicolored socks, and that's how I think about an ETF, you buy one thing, and it gives you exposure to lots of different stocks underlying it.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As for Alyshia, her investment has grown by about $2,000 and she started six months ago, and she plans to keep going.\par \par \uc2 ALYSHIA RUSHING (INVESTOR)\par \par \uc2 Investing is the priority right now, like, something I'm going to do is invest in something.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what I really love about this is how Alyshia did it. She started small. So if you automate and make small regular contributions, $10 or $20 a paycheck, over time it really grows. And then you want to use the windfalls wisely, if you get a tax refund, an inheritance, maybe you make a return and get a little money back, bank it, put it towards your retirement. And then finally, talk to your employer. A number of employers have free counseling that really can walk you through this. And I just want to really double down on the idea of starting small. If you started 22 years old, put $10 every two weeks into an IRA or 401 (k), invested in stock, so, like, an S&P 500 index fund, by the time you are 67 years old, you will have over $74,000. And that's because of compound interest in starting early. And you were just saying\u160\'00\'A0you started early.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I remember being in elementary school, and I wanted a Schwinn, you know, with the banana seat and all that.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The handlebars.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, the handlebars, the high rise. I remember opening my first savings account, that was in, and it's just something that's stayed with me.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bring the piggy bank as a mom and dad, and grown-ups.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was your first savings account? Do you remember?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I had one when I was, like, 10.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I loved it. I love the bank.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, right, right, exactly.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It felt such an accomplishment, going to the...\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the candy at the bank. That's really good, too.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241009ek9n0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 33,000 BOEING MACHINISTS ON STRIKE UNION MEMBERS REJECTED TENTATIVE DEAL\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 WAR IN UKRAINE, BIDEN, STARMER, ZELENSKYY\par \par \uc2 TIMBERLAKE, DWI\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, CONCUSSION, \uc2 NFL\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STARLINER, WILMORE, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES\par \par \uc2 SPHERE, UFC 306\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP OF "HOCUS POCUS"\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE FOOTBALL, HOWARD, "COLLEGE GAMEDAY"\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 EMMY NOMINEES\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, CAMPAIGN, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLEGROUND BLITZ IN THE RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP HARRIS STOPS IN PA, TRUMP IN THE WEST\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE, UNION, DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 33,000 BOEING MACHINISTS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION MEMBERS REJECTED TENTATIVE DEAL\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now we're going to turn\u160\'00\'A0to the striking workers at \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , hitting the picket lines, rejecting the company's pay increase offer. And ABC's Morgan Norwood is here now. Morgan, the two sides seem to be very far apart.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely, we're talking about more turbulent times for \uc2 Boeing\uc2  with the US economy caught in the crosshairs. I mean, we're bracing for impact here because 33,000 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  union members are walking off the job, they're now on the picket lines, and they're on strike, rejecting the troubled jet maker's latest offer that would have hiked pay by 25 percent over four years. Now, workers say \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's proposal, especially with inflation, just wasn't going to cut it. They're also demanding a return to pension plans.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But this strike comes as a fresh blow to the company after it suffered two fatal plane crashes and a door panel flying off mid-flight, a problem-riddled spacecraft that just recently spacecraft that was recently forced to leave two astronauts behind at the International Space Station. But with the strike, production of \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's popular 737 Max and 777s coming to a screeching halt. And depending on how long the strike carries on, it could cost the US economy tens of billions of dollars. As Gio pointed out, both sides still far apart but set to return to the negotiating table early next week, Janai.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Boeing\uc2  still making those headlines. Thank you, Morgan, for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241002ek9e0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 33,000 BOEING MACHINISTS ON STRIKE UNION REJECTED TENTATIVE DEAL, COMPANY COULD LOSE OVER $100M PER DAY\b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike. 33,000 workers off the job this morning after rejecting a tentative contract with the aerospace giant. The strike could cost the company billions as it faces a series of major setbacks. ABC's Morgan Norwood is here with the latest. Morgan, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 33,000 BOEING MACHINISTS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION MEMBERS REJECTED TENTATIVE DEAL, COMPANY COULD LOSE OVER $100M PER DAY\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Whit. That's right. More turbulence for \uc2 Boeing\uc2 . Both sides are eager to get a deal done here, but until then, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is set to be hemorrhaging more than $100 million a day with concern now about their bottom line and what that could mean for the world's second largest plane manufacturer. But one thing is for certain, the US economy will take a hit.\par \par \uc2 BOEING WORKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Strike, strike, strike.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the US economy bracing for impact after 33,000 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  union members walked off the job and to the picket lines on strike and rejecting the troubled jet maker's latest offer that would have hiked pay by 25 percent over four years.\par \par \uc2 JAMES MANN (BOEING EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 The first thing I saw right off the bat was a 25 percent raise over a four year period. That's not going to catch up with my, my rent and my bills.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the first strike in 16 years and workers say it's been that long since they've had a raise, but say \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's proposal, especially with inflation, just wasn't going to cut it. They're also demanding a return to pension plans.\par \par \uc2 CARLA BERRY (EMPLOYEE AT THE MATERIAL INTEGRATION CENTER AT BOEING)\par \par \uc2 It's, you know, difficult and with the economy right now, it's rough.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Carla Barry is a longtime \uc2 Boeing\uc2  employee. Her daughter, Andrea, also worked for the company. The two now becoming food delivery workers to make ends meet until there's a deal.\par \par \uc2 ANDREA BERRY (FORMER EMPLOYEE AT BOEING)\par \par \uc2 That is how we're going to be able to go and make it so that we can make up that extra money to be able to make sure we can survive during this time.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike comes as a fresh blow to \uc2 Boeing\uc2  after it suffered two fatal plane crashes, a door panel flying off mid-flight, and a problem-riddled spacecraft that was forced to leave two astronauts behind at the International Space Station. The financial impact to \uc2 Boeing\uc2  will be steep. The strike is expected to cost the company approximately $108 million per day. Its CFO saying on Friday the strike will impact production, deliveries, and operations, and will jeopardize recovery.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING STRIKE RESPONSE\par \par \uc2 BRIAN WEST\uc2  (CFO AT BOEING)\par \par \uc2 We want to get back to table, and we want to reach an agreement that's good for our people.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And depending on how long this strike carries on, it could cost the US economy tens of billions of dollars. Both sides set to return to the negotiating table early next week, the White House say they're encouraging both sides to hash it out in good faith. Janai?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That daily figure for what it will cost \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is staggering. Morgan, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241002ek9e00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BOEING WORKERS GO ON STRIKE 33,000 UNION MEMBERS WALK OFF JOB AFTER REJECTING JETMAKER'S CONTRACT OFFER\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING STRIKE\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE, WORKERS, HOLDEN, PENSION, HARTEVELDT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are looking forward to that, Robin. First our top story, another big hit for \uc2 Boeing\uc2 . 30,000 workers walked off the job overnight, which could pose serious problems for the already troubled company. Alex Perez is on the scene at the main \uc2 Boeing\uc2  plant in Washington State. Good morning, Alex.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING WORKERS GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 33,000 UNION WORKERS WALK OFF JOB AFTER REJECTING JETMAKER'S CONTRACT OFFER\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, George. Workers hit the picket lines here at Midnight. It remains unclear just how long this strike will last. But tens of thousands of employees voted, and 96% said they support this strike.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, 33,000 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  union members walking off the job.\par \par \uc2 BOEING WORKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Strike. Strike.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The company now bracing for production shutdowns after union members overwhelmingly rejected the latest contract offered by the troubled aviation company.\par \par \uc2 JON HOLDEN (PRESIDENT IAM DISTRICT 751)\par \par \uc2 This is about respect. This is about addressing the past. And this is about fighting for our future.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Aircraft assembly workers, mainly here in Seattle, turning down \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's latest deal in which they offered a 25% pay raise over four years. But workers demanding more, claiming they haven't had a raise in 16 years.\par \par \uc2 BOEING WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I've been here for 37 years and it's historically one of the worst contracts.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The union's initial demand was for a 40% raise over three years and a return to pensions instead of 401k contributions. \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's new CEO saying in a statement, "I know that we can get back on track, but a strike would put our shared recovery in jeopardy."\par \par \uc2 BOEING WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 And after the last losing our pension, I'm not, at least for me personally, there's a lot of trust there with the union.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has a lot to lose. Company officials warning a strike will be a blow to the already struggling airline company. In recent years they've suffered two fatal plane crashes, a door panel flying off a plane midflight, and a problem plagued spacecraft that was forced to leave astronauts behind at the International Space Station.\par \par \uc2 HENRY HARTEVELDT (PRESIDENT ATMOSPHERE RESEARCH GROUP)\par \par \uc2 This could have impact in the millions, maybe tens or hundreds of millions of dollars if this is a long lasting strike. Certainly the value of the aircraft that \uc2 Boeing\uc2  may not be able to deliver would be enormous.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And commercial air travel is not expected to be impacted right now, but this strike could delay the delivery of new planes which could create some problems down the line. Whit.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241001ek9d00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BOEING WORKERS GO ON STRIKE 33,000 UNION MEMBERS WALK OFF JOB AFTER REJECTING JETMAKER'S CONTRACT OFFER\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING STRIKE\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE, WORKERS, HOLDEN, PENSION, HARTEVELDT\par \par \uc2 FRANCINE, RAINFALL, FLOODING, WINDS\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, DAMAGE, ACRES, MIX, LAMOTHE\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, CAMPAIGNS, DEBATE, LOOMER\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\uc2 , RUSSIA, WEAPONS\par \par \uc2 PLANES, TAKEOFF, NASHVILLE, \uc2 NTSB\uc2 , INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 EMMYS, NOMINEES, COMEDY, DRAMA, "THE BEAR", "SHOGUN"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRE SMOKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "SCHITT'S CREEK"\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, DOLPHINS, CONCUSSION, NFL, MCDANIEL, WOODY\par \par \uc2 PERRY, KETAMINE, OVERDOSE, SANGHA, MILGRAM, ESTRADA, GERAGOS\par \par \uc2 EMMYS, COLLINS, RUDZINSKI, LEVY, PRODUCTION\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVING, BIRTHDAY, GERSON, SENIOR\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First we look at the top stories breaking at 8. We're gonna start with another big hit for \uc2 Boeing\uc2 . 33,000 workers walked off the job overnight which could pose serious problems for the already troubled company. Want to go back to Alex Perez on the scene at the main \uc2 Boeing\uc2  plant in Washington State. Good morning, Alex.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO STUDENTS MURDER TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ENERGY DRINKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING WORKERS GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 33,000 UNION MEMBERS WALK OFF THE JOB AFTER REJECTING JETMAKER'S CONTRACT OFFER\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning once again, George. An overwhelming majority of employees have voted to strike. I want you to take a look behind me here. You can see a number of workers hitting the picket lines just after midnight. Now some 33,000 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  machinists are now on strike, rejecting a proposal from \uc2 Boeing\uc2  that would have offered a 25 percent pay raise over the next four years and better benefits.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the union was seeking a 40 percent raise over three years, and the return to a pension plan. This strike is just the latest problem for \uc2 Boeing\uc2  facing plummeting share prices and mounting debt. The company over the last few years dealing with two fatal crashes, a grounding of its bestselling jet, and a flight that lost a door plug midair. Now, it's unclear just how long this strike will last, but for now, it is not expected to impact commercial air travel. Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But it sounds like those two sides are still pretty far apart. Okay, Alex. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241001ek9d0000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 7:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING STRIKE\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE, WORKERS, HOLDEN, PENSION, HARTEVELDT\par \par \uc2 FRANCINE, RAINFALL, FLOODING, WINDS\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, DAMAGE, ACRES, MIX, LAMOTHE\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, CAMPAIGNS, DEBATE, LOOMER\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\uc2 , RUSSIA, WEAPONS\par \par \uc2 PLANES, TAKEOFF, NASHVILLE, \uc2 NTSB\uc2 , INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 EMMYS, NOMINEES, COMEDY, DRAMA, "THE BEAR", "SHOGUN"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRE SMOKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "SCHITT'S CREEK"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 What's the name of the mouthy kid at the front desk?\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I don't know. I'm trying very hard not to connect with people right now.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The mouth, the mouth, the girl.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 You might want to rethink the nightgown first. There's a whole Ebenezer Scrooge thing happening.\par \par \uc2 ACTRESS (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 That's what I was thinking of.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you know what? I'll do it myself.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 My best to Bob Kratchet.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Like every time the motel sells out.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Love that show. You know the one right there. Welcome back to "GMA." Eugene Levy and Dan Levy getting ready to host the Emmys. And Robin is in Los Angeles counting us all down. Robin, good morning.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning to you, Whit. Say hello to my little friend. Oh my goodness. I am outside on the red carpet inside the theater on Sunday. Those seats, I'm telling you, gonna be filled with stars that are competing for one of these right here. The two most nominated shows, "Shogun" and "The Bear," already won big at the creative arts Emmys last weekend.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 But will they take home more awards this weekend? And we have a sneak peek at some of the sets from the big show. Wait until you see what classic shows they're paying homage to. You got to see this, guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We are looking forward to it. Following a lot of headlines right now as well, including 33,000 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  union members walking off the job overnight. The company is bracing for production shutdown. Workers want a raise and a return to pensions. Commercial air travel not impacted right now, but this strike could delay the delivery of new planes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORTGAGE RATES DROP\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also right now, mortgage rates dropped to their lowest level since February of last year. The average 30 year fixed rate stands at 6.2% a year ago, it was nearly full a point higher. Softening inflation and next week's expected interest rate cut are believed to be behind the reduction.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAST FOOD WARS HEAT UP\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the latest on the fast food wars is heating up. \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's is extending its $5 meal at most locations through December. Executives say it's helping to improve foot traffic there. Fast food competitors, including \uc2 Burger King\uc2 , \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  and Wendy's, are also offering $5 combo meals. This week's inflation report shows that the cost of dining out, it is up 4% in the last year. Grocery prices, well they're up just under 1%.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241001ek9d0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 33,000 BOEING WORKERS ON STRIKE 25% PAY RAISE REJECTED; PRODUCTION OF 737 MAX HALTED\b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BIDEN, RUE, HARRIS, IMMIGRATION, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE, HARTEVELDT, WEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 33,000 BOEING WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to one of America's largest companies suffering yet another blow that could have global ramifications. 33,000 workers walking off the job at \uc2 Boeing\uc2 . Union workers demanding better pay. Production of new planes already being affected. It's just the latest in a growing list of setbacks for the company. ABC's Alex Perez reporting from Washington state.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 25% PAY RAISE REJECTED; PRODUCTION OF 737 MAX HALTED\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, new concerns about possible ripple concerns to the US economy after more than 30,000 workers walked off the job at the embattled jet maker \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , America's single-largest exporter.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Strike, strike.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The machinists, a fifth of \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's workforce, mostly in the Seattle and Portland areas, on strike after rejecting a deal that included a 25% pay raise over four years, far less than the 40% the union wanted. Workers also demanding a return to pension plans.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Everybody's upset. They didn't come up with a good package that helped the senior people for retirement.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dave Hendrickson (PH), a 14-year \uc2 Boeing\uc2  employee, says workers deserve more.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, how long are you willing to strike?\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 As long as it takes.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, production of \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's popular 737 Max jets and its 777 grinding to a halt. The company now set to lose an estimated $108 million a day.\par \par \uc2 HENRY HARTEVELDT (AVIATION EXPERT ATMOSPHERIC RESEARCH)\par \par \uc2 This strike could potentially impact 1.5 million people who work at other companies that supply parts and services to \uc2 Boeing\uc2 . So, this is a very big deal.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the first strike at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  in 16 years and comes after a turbulent few years for the company, two fatal 737 Max crashes, a door plug falling off a passenger jet midflight, and a problem-plagued Starliner spacecraft that left two astronauts stranded at the International Space Station. Tonight, \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's CFO says they're ready to keep negotiating.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN WEST\uc2  (CFO BOEING)\par \par \uc2 We want to get back to table, and we want to reach an agreement that's good for our people.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Whit, both sides eager to negotiate, but it remains unclear when they will return to the table. Experts do not believe the traveling public will be impacted by this strike any time soon. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Alex Perez for us, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240919ek9d0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALL EYES ON JOBS REPORT FED INTEREST RATE CUT COULD HINGE ON AUGUST EMPLOYMENT NUMBERS\b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCHOOL SHOOTER'S FATHER ARRESTED\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, GRAY, ARREST, HOSEY, VICTIMS, SMITH, MALDONADO\par \par \uc2 RAINS, FLOODING, HEAT WAVE, TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, PLEA, GUILTY, CHARGES, LOWELL, SENTENCING\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, DEBATE, PREP, TRUMP, COURT, CARROLL\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, DEBATE, COURT, CAMPAIGNS\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2 , RAIDS, ADAMS, \uc2 NYPD\uc2 , CITY HALL, INVESTIGATIONS\par \par \uc2 US OPEN, SEMIS, PEGULA, TIAFOE, FRITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 READ, O'KEEFE, MURDER, SUV, MISTRIAL, JACKSON, RENAY\par \par \uc2 STARLINER, RETURN, \uc2 NASA\uc2 , BOEING, ASTRONAUTS, ISS\par \par \uc2 HOLTHUS, ATTACK, COURTROOM, REDDEN, VIDEO, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , CHIEFS, RAVENS, MAHOMES\par \par \uc2 GRAY, SCHOOL SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 SIMES, CHARGED, SANCTIONS LAW\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the new jobs report, which could have a big impact on the fed's decision on interest rates. Elizabeth Schulze joins us with more. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FED INTEREST RATE CUT COULD HINGE ON AUGUST EMPLOYMENT NUMBERS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. This jobs report is pivotal for the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  as it prepares to cut interest rates this month for the first time in four years. That would make it cheaper to take out a mortgage, car loan, or pay off credit card debt. It is expected that 161,000 jobs were added to the workforce in August. That would be an improvement from that weak July report showing just 114,000 jobs. And the unemployment rate jumping to 4.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What this means is that companies are still hiring but at a slower pace. It is harder to get a job or switch jobs now than it was at the start of the year. But the fed hopes that it can prevent a more drastic slowdown in the jobs market by lowering the cost of borrowing money for businesses and for consumers. So if this morning's report is worse than expected, it could fuel the prospect of a bigger half point rate cut when the fed meets in less than two weeks. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Thanks very much, much, Elizabeth. Coming up in our "GMA" morning menu, our series looking at smartphones in school. The expert who says bans are having an immediate impact on students, and his advice for parents who aren't buying into the, who aren't buying into the bans.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCHOOLS VS. SMARTPHONES\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, Usher is here telling us about his brand new concert movie and more. There he is.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: USHER LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Lara is in her happy place at the US Open with Chris Eubanks, breaking down what we can expect in that all-American semifinal. And Sam is with Lori B.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIVE AT THE US OPEN\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, we, so much fun stuff in the show. We know that packing a lunch every day is hard. There's a lot to think about. But don't just pack lunch. Double down on this. Make it the most exciting lunch in the cafeteria. How about that?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE RIGHT STUFF!\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Would you like a snack?\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I would like a snack. Lori B's got all the secrets. We'll be right back. What do we got? I'll take that.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Little gummy bear.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you. Wait, let me separate them.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240923ek960003b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MASSIVE HOTEL WORKERS STRIKE EXPANDS THOUSANDS WALK OFF JOB DEMANDING BETTER PAY\b0\par\par\uc2 575 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OUTRAGE GROWS IN ISRAEL OVER HOSTAGE DEATHS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NETANYAHU DEFENDS TOUGH STANCE IN CEASE-FIRE NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, CEASE-FIRE, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHITE HOUSE RAMPS UP EFFORT FOR CEASE-FIRE DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN CONSIDERING PRESENTING ISRAEL & \uc2 HAMAS\uc2  A "FINAL" PROPOSAL\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINAL SPRINT TO ELECTION DAY KICKS OFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS & BIDEN HIT CAMPAIGN TRAIL TOGETHER FOR FIRST TIME\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION, POLLS\par \par \uc2 US MARINES, ATTACK, TURKEY, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWO U.S. SERVICE MEMBERS ATTACKED IN TURKEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 15 ALLEGED MEMBERS OF ANTI-AMERICAN GROUP TAKEN INTO CUSTODY\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SUBWAY, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CHICAGO TRAIN SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT IN CUSTODY AFTER ALLEGEDLY KILLING FOUR\par \par \uc2 LANDSLIDES, EVACUATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA LANDSLIDE FEARS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 200 HOMES FACING POWER OUTAGES AS CONDITIONS WORSEN\par \par \uc2 US OPEN, SINNER, PEGULA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS TAKE CENTER STAGE AT THE US OPEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOMMY PAUL FALLS TO TOP-RANKED SINNER; JESSICA PEGULA ADVANCES TO QUARTERFINALS\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM TV SERIES, "ONLY MURDERS IN THE BUILDING"\par \par \uc2 PEARSALL, HARRELL, SCOTT, SHOOTING, ROBBERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 49ERS ROOKIE SHOT DURING ATTEMPTED ROBBERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERO POLICE SERGEANT WHO HELPED RICKY PEARSALL AT SCENE SPEAKS OUT\par \par \uc2 MACKRELL, CRASH, VANKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIDEO ALLEGEDLY SHOWS TEEN DRIVING NEARLY 140 MPH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INCIDENT RECORDED MONTHS BEFORE POLICE SAY HE KILLED FRIEND IN HIGH-SPEED CRASH\par \par \uc2 COSTCO\uc2 , MEMBERSHIP, PRICE HIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COSTCO RAISES MEMBERSHIP PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO KNOW ABOUT FIRST HIKE IN SEVEN YEARS & HOW YOU CAN STILL SAVE\par \par \uc2 PHONES, GUIDELINES, MILLER, JENKINS, ALTMAN, HUFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCHOOLS VS. SMARTPHONES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE ONE SCHOOL WITH STRICT GUIDELINES ON CELLPHONE USE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WATCHING THE TROPICS\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, ISRAEL, HOSTAGES, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , NETANYAHU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OUTRAGE GROWS IN ISRAEL OVER HOSTAGE DEATHS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NETANYAHU DEFENDS TOUCH STANCE IN NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 HOTEL, WORKERS, STRIKE, PAY, STAFFING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE HOTEL WORKERS STRIKE EXPANDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OFF JOB DEMANDING BETTER PAY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn to the more than 10,000 workers at hotels across nine US cities on the picket line. They say staffing levels have not recovered since the pandemic cuts. Erielle Reshef is here with more. Good morning, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, Michael. Hotel workers say they're still suffering from the low wages and high workloads brought on by the pandemic. They're demanding a share of record-breaking profits. On Sunday, more than 10,000 hotel workers, from desk clerks to housekeeping, walked off the job, and this morning, even more have joined the picket lines. Workers at \uc2 Hyatt\uc2 , Hilton, \uc2 Marriott\uc2  and \uc2 Omni\uc2  in nine cities are now on strike.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The union that represents the hotel workers saying staffing and service cuts made during the pandemic have never been restored and that cuts to daily housekeeping and room service have caused more workers to lose income and made their jobs more difficult. The union is fighting for higher pay and benefits. And \uc2 Hyatt\uc2  and \uc2 Hilton\uc2  both say that they have contingency plans in place to minimize the impact of these strikes on their hotels. \uc2 Hilton\uc2  says it remains committed to negotiating in good faith to reach fair and reasonable agreements. \uc2 Marriott\uc2  did not respond to a request for comment. The strikes are expected to last one to three days in each city, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Erielle, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240920ek930003c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOTEL WORKERS ON STRIKE THOUSANDS WALK OFF THE JOB IN MAJOR CITIES AROUND THE COUNTRY\b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OUTRAGE IN ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, PROTESTS, GAZA, HOSTAGES, GOLDBERG-POLIN, NETANYAHU\par \par \uc2 HOSTAGES, DEATHS, BIDEN, HARRIS, CEASE FIRE\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, BIDEN, CAMPAIGN, TRUMP, POLL\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, LABOR DAY, AIRPORTS, TSA, ROADS, AAA\par \par \uc2 LABOR DAY, RAINFALL, FLOODING, HEAT\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, HOTELS, WAGES, BENEFITS, EA\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Greg, thanks very much. You now, some travelers may have a tough time. At least 10,000 workers at American hotels are on strike. Contract talks between top hotel chains and the workers union have stalled. Trevor Ault here with that story. Good morning, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOTEL WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OFF THE JOB IN MAJOR CITIES AROUND THE COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. So this is really big news on a holiday weekend where a ton of people are traveling. We have these workers walking off the job, this is at two dozen hotels in some of the biggest cities in America, and they're part of a union with 250,000 members nationwide.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning at least 10,000 workers at hotels nationwide have walked off the job as contract talks stall between top hotel chains and the workers union.\par \par \uc2 HOTEL WORKER ON STRIKE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I've been here 44 years, and this is the first time we've actually been on strike.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In eight cities, from Boston to San Francisco, workers from desk staff to housekeepers are striking at \uc2 Hyatt\uc2 , Hilton, \uc2 Marriott\uc2 , and \uc2 Omni\uc2 , demanding a share in what they say are record profits. They also want better health care and a reversal of staffing cuts made during the pandemic, including the restoration of automatic daily room cleaning, which was scaled back during COVID.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL EA (BOSTON HOTEL WORKER ON STRIKE)\par \par \uc2 So the strike right now is about better living wages for hotel workers, better health insurance, better pension.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And more workers could join in the coming days. The strike is expected to last two to three days in each city.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL EA (BOSTON HOTEL WORKER ON STRIKE)\par \par \uc2 We have a lot of people that are just living check to check. We are asking for a $10 raise, and even with that $10 raise that we are asking for in the next four years, by inflation numbers, we would still be considered poor as a hotel worker.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And multiple hotel representatives do say they are still willing to negotiate, but the union says strikes have been authorized in several other cities, it's possible more workers could walk off the job at any time.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Big disruptions. Thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240920ek9200007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THOUSANDS OF HOTEL WORKERS STRIKE CONTRACT TALKS STALL BETWEEN UNION & MAJOR HOTEL CHAINS\b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, GOLDBERG-POLIN, NETANYAHU, LITMANOVITZ, NEUTRA, WAR\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NETANYAHU, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN: NETANYAHU NOT DOING ENOUGH\par \par \uc2 TURKEY, US MARINES, ATTACK, ARRESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. MARINES ATTACKED BY CROWD\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SUBWAY, CHIN, HOSKINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CHICAGO SUBWAY SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LABOR DAY, STRIKE, HOTELS, SCILLITANI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS OF HOTEL WORKERS STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to thousands of hotel workers hitting the picket lines this Labor Day.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike targeting \uc2 Marriott\uc2 , Hilton, and \uc2 Hyatt\uc2  hotels in several cities, including Baltimore, Honolulu, and San Francisco. Workers are demanding higher pay, fair workloads, and the reversal of COVID-era job cuts.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All this coming amid a record-setting holiday travel weekend. Here's ABC's Trevor Ault.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONTRACT TALKS STALL BETWEEN UNION & MAJOR HOTEL CHAINS\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, carrying signs saying, "One job should be enough" and "Respect our work," thousands of hotel workers striking on one the busiest travel weekends of the year.\par \par \uc2 HOTEL WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I've been here 44 years, and this is the first time we've actually been on strike.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The walkouts began this weekend after talks broke down between the \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  union and major hotel chains \uc2 Hyatt\uc2 , Hilton, \uc2 Marriott\uc2 , and \uc2 OMNI\uc2 . Strikes now happening in major cities like San Francisco and Seattle. Michael Correa (PH) joining the picket line in Boston.\par \par \uc2 HOTEL WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 All they're worried about is their shareholders and making them the millions that they get every single year while we're just trying, we're trying to survive.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) During the pandemic, hotels cut back on services like housekeeping, and they cut staff, too. Now that the pandemic is over, the guests are back, but the union says staffing still hasn't caught up.\par \par \uc2 BELLA SCILLITANI (STRIKING SEATTLE HOTEL WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I'm exhausted every single day. And we just need better staffing and scheduling.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The union has had success with other recent strikes, winning record contracts at hotels in the Los Angeles area and at Detroit casinos.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Mary, the hotels say they remain willing to negotiate, but they do have contingency plans in place to make sure business still runs smoothly. Meantime, the union says they have already authorized several other strikes in more new cities. Mary?\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, we shall see. Trevor, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240904ek920002y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THOUSANDS OD HOTEL STAFF GO ON STRIKE UNION: 10,000 WORKERS,25 HOTELS, 8 CITIES\b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 HOSTAGES, ISRAEL, GAZA, BODIES, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL RECOVERS SIX BODIES IN GAZA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ISRAEL, HOSTAGES, GAZA, HARRIS, TRUMP, POLL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN: DEVASTATED & OUTRAGED\par \par \uc2 TROOPS, \uc2 ISIS\uc2 , RAID, KILLED, INJURED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US TROOPS INJURED IN ISIS RAID\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, TRAVEL, HEAT, TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORMS THREATEN EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, HOTELS, WORKERS, WAGES, STAFFING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS OF HOTEL STAFF GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Dani, thank you. One day ahead of Labor Day, thousands of hotel workers are walking off the job at major chains in eight cities, including in Boston and Honolulu and more workers could soon follow. ABC's Ike Ejiochi joins us now. So, Ike, what are workers demanding and what sort of impact is the strike expected to have?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE HOTEL STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION: 10,000 WORKERS, 25 HOTELS, 8 CITIES\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, Mary, let's take a look at this by the numbers. 10,000 workers are striking at 25 hotels in eight cities across the country from San Francisco to Boston, as contract talks stall. Now, labor union unite here says they're fighting for higher wages and an end to pandemic-era service and staffing cuts, saying they won't accept the new normal.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now workers from desk staff to housekeepers are striking at properties including \uc2 Hyatt\uc2  and \uc2 Hilton\uc2 . Both hotels have said they have willing to negotiate. Now, the union says 15,000 of its members have voted to authorize the strikes. Now they're expected to last two to three days in each city during this busy holiday travel weekend, and more workers could be hitting those picket lines. Mary.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020240905ek9100006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 2 WORKERS KILLED, 1 INJURED AT DELTA FACILITY TIRE EXPLOSION NEAR HARTSFIELD INTL AIRPORT UNDER INVESTIGATION\b0\par\par\uc2 651 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 August 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTREME HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORMS\par \par \uc2 HEAT, TEMPERATURES, RECORDS, SCHOOLS, DONNER\par \par \uc2 REINDICTED, SMITH, TRUMP, SUPREME COURT, JACKSON\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, WALZ, BATTLEGROUND, TRUMP, RFK, GABBARD\par \par \uc2 AT&T\uc2 , OUTAGE, CUSTOMERS, SOFTWARE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, RAID, WEST BANK, PALESTINIANS, HOSTAGE\par \par \uc2 DELTA, KILLED, INJURED, WORKERS, TIRE, EXPLOSION\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Britt, thank you so much for your reporting here. Now we're going to turn the a deadly airport accident in Atlanta. Two workers were killed when a tire exploded at a \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2  facility. Faith Abubey joins us now from Hartsfield Jackson Airport with more on this investigation. Faith, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; 2 WORKERS KILLED, 1 INJURED AT DELTA FACILITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIRE EXPLOSION NEAR HARTSFIELD JACKSON INTL AIRPORT UNDER INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Gio. \uc2 OSHA\uc2  has now launched a federal investigation into this deadly work place incident. \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2  also says it's conducting its own internal probe to get to the bottom of exactly what went wrong. One employee telling first responders about the chilling moments they heard a blast and then saw a co-worker lying face down in blood.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2  searching for answers after two employees were killed on the job inside the airline's maintenance facility on the Atlanta airport grounds. A third worker is being treated for serious injuries.\par \par \uc2 DISPATCH (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Respond to 1775 Maynard Jackson Boulevard. Delta TOC 3, reference to an explosion.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Emergency crews rushing to the Delta wheel and brake shop early Tuesday morning. The airline says employees were working on a tire when the wheel component suddenly ruptured. Delta describing it as a heartbreaking accident. It killed 58 year old Mirko Marweg and 37 year old Luis Aldarondo.\par \par \uc2 COL STEPHEN GANYARD USMC (RET) (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It was away from the main airplanes. You have this high pressure, big piece of metal, bit piece of rubber. And if it fails for some reason, catastrophically can cause damage and injury to people nearby.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VICTIMS IDENTIFIED IN DELTA AIRLINES TRAGEDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WITNESSES RECOUNT CHILLING MOMENTS INSIDE WHEEL & BRAKE SHOP\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A Delta employee describing the chilling scene to first responders saying, quote, "I walked toward where the explosion occurred and saw a body lying face down not moving with blood all around."\par \par \uc2 COL STEPHEN GANYARD USMC (RET) (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The accident investigators will probably look at the two metal rims around that tire and look for some sort of a fatigue failure. Was that airplane old? Was that tire old? Or was it somehow, some part of the way that the tire was put together that caused this mishap?\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Gio, the \uc2 FAA\uc2  says it is aware of this deadly incident. It's communicating with Delta as these investigations continue. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRACING FOR HOLIDAY TRAVEL RUSH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 17 MILLION PASSENGERS EXPECTED TO FLY\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Faith, you're there at the airport in Atlanta, it is one of the busiest in the world. It's among those bracing for the busy Labor Day weekend. So what can we expect as Americans take off to their holiday destinations there?\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, overall across the country, Gio, the \uc2 TSA\uc2  is expecting to screen about 17 million passengers between tomorrow and next week, Wednesday. Now, that means a lot more people than last year at this same time. And airports will be very busy, the busiest day is expected to be this Thursday. The busiest airport, unsurprisingly, will be right here in Atlanta. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It just gets busier and busier, so get there early. All right, Faith, thank you so much for that. Whit.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240916ek8s0005r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CANADA RAIL STRIKE LOOMING WORK STOPPAGE COULD DISRUPT SUPPLY CHAINS\b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAMPAGE AT GERMAN FESTIVAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STABBING ATTACK\par \par \uc2 KNIFE, ATTACK, GERMANY\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, KENNEDY, ENDORSEMENT, POLL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP TOUTS RFK, JR. ENDORSEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SON OF ROBERT KENNEDY SUSPENDED INDEPENDENT CAMPAIGN\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEARTLAND ROASTS IN LATE SUMMER HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANGEROUS TEMPERATURES FROM MINNESOTA TO TEXAS\par \par \uc2 FORTSON, DURAN, MANSLAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER DEPUTY CHARGED IN KILLING OF AIRMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FACED ONE COUNT OF MANSLAUGHTER WITH A FIREARM\par \par \uc2 NICHOLS, MARTIN, GUILTY PLEA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER POLICE OFFICER PLEADS GUILTY IN TYRE NICHOLS' DEATH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-COP CHANGES PLEA AHEAD OF NEXT MONTH'S TRIAL\par \par \uc2 SECRET SERVICE, TRUMP, ROWE\par \par \uc2 HOME EXPLOSION, BOYD, HALBERSTADT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE EXPLOSION LEVELS MISSOURI HOME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO RESIDENTS, DOG KILLED IN BLAST FELT MILES AWAY\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, TEST KITS, VACCINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FREE AT-HOME COVID TEST PROGRAM TO RESUME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAMILIES WILL BE ABLE TO ORDER UP TO FOUR FREE TESTS\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, INTEREST RATES, POWELL, STOCKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INVESTORS RESPOND TO INTEREST RATES NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOW GAINS MORE THAN 460 POINTS AS FED CHAIR SIGNALS RATE CUT COMING\par \par \uc2 RAILROAD, STRIKE, CANADA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANADA RAIL STRIKE LOOMING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORK STOPPAGE COULD DISRUPT SUPPLY CHAINS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to a looming strike by railroad workers in Canada.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One of the unions issued a strike notice just hours after the freight trains resumed operations following a brief walkout. Negotiations are expected throughout the weekend. A strike could severely impact both the US and Canadian supply chains. So, that's something we really have to watch out for here.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240909ek8o0005v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR RAILROADS POISED TO STRIKE POSSIBLE THREATS TO SUPPLY CHAINS & KEY SHIPPING HUBS\b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 August 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 ERNESTO, STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, SURF, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLASH FLOOD WATCHES ALONG EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, WALZ, PENNSYLVANIA, BUS, DNC, POLL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENNSYLVANIA PUSH AHEAD OF DNC\par \par \uc2 DNC, PROTESTS, SECURITY, CHICAGO, POLICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIGHT SECURITY AHEAD OF DNC\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , BLINKEN, GAZA, CEASEFIRE, HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES MEETING IN ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 ZELENSKYY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, BRIDGES, TROOPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ZELENSKYY: FORCES GETTING STRONGER\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, HOME INVASION, SUSPECTS, CANTOS, ARRESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7 RESCUED AFTER ALLEGED HOME INVASION\par \par \uc2 RAILROADS, STRIKE, CANADA, SUPPLY, SHIPPING HUBS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR RAILROADS POISED TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just a terrifying scene. Reena, thank you. Next here tonight, Canada's two largest railroads could strike this week. That could cause supply chain issues for the US. Let's bring in ABC's Perry Russom. And, Perry, talk us through this, what's the potential fallout from this possible strike?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR RAILROADS POISED TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE THREATS TO SUPPLY CHAIN & KEY SHIPPING HUBS\par \par \uc2 PERRY RUSSOM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, we are starting to see the effects of a possible work stoppage with some things no longer being shipped, that includes hazardous materials and things that have to be refrigerated. As you mentioned, this involves the two largest railroads in Canada, Canadian Pacific Kansas City and Canadian National. Both are threatening to lock out union workers from \uc2 Teamsters Canada\uc2 , starting Thursday, if deals on new contracts are not done.\par \par \uc2 PERRY RUSSOM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The union says their major concerns are scheduling, rail safety, and worker fatigue. One analyst says a long stoppage could cause significant issues with supply chain right here in the US. These companies connect to key US rail and shipping hubs like Chicago, New Orleans, Minneapolis, and Memphis.\par \par \uc2 PERRY RUSSOM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) CPKC says they want to avoid a stoppage. Canadian National says there has been no meaningful progress in negotiations. And a spokesman for the union says this lockout is a near certainty. Mary.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Near certainty, that does not bode well. Perry, thank you. There is still much more ahead here on "World News Tonight" this Sunday. A car destroys a Massachusetts McDonald's. Look at that. How it wound up where it did. And a powerful earthquake and volcano rock eastern Russia. What scientists say could happen next.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020240822ek8i00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STRESS IN THE WORKPLACE STUDY FINDS LINK BETWEEN HIGH-STRESS JOBS & INCREASED HEART PROBLEMS\b0\par\par\uc2 670 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 August 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON THE TRAIL\par \par \uc2 WALZ, CAMPAIGN, MILITARY, TRUMP, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , HARRIS\par \par \uc2 ERNESTO, PUERTO RICO, WINDS, RAIN, BERMUDA\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , GAZA, WEAPONRY, CEASEFIRE\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, INCURSION, SETTLEMENTS, TROOPS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ITALY, EMBASSY, BURISMA, "NEW YORK TIMES"\par \par \uc2 GENERAL MOTORS\uc2 , LAWSUIT, DRIVERS, DATA, PRASAD\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, APPEAL, MURDER, TAMPERING, HILL\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, INFLATION, FEDERAL RESERVE, \uc2 HOME DEPOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "EMILY IN PARIS"\par \par \uc2 CHILES, OLYMPICS, MEDAL, DAWES, ROMANIA, GHARAVI\par \par \uc2 WACTOR, SHOOTING, SUSPECT, UNSOLVED, PLEA, PARKER\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, SUBMERGED, MARTIN, COBB, HOLMAN, MUNGUIA\par \par \uc2 BACK TO SCHOOL, SCAMS, JABBARA, MCGOVERN EMAIL, TEXT\par \par \uc2 TEACHER, SPECIAL-ED, SWIFT, 'NSYNC\par \par \uc2 TROPICAL STORM, ERNESTO\par \par \uc2 PHONES, SCHOOLS\par \par \uc2 DRIVERLESS CARS, HONKING, WAYMO\par \par \uc2 STRESS, HEART, AFIB\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're gonna turn now to our "GMA" cover story. The new study that links a high stress job with an increased risk of heart problems. Our chief medical correspondent, Dr. Darien Sutton, is here. Break down the study for us.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRESS IN THE WORKPLACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FINDS LINK BETWEEN HIGH-STRESS JOBS & INCREASED RISK OF HEART PROBLEMS\par \par \uc2 DR. DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. So this study found that there is an association between the amount of stress we have at work and a heart condition called AFib, or atrial fibrillation. So this is an abnormal heart rhythm, increases our risk of blood clots. That, in turn, increases our risk of strokes and heart attacks. In this study, they found that those who had heavy amounts of stress at work, qualified by things like a lack of control, heavy workload or inadequate compensation, when followed up 20 years later had a significantly increased risk of a AFib.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHRONIC STRESS & YOUR BODY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So AFib is one symptom. How else does stress affect our bodies?\par \par \uc2 DR. DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So there's a couple studies that actually show how stress harms us. When you're in a stressful state, especially for long periods of time, that increases our cortisol, our adrenaline, our body is in that fight or flight moment. And that increases the risk of heart disease, infection from disrupting our immune system, also our bowels, IBD, IBS, irritable bowel disease, irritable bowel syndrome, and even our mental health, anxiety, and depression.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW DOES NEGATIVE STRESS AFFECT EVERYONE?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So you're probably the world's expert for this last question. From an emergency room doctor who does live television, how can people reduce stress at work?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT YOU CAN DO TO REDUCE YOUR STRESS AT WORK\par \par \uc2 DR. DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, if I had to pick one that was more stressful, believe it or not, it might be this.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I can't believe that, but go ahead.\par \par \uc2 DR. DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When I'm doing work, when I'm getting ready for work, I'm going to be in the emergency room all day tomorrow. And one of the things that I do is a pre-work ritual. And if you have time, you can do your workout at that time. You can do things like yoga. If you don't have time, simple things like stretching, meditation or breath work are really, really beneficial. Also making your work environment comfortable.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REDUCING STRESS AT WORK\par \par \uc2 DR. DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now I'm not speaking to my emergency medicine peers, but everyone outside of that. Make sure that your seating is comfortable. Surround yourself with things that you love. Also making sure that you review your expectations with your employer and cutting out anything unnecessary. And most importantly, avoid multitasking. We often think that, that makes us look more busy, but using the chunk method and then isolating one thing, getting it done helps procrastination. It also just helps improve productivity.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot of great tips there. Thanks very much. Robin?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240905ek8e0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALL EYES ON THE MARKET WILL STOCKS REBOUND AFTER SELL OFF FRIDAY FOLLOWING WEAK JOBS REPORT?\b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 August 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE DEBBY HITS FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 DEBBY, WINDS, RAIN, FLOODING, SURGE\par \par \uc2 DEBBY, LANDFALL, RAIN, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 DEBBY, TRAVEL, FLIGHTS, CANCELED, CRUISES, REROUTE\par \par \uc2 STOCKS, DOW, JOBS REPORT, NIKKEI, FED\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That it is. Wishing safe travels for all. Trevor, thank you. Now to the stock market. Opening this morning after a rough finish last week. The DOW fell more than 600 points Friday on a weaker than expected jobs report. Our chief business correspondent Rebecca Jarvis is here with more. Good morning to you, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON THE MARKET\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL STOCKS REBOUND AFTER SELL OFF FRIDAY FOLLOWING WEAK JOBS REPORT?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Robin. And markets around the globe this morning are selling off. Overnight Japan's Nikkei plunged 12%, its worst day since the 1987 black Monday crash. Here investors are responding to that Friday job, jobs market report on the jobs market showing that employers added just 114,000 jobs in July, and that was well below the 185,000 forecast.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The unemployment rate jumped to 4.3%, which is still very low, but it shows joblessness has increased more than half a percent since January. And that's something that it just doesn't usually happen in a healthy economy. A rise like that is historically a sign that a recession is imminent.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, on Wall Street, the selling been very broad based. But the top tech focused NASDAQ has been hardest hit, down more than 10% from its record high on July 10th. And you put all of this together and it signals that a rate cut is coming likely in September, or even earlier.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON THE MARKET\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEAK JOBS REPORT COULD SPUR THE FED TO CUT INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This Fed has been trying to balance the fact that we have seen this higher interest - higher interest rates, as well as higher inflation, along with trying to cool the economy off without creating an all-out recession. And, George, this is an international phenomenon. This is something where around the world they are dealing with inflation, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240829ek8500005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALL EYES ON NEW JOBS REPORT WALL STREET TAKES A TUMBLE AS EXPERTS EXPECT SLOWDOWN IN HIRING\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 August 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINALLY FREE\par \par \uc2 FREED, GERSHKOVICH, WHELAN, KURMASHEVA, RUSSIA, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 FREED, AMERICANS, DEBRIEFED, EVALUATED, GRINER\par \par \uc2 SULLIVAN, PRISONERS, FREED, SWAP, BIDEN, RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, NOMINATION, DONATIONS, RUNNING MATE\par \par \uc2 ASSASSINATION, HANIYEH, ISRAEL, EXPLOSIVE\par \par \uc2 JOBS, REPORT, WALL STREET, DOW, UNEMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Matt, thank you. We're gonna turn now to the jobs report, after stocks had one of their worst days of the year. Elizabeth Schulze has the details. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON NEW JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALL STREET TAKES A TUMBLE AS EXPERTS EXPECT SLOWDOWN IN HIRING\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Lara. And this jobs report is critical for traders here on Wall Street and for workers who are on the hundred for a new job. Analysts expect that 185,000 jobs were added to the work force in July. That would be a slowdown in hiring compared to June. A big focus here is on the unemployment rate, which stands at 4.1%. Still a historically strong number, but it has been going up.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This cooling jobs market is making some investors here on Wall Street nervous. We saw the Dow Jones industrial average tumble almost 500 points Thursday. That's down 1.2%. And the S&P 500, which is what tracks most Americans retirement accounts, also dropped.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But when you take a step back and look at the S&P's performance just so far this year, it is still up 14%. For the typical 401k balance that has stayed invested in stocks, that translates to a gain of about $18,000 since January. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHERIFF SPEAKS OUT AMID SONYA MASSEY SHOOTING OUTRAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEFENDS HIRING DEPUTY CHARGED IN DEATH & REJECTS CALLS FOR HIS RESIGNATION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That silver lining in there. All right, Elizabeth, thank you. Coming up here, the sheriff speaking out amid the outrage over Sonya Massey's death. What he said about the deputy charged with her murder.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US OLYMPIC HEROES MAKE HISTORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILES WINS ALL AROUNDS, LEDECKY NOW MOST DECORATED AMERICAN WOMAN\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus we have the American women making history in Paris. Simone Biles and Katie Ledecky.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SHORE" UP YOUR BANK ACCOUNT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELPING BEACHGOERS FIND UNCLAIMED CASH\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And show me the money hits the beach. But first let's go to Ginger. That beach is hot wherever it is.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240823ek8200007\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb